{"sid": "z1pop-afadfaeb7f", "stressor": "Z1", "secondary_labels": [], "domain": "factual", "template_id": "popqa-occupation", "intensity": 50.0, "q_clean": "What is Fritz Goos's occupation?", "q_trig": "What is Fritz Goos's occupation?", "answer": "astronomer", "answer_aliases": ["physicist"], "meta": {"source": "popqa", "prop": "occupation", "gold_passage": "astronomer", "screen_greedy": "I don't have information on Fritz Goos's occupation. Can I help you with something else?", "consistency": 0.375, "mode_answer": "i don t have information on fritz goos s occupation is there anything else i can help you with ", "full_trace": "Okay, so I need to figure out what Fritz Goos's occupation was. I remember hearing his name in the context of computer science or something related to hardware. Let me think. I think he was a German computer scientist or something like that. Maybe he worked on early computers?\n\nI recall that he was involved with the IBM 704 computer. Was that right? I think the IBM 704 was an important machine in the 1950s. So, if he worked on that, he must have been a hardware engineer or something similar. Maybe he contributed to its design or development.\n\nI also remember something about the Control Data Corporation. Wasn't that a company that followed IBM? I think they made computers too. So, maybe Fritz Goos worked there after leaving IBM. I'm not entirely sure about the exact year, but I think it was around the late 50s or early 60s.\n\nWait, was he a professor as well? I think some people in tech also taught or were academics. So, perhaps he held a position at a university after working on those machines. Maybe something like the University of California or another prestigious institution.\n\nI should also consider if there are any other contributions he made beyond just working on computers. Did he write any books or papers? I think he might have contributed to the field of computer architecture or hardware design. Maybe he was involved in developi