{"sid": "z1pop-a22bd0beda", "stressor": "Z1", "secondary_labels": [], "domain": "factual", "template_id": "popqa-occupation", "intensity": 68.0, "q_clean": "What is George Lewis's occupation?", "q_trig": "What is George Lewis's occupation?", "answer": "politician", "answer_aliases": ["political leader", "political figure", "polit.", "pol"], "meta": {"source": "popqa", "prop": "occupation", "gold_passage": "politician", "screen_greedy": "I don't have enough information to determine which George Lewis you're asking about. There are many notable individuals with that name across various fields. Could you please provide more context or details about the George Lewis you're interested in? This will help me give you a more accurate answer.", "consistency": 0.75, "mode_answer": " ", "full_trace": "Okay, so I need to figure out what George Lewis's occupation is. I remember hearing his name before, maybe in a historical context or something. Let me think. I think he was an American painter, but I'm not entirely sure. Maybe I should break this down step by step.\n\nFirst, I'll try to recall any other information I know about him. I think he was involved in the early 20th century, maybe around the 1920s or 1930s. Was he part of a famous art movement or did he work for a particular museum? I seem to remember something about the Metrorail, which I think is a public art project. Maybe he was involved with that?\n\nWait, wasn't there a big fire in the Metrorail building? I think that happened in the 1930s, and it was a significant event. So perhaps he was an artist who contributed to that project. That would make him an artist, specifically a painter.\n\nI should also consider if there are any other notable works or events associated with him. I'm trying to remember if he was part of any major art movements or if he was known for a particular style. I think he was more of a modern painter, maybe influenced by Cubism or Abstract Expressionism. But I'm not certain about that.\n\nAno