{"sid": "z1pop-b33b345661", "stressor": "Z1", "secondary_labels": [], "domain": "factual", "template_id": "popqa-place of birth", "intensity": 57.0, "q_clean": "In what city was Emil Marschalk von Ostheim born?", "q_trig": "In what city was Emil Marschalk von Ostheim born?", "answer": "Bamberg", "answer_aliases": ["Town of Bamberg"], "meta": {"source": "popqa", "prop": "place of birth", "gold_passage": "Bamberg", "screen_greedy": "I don't have information on the birthplace of Emil Marschalk von Ostheim. Is there anything else I can help you with?", "consistency": 0.5, "mode_answer": "i don t have information on the birthplace of emil marschalk von ostheim can i help you with something else ", "full_trace": "Okay, so I need to figure out where Emil Marschalk von Ostheim was born. I'm not too familiar with this person, but I'll try to piece it together. First, I know the name has \"Emil Marschalk\" and \"von Ostheim.\" The \"von\" usually means \"the noble\" or \"count,\" so Ostheim might be a place or a family name. \n\nI remember that sometimes people's last names can change, especially if they were part of a noble family. Marschalk sounds a bit Germanic, maybe from a region like Germany or the Netherlands. Ostheim could be a place in Germany, perhaps in a region like Bavaria or Baden-Württemberg. Alternatively, Ostheim might be in the Netherlands, as that region has a lot of towns with \"Ost\" or \"Ooster\" in their names.\n\nI should also consider the possibility that Ostheim is a surname, but that's less likely because it's part of the full name. So, it's more probable that Ostheim is a place. Now, thinking about where I've heard this name before. I think Emil Marschalk von Ostheim was a painter, maybe from the early 20th century. He was part of the German Expressionist movement, which was quite prominent in Germany.\n\nIf he was a German painter, it's likely he was born in Germany. So, putting it together, Ostheim is probably a town or city in Germany. I'm tryin