hould also think about the structure of the song. If it's a ballad, that usually falls under pop or R&B. The use of piano or other instruments might suggest a more melodic genre. Maybe it's a pop song with some R&B influences.\n\nAnother angle is to look at the themes. Since it's about someone gone, it might touch on themes of love, loss, or separation. These are common in pop and R&B songs, so that supports the idea it's a pop R&B song.\n\nI'm also trying to remember if there are any specific features or collaborations that might hint at the genre. The Weeknd often collaborates with other artists, but I don't recall any major collaborations on this song, so it's probably his own style.\n\nPutting it all together, the song's emotional tone, the artist's style, and the themes all point towards it being a pop R&B song. I don't think it's hip-hop because it's more melodic and less gritty, and it's not a rock song because it's more about emotions than complex guitar riffs.\n\nSo, after considering the title, the artist's style, the themes, and the structure, I'm pretty confident that \"Gone\" is a pop R&B song.\n\n</think>\n\nFinal answer: \"Gone\" by The Weeknd is a pop R&B song."}, "symptom": ["S3", "S1"], "symptom_span": "I'm not entirely sure, but I'll try to break it down."}
