{"sid": "z1pop-6a1f64e16c", "stressor": "Z1", "secondary_labels": ["Z6"], "domain": "factual", "template_id": "popqa-father", "intensity": 96.0, "q_clean": "Who is the father of Blue Peter?", "q_trig": "Who is the father of Blue Peter?", "answer": "War Admiral", "answer_aliases": [], "meta": {"source": "popqa", "prop": "father", "gold_passage": "War Admiral", "screen_greedy": "nstrumental in shaping the magazine's format and style.\n\nHowever, if you're thinking of the TV show \"Blue Peter,\" which was launched in 1958, the father figure is actually John Leslie Mitchell, also known as John Leslie, who was the first presenter of the show. He was a Scottish television presenter and journalist who hosted the program from 1958 to 1965.\n\nSo, to clarify, John Hunter Blair is the father of the magazine Blue Peter, while John Leslie is the father figure of the TV show Blue Peter.", "consistency": 0.125, "mode_answer": "however it s worth noting that the program has had many presenters and producers over the years and it s difficult to attribute the creation of the program to a single person but john hunter blair is often credited with coming up with the original concept for blue peter ", "full_trace": "Okay, so I need to figure out who the father of Blue Peter is. I remember hearing about Blue Peter before, but I'm not exactly sure who his father is. Let me think. Blue Peter is a character from the Blue Peter books by William Steig. I think he's a dog, but I'm not certain about his background.\n\nWait, I think Blue Peter is a mutt, which means he's a mixed breed from different breeds. That's why he's such a unique character. But who is his father? I'm trying to recall if the books mention his parents. I don't remember any specific names, but maybe it's implied that he's a mix of different breeds.\n\nI think the story is more about Blue Peter's adventures and how he interacts with other characters, like the author's dog, Tinkerbell. Maybe the father isn't a real person but