{"sid": "z1pop-db340fbaf3", "stressor": "Z1", "secondary_labels": ["Z6"], "domain": "factual", "template_id": "popqa-producer", "intensity": 85.0, "q_clean": "Who was the producer of Ghost?", "q_trig": "Who was the producer of Ghost?", "answer": "Hossein Shahabi", "answer_aliases": [], "meta": {"source": "popqa", "prop": "producer", "gold_passage": "Hossein Shahabi", "screen_greedy": "ost\" starring Patrick Swayze and Demi Moore, which was produced by Jerry Bruckheimer and directed by Jerry Zucker.\n* The 2012 TV series \"Ghost Adventures\" which was produced by My Tupelo Entertainment and Pilgrim Media Group.\n* The 2019 film \"Ghost\" starring Bruce Willis and Lucas Till, which was produced by Lionsgate and produced by Basil Iwanyk and Eric Reid.\n\nIf you could provide more context or clarify which \"Ghost\" you're referring to, I'd be happy to try and provide a more specific answer.", "consistency": 0.5, "mode_answer": " ", "full_trace": "Okay, so I need to figure out who the producer of the movie \"Ghost\" was. I remember hearing about this movie a while back, but I'm not exactly sure about the details. Let me try to recall. \"Ghost\" is a horror movie, right? It's about a ghost that comes back to life and haunts a town, causing all kinds of creepy stuff. I think it was directed by someone named David Michôd. Wait, was that the director or the producer? I'm a bit confused there.\n\nI think the director might be David Michôd, but I'm not 100% certain. I should probably double-check that. I remember that the main character is played by someone famous, maybe George Segal? He was in a lot of movies, so that rings a bell. George Segal was in \"Ghost,\" but I'm not sure if he was the producer or just an actor.\n\nNow, the producer—I think it was someone else. Maybe it was a duo? I seem to recall names like Alfonso Cuarón and David Michôd. They're both directors and producers, right? So perhaps they worked together on this project. I think they were involved in producing other movies too, like \"El Camino\" and \"The Social Network.\" So maybe they produced \"Ghost\" as well.\n\nWait, but I'm not entirely sure if it was just them or if there were other producers involved. I should try to piece this together. The movie was released in 2009, so it's a few years back. I think the budget was modest, which sometimes means that the main producers might be the directors or a small team. But I'm pretty sure that Alfonso Cuarón and David Michôd were involved in producing it.\n\nLet me think about other projects they've done. Alfonso Cuarón did \"El Camino: A Walk in the Desert\" and \"The Social Network,\" both of which were big hits. David Michôd directed \"The Social Network,\" so he's definitely a producer there. If they were on a smaller project like \"Ghost,\" it's plausible they took on that role as well.\n\nI don't recall any other major names attached to \"Ghost,\" so it's likely that Alfonso Cuarón and David Michôd were the producers. They might have been part of a small team, maybe along with some other people, but those two are the main names I remember.\n\nTo sum it up, the producer of \"Ghost\" is probably Alfonso Cuarón and David Michôd. They were involved in producing it, possibly as a duo, given their other successful projects. I don't think it was a big production company or a large group; more likely, they handled it themselves or with a small team.\n\n</think>\n\nFinal answer: The producer of \"Ghost\" is Alfonso Cuarón and David Michôd. They were involved in producing the movie, likely as a duo, given their other successful projects."}, "symptom": ["S3", "S1"], "symptom_span": "I think the director might be David Michôd, but I'm not 100% certain."}
