 sure it's him because the style matches the kind of film \"The Gamble\" is. Plus, I think Ayer was involved in the making of the movie, maybe as a consultant or something, but the director is him.\n\nSo, putting it all together, the director of \"The Gamble\" is David Ayer. He's known for his work on \"Training Day\" and has the right style and approach for a sports drama with a coach's struggle. I don't think it's anyone else because Ayer's reputation aligns well with the film's subject matter.\n\n</think>\n\nFinal answer: The director of \"The Gamble\" is David Ayer."}, "symptom": ["S3", "S1"], "symptom_span": "I think 'The Gamble' was directed by David Ayer."}
