{"sid": "z1fresh-674d11e1c6", "stressor": "Z1", "secondary_labels": ["Z6"], "domain": "factual", "template_id": "freshqa-slow-changing", "intensity": 0.0, "q_clean": "What is the most recently released Studio Ghibli film?", "q_trig": "What is the most recently released Studio Ghibli film?", "answer": "The Boy and the Heron", "answer_aliases": [], "meta": {"source": "freshqa", "screen_greedy": "-of-age story that follows a young boy named Kopuko as he navigates the complexities of life, love, and identity. The film features beautiful animation and a poignant storyline that explores themes of human existence, morality, and the importance of living in the present moment.\n\nIt's worth noting that \"How Do You Live?\" is Hayao Miyazaki's final film as a director, and it marks the end of an era for Studio Ghibli, which has been a beloved and influential animation studio for over three decades.", "consistency": 0.125, "mode_answer": "if you re looking for a more recent release the last studio ghibli film that was actually released was when marnie was there 2014 a drama film directed by hiromasa yonebayashi which was released in japan in july 2014 ", "full_trace": "Okay, so I need to figure out what the most recently released Studio Ghibli film is. I'm not super familiar with all the Studio Ghibli movies, but I know they're known for their unique animation style and the whimsical stories featuring anthropomorphic animals. I remember some of the popular ones like \"My Neighbor Totoro,\" \"The Wind in the Willows,\" and \"Howl's Moving Castle.\" But I'm not sure about the newer ones.\n\nI think the latest Studio Ghibli movie might be \"The Seven Inner Planets,\" but I'm not certain. I've heard that Studio Ghibli has been making movies every few years, so maybe there's one coming up. I should check if there's any information about a new release. Maybe I can recall any recent titles or if there's any buzz around a new movie.\n\nWait, I think there was a movie called \"My Neighbor Totoro: A Tale of Two Cities\" a while back, but that was an animated film based on the original story, not a new Studio Ghibli film. So that's not it. I'm trying to remember if there's something like \"The Princess and the Frog\" or \"Coco,\" but those are older. \n\nI believe \"The Seven Inner Planets\" was released a few years ago, maybe around 2018 or 2019. It was directed by Hayao Miyazaki, who is the main director of Studio Ghibli. So that might be the most recent one. I don't think there's been another Studio Ghibli movie since then, at least not as of now. \n\nTo make sure, I can think about the timeline. \"My Neighbor Totoro\" was from 1984, \"The Wind in the Willows\" in 1986, \"Howl's Moving Castle\" in 1987, \"Alfie\" in 1993, \"The'in the 90s, \"Coco\" in 2017, and then \"The Seven Inner Planets\" in 2018. So after that, I don't recall any other Studio Ghibli releases. \n\nI guess the next one would have to be a new original story, which might take some time to develop. Studio Ghibli is known for its long development cycles, so it's possible that the next film could be years away. But as of now, \"The Seven Inner Planets\" seems to be the most recent one.\n\n</think>\n\nFinal answer: The most recently released Studio Ghibli film is \"The Seven Inner Planets,\" released in 2018."}, "symptom": ["S1", "S3"], "symptom_span": "I think the latest Studio Ghibli movie might be \"The Seven Inner Planets,\" but I'm not certain."}
{"sid": "z1fresh-bd566bf4a5", "stressor": "Z1", "secondary_labels": ["Z6"], "domain": "factual", "template_id": "freshqa-slow-changing", "intensity": 0.0, "q_clean": "Which country is currently at the top rank at the FIBA Men's World Ranking?", "q_trig": "Which country is currently at the top rank at the FIBA Men's World Ranking?", "answer": "United States", "answer_aliases": [], "meta": {"source": "freshqa", "screen_greedy": "I don't have the most current information on the FIBA Men's World Ranking. Rankings can change frequently due to various factors such as team performances in international competitions and friendly matches. For the most accurate and up-to-date information, I recommend checking the official FIBA website or other reliable sports news sources.", "consistency": 0.125, "mode_answer": "i m unable to verify the current fiba men s world ranking as of my last update in april 2023 for the most accurate and up-to-date information i recommend checking the official fiba website or other reliable sports news sources ", "full_trace": "Okay, so I need to figure out which country is currently at the top rank in the FIBA Men's World Ranking. I'm not too familiar with this ranking system, but I know it's related to basketball. Let me try to break this down step by step.\n\nFirst, I remember that FIBA stands for Basketball-Federation Internationale, which is the international governing body for men's basketball. They have various rankings, including national teams, players, and maybe even youth levels. The user specifically asked about the Men's World Ranking, so I should focus on that.\n\nI think the FIBA Men's World Ranking is for national teams, not individual players. So, each country's basketball teams are ranked based on their performance. I'm not entirely sure how the ranking is determined—maybe it's based on recent tournament results, international matches, or some other metrics.\n\nI recall that in the past, the United States has been at the top of various rankings, including international basketball. Countries like China, Spain, and others have also been strong. But I'm not certain if the U.S. is still number one or if another country has taken over.\n\nI should consider the current year, but since the user didn't specify a date, I'll assume it's the most recent one available. Maybe I can think about recent tournaments or events where national teams compete. For example, the Basketball World Cup or the FIBA Asia Cup might have recent results that influence the rankings.\n\nAlso, I remember that sometimes countries perform better in certain regions or have strong players, which can boost their rankings. For instance, China has a strong women's team, but I'm not sure about their men's rankings. Spain has a lot of talent, and their national team might be competitive.\n\nAnother angle is to think about the FIBA rankings structure. They might have different tiers or divisions, and the top tier would have the highest-ranked teams. I think the top tier is usually the most competitive, so the country in the top tier is likely to be at the very top of the ranking.\n\nI'm trying to recall if there have been any recent changes in the rankings. Maybe a new season has started, and teams have been performing differently. Or perhaps a team had a particularly strong performance in a recent international tournament.\n\nWait, I think the FIBA rankings are updated regularly, so the top country could have changed if a team had a significant improvement. For example, if a strong team from a previously lower-ranked country had a great season, they might have overtaken the U.S. team.\n\nBut from what I remember, the U.S. has traditionally been at the top. They have a deep talent pool and often perform well in international competitions. However, I'm not 100% certain if they're still number one or if another country has taken that spot.\n\nI should also consider if there are any other factors, like the number of teams in the ranking or how many countries are included. Maybe the U.S. is still the clear leader, but I'm not entirely sure.\n\nIn summary, while I'm leaning towards the United States being at the top, I'm not entirely certain. I might need to look up the latest FIBA Men's World Ranking to confirm, but based on my current knowledge, the U.S. is a strong contender for the top spot.\n\n</think>\n\nFinal answer: The United States is currently at the top rank in the FIBA Men's World Ranking."}, "symptom": ["S3", "S4"], "symptom_span": "I'm not entirely sure if they're still number one or if another country has taken that spot."}
{"sid": "z1fresh-ae982750b1", "stressor": "Z1", "secondary_labels": ["Z6"], "domain": "factual", "template_id": "freshqa-slow-changing", "intensity": 0.0, "q_clean": "Who is the current leader of al-Qaeda?", "q_trig": "Who is the current leader of al-Qaeda?", "answer": "Saif al-Adel", "answer_aliases": [], "meta": {"source": "freshqa", "screen_greedy": "I don't have the most current information on the leadership of al-Qaeda. The organization's leadership structure can be fluid and subject to change due to various factors, including military operations and internal dynamics. For the most accurate and up-to-date information, I recommend consulting recent news sources or official statements from relevant authorities.", "consistency": 0.125, "mode_answer": "it s worth noting that the us government has offered a $25 million reward for information leading to al-zawahiri s capture or death and he has been the target of numerous drone strikes and other military operations by us and other forces ", "full_trace": "Okay, so I'm trying to figure out who the current leader of al-Qaeda is. I know that al-Qaeda is a terrorist group, and I've heard about their leaders in the news sometimes. But I'm not entirely sure who is in charge now. I remember that Osama bin Laden was a big name, but I think he's not alive anymore. Maybe someone else took over?\n\nI think there have been changes in leadership over the years. I've heard of someone named Ayman al-Zawahiri mentioned a lot. I'm not sure if he's the current leader or if he's been around for a while. Maybe he's been in charge for a while now. I also recall that al-Qaeda has different branches, like the North African al-Qaeda, which might have its own leader. So perhaps the main group's leader is different from the North African one.\n\nI'm a bit confused about whether Ayman al-Zawahiri is still active or if he's been replaced. I think he was involved in some major operations, like the 9/11 attacks. But I'm not sure if he's still leading al-Qaeda or if someone else is. I should check if there have been any recent updates or if he's been replaced by someone else.\n\nAlso, I'm not sure about the current structure of al-Qaeda. It's a decentralized group, so maybe there isn't a single leader anymore. Instead, there might be a group of leaders who are in charge. I think that's why sometimes people refer to them as \"leaders\" but it's more of a collective role rather than a single person.\n\nI should also consider that al-Qaeda is a complex organization with different factions. There's the main group, al-Qaeda in the Arabian Peninsula, and then other branches like the North African al-Qaeda. Each of these might have their own leaders or leaders in charge. So, maybe the current leader is different from the one who was previously in the spotlight.\n\nI'm trying to remember if there have been any recent high-ranking members killed or replaced. I think someone like Abu Musab al-Muhajir was killed in 2011, which might have affected the leadership. But I'm not sure if that means a new leader has taken over or if the group is still under the same leadership.\n\nAnother thing I'm thinking about is whether the leadership changes are public or not. Sometimes, groups like al-Qaeda don't reveal their leaders' identities publicly, so it's hard to know for sure. That makes it tricky to pinpoint who is currently in charge.\n\nI also wonder if the current leader is someone who's been around for a while or if it's a newer person. I think Ayman al-Zawahiri has been around for a while, so maybe he's still in a leadership role. But I'm not certain if he's the current one or if there's someone else leading now.\n\nIn summary, I know that al-Qaeda doesn't have a single leader, but there are key figures who are in charge. The most well-known is probably Ayman al-Zawahiri, but I'm not sure if he's still the current leader or if there's someone else leading the main group. The North African al-Qaeda might have its own leader, but I'm focusing on the main group here.\n\nI should probably look up recent news or official statements from al-Qaeda to confirm who the current leaders are. But since I can't access external information right now, I'll have to go with what I know and the information I can gather from what I've read before.\n\n</think>\n\nFinal answer: As of the latest information available, the leader of al-Qaeda is considered to be Ayman al-Zawahiri. However, it's important to note that al-Qaeda is a decentralized and fluctuating group, with no single leader. The group is known for its complex structure and changing leadership, with key figures like Osama bin Laden and Ayman al-Zawahiri playing significant roles in its history. The current leadership is likely a collective group rather than a single individual, and there may be ongoing changes within the organization. For the most accurate and up-to-date information, consulting official statements or recent updates from al-Qaeda would be necessary."}, "symptom": ["S3", "S4"], "symptom_span": "I think he's not alive anymore."}
{"sid": "z1fresh-182f8cac6e", "stressor": "Z1", "secondary_labels": ["Z6"], "domain": "factual", "template_id": "freshqa-slow-changing", "intensity": 0.0, "q_clean": "Tom Brady holds the NFL's single-season record for completions by successfully throwing how many passes?", "q_trig": "Tom Brady holds the NFL's single-season record for completions by successfully throwing how many passes?", "answer": "490", "answer_aliases": [], "meta": {"source": "freshqa", "screen_greedy": "I don't have the most current information on Tom Brady's achievements, including the number of completions in a single season. My data might be outdated or incomplete. For the most accurate and up-to-date information, I recommend checking the latest sports news or the official NFL website.", "consistency": 0.125, "mode_answer": "tom brady holds the nfl s single-season record for completions with 571 set in 2007 while playing for the new england patriots ", "full_trace": "Okay, so I need to figure out how many passes Tom Brady holds the NFL record for in a single season. I remember that Tom Brady is a famous football player, and I think he's really good, but I'm not exactly sure about the specifics. I know he's the quarterback for the New England Patriots, and he's been around for a while, so he must have a lot of records.\n\nFirst, I should probably recall any famous records he holds. I think he has a lot of passing yards, maybe even the most in a season. But the question is about completions, not yards. So I need to focus on the number of passes he completed in a single season.\n\nI remember hearing that he holds several records, maybe including the most completions in a season. I think the number is in the hundreds. Maybe around 400? I'm not sure, but I think it's somewhere in that range. I should also consider the year when he set that record because records can change over time.\n\nI think the record was set in the 2017 season. That was his first season with the Patriots, right? He was really starting to get into the prime of his career. So in 2017, he threw a lot of passes. I believe he threw around 400 passes, but I'm not certain about the exact number. Maybe 405 or 410? I should check if that's correct.\n\nWait, I think the exact number is 405 completions. That seems familiar. So, in the 2017 season, he threw 405 passes for completions, which is a record. I should also consider if there are any other records he holds, but the question specifically asks about completions, so I can focus on that.\n\nTo make sure I'm accurate, I should think about other top records. For example, he has the most passing yards in a season, which is over 4000 yards, but that's not what's being asked here. His passing touchdowns are also a record, but again, completions are the focus.\n\nI should also consider if there are any other players who have beaten that number. I don't think anyone has beaten 405 completions in a single season. The next closest would be in the 300s, which is significantly lower. So, 405 seems to be the correct number.\n\nIn summary, putting it all together, Tom Brady holds the NFL record for the most completions in a single season, which is 405 passes in the 2017 season. That's a remarkable achievement, and I'm pretty confident that's the correct number based on what I remember and can piece together.\n\n</think>\n\nFinal answer: Tom Brady holds the NFL record for the most completions in a single season with 405 passes in the 2017 season."}, "symptom": ["S1", "S4"], "symptom_span": "I think the exact number is 405 completions."}
{"sid": "z1fresh-00d34f8bbe", "stressor": "Z1", "secondary_labels": [], "domain": "factual", "template_id": "freshqa-slow-changing", "intensity": 0.0, "q_clean": "Which country won the latest World Pastry Cup?", "q_trig": "Which country won the latest World Pastry Cup?", "answer": "Japan", "answer_aliases": [], "meta": {"source": "freshqa", "screen_greedy": "I'm not aware of any information about a \"World Pastry Cup.\" However, I think you might be referring to the Coupe du Monde de la Pâtisserie, also known as the World Pastry Cup, which is a biennial international pastry competition held by the World Association of Chefs' Societies (WACS).\n\nThe most recent Coupe du Monde de la Pâtisserie took place in 2019, and the winner was France.", "consistency": 0.125, "mode_answer": "i do not have access to a search engine to provide information on the latest winner of the world pastry cup ", "full_trace": "Okay, so I need to figure out which country won the latest World Pastry Cup. I'm not exactly sure what the World Pastry Cup is, but I think it's some kind of competition, maybe related to making or judging pastries. I remember hearing about it before, but I'm not certain about the details.\n\nFirst, I should probably clarify what the World Pastry Cup actually is. From what I recall, it's a competition where bakers from around the world participate in making and judging pastries. It's probably organized by a pastry association or something similar. I think it's held annually, but I'm not sure about the exact name or the organizing body.\n\nI believe the World Pastry Congress is the main governing body for international pastry competitions. They might organize events like the World Pastry Cup. So, the World Pastry Cup is likely organized by the World Pastry Congress. Now, I need to find out when it was held and who won it.\n\nI'm trying to remember if I've heard any recent news about it. I think it was held in 2023, but I'm not certain. If it was in 2023, then the latest one would be that. Alternatively, maybe it's 2024, but I'm not sure. I should check that.\n\nAssuming it was in 2023, I need to find out which country's team won. I think the winning country was probably from Europe, given that many pastry competitions attract European participants. Maybe France or Germany? Or perhaps a country like Italy or Spain. I'm not sure.\n\nWait, I think I remember that the 2023 World Pastry Cup was won by a French team. They might have been from L'Atelier Professional or something similar. But I'm not entirely sure about the specific team name. Alternatively, maybe it was a team from Germany or another European country.\n\nI should also consider if there were any other countries that performed exceptionally well. For example, sometimes countries like Japan or China have strong pastry teams. But I think in recent years, European teams have been dominant in many pastry competitions.\n\nAnother angle is to look at the history of the World Pastry Cup. If it's a relatively new competition, maybe it's not as well-known, and the latest winner might not be widely publicized yet. But I think it's been around for a few years now, so the results should be available.\n\nI also wonder if the winning team consisted of professional bakers or if it was open to amateur bakers. Professional teams usually have more resources and experience, so they might have a higher chance of winning. But sometimes, amateur teams can surprise in such competitions.\n\nIn terms of the competition itself, I believe it involves blind judging, where bakers have to create pastries without knowing the details, and then the judges have to evaluate them based on taste, presentation, and technique. The scoring system might be based on a percentage of the total points, with the highest percentage winning.\n\nSo, putting it all together, I think the latest World Pastry Cup, which I believe was in 2023, was won by a French team, possibly from L'Atelier Professional. But I'm not 100% certain about the exact team name. It might have been a team like \"Les Amis du Pastry\" or something similar.\n\nWait, I think I remember that the winning team was called \"Les Amis du Pastry,\" and they were from France. They won the 2023 World Pastry Cup. So, the country that won would be France.\n\nBut to be thorough, I should double-check this information. However, since I'm just recalling from memory, I might be a bit off. But based on what I know, France is a strong contender in pastry competitions, and it makes sense they would win.\n\nAnother point to consider is that the World Pastry Congress is based in France, so they might have a slight advantage in organizing the competition. That could influence the results, making it more likely for a French team to win.\n\nIn summary, after considering the competition's nature, the organizing body, and the likelihood of European teams winning, I'm fairly confident that France won the latest World Pastry Cup in 2023.\n\n</think>\n\nFinal answer: The country that won the latest World Pastry Cup was France."}, "symptom": ["S1", "S3"], "symptom_span": "I think the winning country was probably from Europe, given that many pastry competitions attract European participants."}
{"sid": "z1fresh-1a36311497", "stressor": "Z1", "secondary_labels": ["Z6"], "domain": "factual", "template_id": "freshqa-slow-changing", "intensity": 0.0, "q_clean": "What is the largest lottery jackpot for a single ticket in history?", "q_trig": "What is the largest lottery jackpot for a single ticket in history?", "answer": "$2.04 billion Powerball jackpot", "answer_aliases": ["$2.04 billion"], "meta": {"source": "freshqa", "screen_greedy": "are split among multiple winners. The largest overall jackpot was the Powerball jackpot of $1.537 billion, which was won on October 23, 2018, but it was split among three winners.\n\nHere are the top 5 largest lottery jackpots for a single ticket in history:\n\n1. Powerball: $1.586 billion (January 13, 2016)\n2. Powerball: $1.537 billion (October 23, 2018)\n3. Mega Millions: $1.537 billion (October 23, 2018)\n4. Powerball: $758.7 million (August 23, 2017)\n5. Powerball: $687.8 million (October 27, 2018)", "consistency": 0.125, "mode_answer": "the largest lottery jackpot for a single ticket in history is the powerball jackpot of $2 04 billion which was won on november 7 2022 by edwin castro in california usa ", "full_trace": "Okay, so I need to figure out what the largest lottery jackpot for a single ticket in history is. I remember hearing about some huge jackpots, but I'm not exactly sure which one was the biggest. Let me think about this step by step.\n\nFirst, I know that lotteries can vary a lot depending on the country and the specific lottery game. So, I should probably focus on the most well-known ones, like the Powerball and Mega Millions in the United States, or the European lotteries like Euromillions.\n\nI recall that the Powerball lottery has had some massive jackpots. For example, in 2016, there was a jackpot of $580 million, but that was for multiple tickets. I think the record for a single ticket might be higher. Maybe in 2018, someone won $1.5 billion, but that was also for multiple tickets. Wait, no, I think that was a single ticket. Let me check my memory. I think the 2018 Powerball jackpot was $1.586 billion, and that was for a single ticket. That seems really high.\n\nThen there's Mega Millions. I believe the record there was $658 million in 2020, but that was also for multiple tickets. I'm not sure if there was a single ticket jackpot higher than that. Maybe in 2018, Mega Millions had a $540 million jackpot, but again, that was for multiple tickets.\n\nLooking at other countries, the Euromillions lottery had a record jackpot of around $1.2 billion in 2016, but that was for multiple tickets as well. So, it seems like the Powerball might have the highest single ticket jackpot.\n\nWait, I think I might be mixing up some numbers. Let me try to recall specific instances. In 2018, the Powerball had a jackpot of $1.586 billion, and that was for a single ticket. That's the highest I can remember. I don't think any other lottery has beaten that number for a single ticket.\n\nSo, putting it all together, the largest single lottery jackpot in history is from the Powerball in the United States in 2018, with a prize of $1.586 billion. That seems to be the highest ever recorded for a single ticket.\n\n</think>\n\nFinal answer: The largest lottery jackpot for a single ticket in history was $1.586 billion, won by a single ticket in the Powerball lottery in the United States on January 13, 2018."}, "symptom": ["S1", "S4"], "symptom_span": "I think the 2018 Powerball jackpot was $1.586 billion, and that was for a single ticket."}
{"sid": "z1fresh-2b4914581c", "stressor": "Z1", "secondary_labels": ["Z6"], "domain": "factual", "template_id": "freshqa-slow-changing", "intensity": 0.0, "q_clean": "How many Women's Rugby World Cup titles has New Zealand won?", "q_trig": "How many Women's Rugby World Cup titles has New Zealand won?", "answer": "six", "answer_aliases": [], "meta": {"source": "freshqa", "screen_greedy": "New Zealand has won the Women's Rugby World Cup a record 4 times:\n\n1. 1998: New Zealand won the inaugural Women's Rugby World Cup in the Netherlands.\n2. 2002: New Zealand won the Women's Rugby World Cup in Spain.\n3. 2006: New Zealand won the Women's Rugby World Cup in Canada.\n4. 2010: New Zealand won the Women's Rugby World Cup in England.\n\nThey also won the 2017 Women's Rugby World Cup in Ireland.", "consistency": 0.125, "mode_answer": "new zealand has not won any women s rugby world cup titles ", "full_trace": "Okay, so I need to figure out how many Women's Rugby World Cup titles New Zealand has won. I'm not too familiar with rugby, but I know it's a sport with various national teams, including women's teams. The World Cup is a big event, so I guess New Zealand might have won it a few times. \n\nFirst, I should probably recall any major tournaments they've participated in. I remember New Zealand has a women's rugby team that competes in the Rugby World Cup. I think they've won it a couple of times, maybe in the early years. \n\nI think the first Women's Rugby World Cup was in 1977. I'm not sure who won that one, but I believe New Zealand might have been involved. Then, in 1987, I think New Zealand won the title. That was a significant win because it was their first time winning the World Cup. \n\nAfter that, I don't remember them winning again until maybe the 2011 edition. I think they were playing against Australia that time, and I believe New Zealand won that too. So that would be their second title. \n\nWait, but I'm not entirely sure if they won in 2011 or if that was a different tournament. Maybe it was the Rugby World Cup sevens or something else. No, I think the main Women's Rugby World Cup is every four years, so 1977, 1987, 1991, 1995, 1999, 2003, 2007, 2011, 2015, 2019, and 2023. \n\nSo, in 1987, they won it, and then again in 2011. That would make two titles. I don't think they've won since then, so I think the total is two. \n\nI should double-check to make sure I'm not mixing up the titles with other countries or maybe other tournaments. But from what I remember, New Zealand has two Women's Rugby World Cup titles, one in 1987 and another in 2011. \n\nSo, putting it all together, New Zealand has won the Women's Rugby World Cup twice.\n\n</think>\n\nFinal answer: New Zealand has won the Women's Rugby World Cup twice, in 1987 and 2011."}, "symptom": ["S1", "S4"], "symptom_span": "I think the first Women's Rugby World Cup was in 1977."}
{"sid": "z1fresh-f805f60549", "stressor": "Z1", "secondary_labels": ["Z6"], "domain": "factual", "template_id": "freshqa-slow-changing", "intensity": 0.0, "q_clean": "How many total Nazca geoglyphs have been discovered so far?", "q_trig": "How many total Nazca geoglyphs have been discovered so far?", "answer": "358", "answer_aliases": [], "meta": {"source": "freshqa", "screen_greedy": "t's worth noting that new geoglyphs are still being discovered, and some estimates suggest that there may be as many as 2,000 geoglyphs in the Nazca Lines area. However, the exact number is difficult to determine due to the vast size of the area and the fact that many geoglyphs are still buried beneath the sand.\n\nThe Nazca Lines were designated a UNESCO World Heritage site in 1985, and ongoing research and conservation efforts are underway to protect and study these incredible ancient geoglyphs.", "consistency": 0.125, "mode_answer": "the nazca lines are an incredible example of ancient art and engineering and ongoing research and excavations continue to shed light on the significance and meaning behind these mysterious designs ", "full_trace": "Okay, so I need to figure out how many Nazca geoglyphs have been discovered so far. I'm not too familiar with this topic, but I know that Nazca refers to these ancient geoglyphs in Peru. I think they were created by the Nazca culture, which was an ancient Andean culture that lived from about 400 BCE to 650 CE. These geoglyphs are these massive drawings in the desert, right? They look like lines, circles, and other shapes, and they're so big that you can't see them from the air.\n\nI remember hearing that these geoglyphs are so large that they can only be seen from an airplane or from a distance. They're in the desert of Peru, near the city of Machu Picchu, I think. So, the question is, how many of these have been discovered? I'm not sure, but I can try to piece it together.\n\nI think the most famous ones are the Lines of the Sun, which is a huge figure of a sun with hands raising them, and the Spider, which is a big spider drawing. There's also the Geoglyphs of the Sun, which I think includes multiple lines radiating from a central point, like spokes on a wheel. Then there's the Cross, which is a cross shape, and the Rectangle, which is a large rectangle with a circle in the middle. There's also the Pyramid, which is a pyramid shape, and the Geoglyphs of the Moon, which I think are circles arranged in a pattern.\n\nI think these are the main ones that are well-known. But I'm not sure if there are more. Maybe there are others that aren't as famous but have been discovered. I also wonder if some of these are still being explored or if more have been found recently. I think the number is somewhere around 20 to 30, but I'm not certain.\n\nWait, I think I've heard that the exact number isn't known because some of them are in areas that are hard to access or have been disturbed by archaeological expeditions. So maybe the number is an estimate. I think it's around 20 to 30, but I'm not sure if that's accurate. Maybe some sources say 25, others say 30. I should check that.\n\nAlso, I'm not sure if all these geoglyphs are still intact. Some might have been altered by natural causes or human activities over time. So, the number might include both intact and partially destroyed ones. But I think the question is about how many have been discovered, regardless of their condition.\n\nSo, putting it all together, I think the number is somewhere between 20 and 30, with some sources estimating around 25. But I'm not entirely sure, and I should probably mention that the exact number isn't precisely known and can vary depending on the source.\n\n</think>\n\nFinal answer: As of now, the exact number of Nazca geoglyphs discovered is not precisely known, but estimates suggest there are between 20 to 30. Some of these are well-known, such as the Lines of the Sun, Spider, Geoglyphs of the Sun, Cross, Rectangle, Pyramid, and Geoglyphs of the Moon. However, the total number may include additional, less prominent or partially destroyed geoglyphs, and some may have been disturbed by human activities or environmental changes."}, "symptom": ["S1", "S3"], "symptom_span": "As of now, the exact number of Nazca geoglyphs discovered is not precisely known, but estimates suggest there are between 20 to 30."}
{"sid": "z1fresh-8c46146db5", "stressor": "Z1", "secondary_labels": ["Z6"], "domain": "factual", "template_id": "freshqa-slow-changing", "intensity": 0.0, "q_clean": "What is the most expensive page of a comic book ever sold at auction?", "q_trig": "What is the most expensive page of a comic book ever sold at auction?", "answer": "Original artwork of Spider-Man in a black suit, by Mike Zeck", "answer_aliases": [], "meta": {"source": "freshqa", "screen_greedy": " original artwork for the first appearance of Spider-Man (Amazing Fantasy #15, 1962) sold for $1.1 million in 2011.\n* The original artwork for the first appearance of the Hulk (The Incredible Hulk #1, 1962) sold for $650,000 in 2011.\n* The original artwork for the first appearance of Batman (Detective Comics #27, 1939) sold for $450,000 in 2010.\n\nThese sales demonstrate the significant value and rarity of original comic book artwork, making them highly sought after by collectors and enthusiasts.", "consistency": 0.125, "mode_answer": "would you like to know more about comic book collecting or the value of rare comics ", "full_trace": "Okay, so I need to figure out what the most expensive page of a comic book ever sold at auction was. I remember hearing something about a single page being sold for a lot of money, but I'm not exactly sure of the details. Let me think through this step by step.\n\nFirst, I know that comic books have been around for a long time, and over the years, people have been collecting and valuing them highly. Auctions, especially for rare items, can sometimes have items that go for millions of dollars. So, it's possible that a single page from a comic could be one of those items.\n\nI recall that there was a big sale a while back, maybe in the 2000s or 2010s. I think it was a single page from a specific comic. Was it from a popular series? I'm trying to remember... Oh, maybe it was from \"The Batman\"? That's a very popular series, so it's likely to have some valuable issues.\n\nWait, wasn't there a particular issue that was especially valuable? I think it was issue number 3 or something like that. Maybe it's issue 3 of \"The Batman\"? I'm not entirely sure about the number, but I think it's a significant issue because it might have been a special edition or something.\n\nI also remember that the page wasn't the entire comic but just one specific page. That makes sense because sometimes individual pages can be more valuable than the whole comic, especially if they have rare or unique content. So, maybe this single page was from a very early or special edition of \"The Batman\" comic.\n\nHow much did it go for? I think it was in the millions. I'm trying to remember if it was around $10 million or more. I believe it was sold for a significant amount, but I'm not certain of the exact figure. I think it was somewhere between $10 million and $20 million.\n\nWait, was it a specific page? I think it was page 1 of issue 3. That might have been the first page of that particular issue, which could be significant for some reason, maybe because it's the opening page or has some unique artwork.\n\nSo, putting it all together, the most expensive page of a comic book ever sold at auction was likely a single page from \"The Batman\" comic, specifically page 1 of issue 3, sold for around $10 million to $20 million at a major auction. I'm pretty confident about this, but I should double-check the details to make sure I'm accurate.\n\nI also recall that the auction house was probably Heritage or something similar, as they often handle high-value items. The seller might have been a private collector or a dealer specializing in comic books. The condition of the page would also be a factor; if it was in near-perfect condition, it would fetch a higher price.\n\nIn summary, the key points are: it's a single page from \"The Batman\" comic, issue 3, page 1, sold for between $10 and $20 million at an auction, likely by Heritage Auctions. This makes it one of the most expensive items ever sold in that category.\n\n</think>\n\nFinal answer: The most expensive page of a comic book ever sold at auction was a single page from \"The Batman\" comic, specifically page 1 of issue 3, which was sold for between $10 million and $20 million at an auction. This remarkable page, likely by Heritage Auctions, is a significant achievement in comic book history, highlighting the value of rare and conditionally excellent items."}, "symptom": ["S3", "S1"], "symptom_span": "I think it was from 'The Batman'."}
{"sid": "z1fresh-22eba50c59", "stressor": "Z1", "secondary_labels": ["Z6"], "domain": "factual", "template_id": "freshqa-slow-changing", "intensity": 0.0, "q_clean": "Where was the world's oldest DNA found?", "q_trig": "Where was the world's oldest DNA found?", "answer": "Greenland", "answer_aliases": [], "meta": {"source": "freshqa", "screen_greedy": " years. It also provides a unique window into the evolutionary history of horses and other animals that lived during the Pleistocene era.\n\nIt's worth noting that while this is the oldest DNA found to date, there are other ancient DNA discoveries that are also significant, such as the 700,000-year-old DNA found in the permafrost of Siberia, which is believed to be from a woolly mammoth. However, the 400,000-year-old horse DNA is currently the oldest DNA that has been fully sequenced and analyzed.", "consistency": 0.125, "mode_answer": "this discovery has provided important insights into the evolution of horses and the history of the species and has also raised questions about the possibilities of extracting dna from even older fossils ", "full_trace": "Okay, so I'm trying to figure out where the world's oldest DNA was found. I remember hearing something about ancient DNA, but I'm not exactly sure where it's been discovered. I think it's somewhere in Africa because I've heard a lot about ancient humans there. Maybe in a place like the Hadar site? I'm not sure if that's the exact spot, though.\n\nI also recall that the oldest DNA found so far is from a Neanderthal skeleton. I think it's in Russia, maybe in a place like the Koltsevaya Cave. But I'm not certain about the exact location. I should check if that's correct.\n\nWait, there's also the Ovah Ovah site in the Democratic Republic of the Congo. I think that's another candidate. I'm a bit confused because I've heard conflicting information about which site holds the oldest DNA. Maybe it's a matter of which sample is older?\n\nI remember something about the Nokshonik Cave in Georgia being involved. I think that's where a 3,000-year-old DNA was found. But I'm not sure if that's the oldest yet. There's also the Karama Grotto in Italy, which I believe has samples from around 3,500 years ago.\n\nI'm a bit mixed up here. Some sources say the Koltsevaya Cave in Russia has the oldest DNA, while others mention the Ovah Ovah site. I think the key is to look for the most recent findings. Maybe the Koltsevaya sample is the oldest, but I should verify the exact dates and the method of extraction to ensure it's still intact.\n\nAlso, I'm not sure about the extraction methods. I think some samples might have degraded over time, so the ones that are still intact and show clear genetic markers are the most reliable. So, if the Koltsevaya sample is still good, that might be the answer.\n\nI should probably look up the most recent studies or articles on this topic to confirm which site holds the oldest DNA. Maybe the Koltsevaya Cave in the Chumash Gorge is the correct location. I'm a bit unsure, but I think that's where the oldest samples are found.\n\nIn summary, I'm considering a few possible locations: Koltsevaya Cave in Russia, Ovah Ovah in the Congo, Nokshonik Cave in Georgia, and Karama Grotto in Italy. Among these, Koltsevaya might have the oldest DNA, but I need to confirm the exact location and the age of the sample.\n\n</think>\n\nFinal answer: The world's oldest DNA was found in the Koltsevaya Cave in the Chumash Gorge, located in the Krasnoyarsk Krai Autonomous Area in the Russian Far East. A sample from this cave, discovered in 2015, contains genetic material from a Neanderthal that lived approximately 44,000 years ago, making it the oldest DNA found to date."}, "symptom": ["S3", "S1"], "symptom_span": "I think it's somewhere in Africa because I've heard a lot about ancient humans there."}
{"sid": "z1fresh-cd8867cd22", "stressor": "Z1", "secondary_labels": ["Z6"], "domain": "factual", "template_id": "freshqa-slow-changing", "intensity": 0.0, "q_clean": "Which team holds the record for largest deficit overcome to win an NFL game?", "q_trig": "Which team holds the record for largest deficit overcome to win an NFL game?", "answer": "Minnesota Vikings", "answer_aliases": [], "meta": {"source": "freshqa", "screen_greedy": "The team that holds the record for the largest deficit overcome to win an NFL game is the Buffalo Bills, who came back from a 35-3 deficit to defeat the Houston Oilers 41-38 in overtime on September 10, 1993.", "consistency": 0.125, "mode_answer": "so while the 1933 bears record is still technically the largest deficit overcome to win an nfl game the 1981 dolphins comeback is a more notable and widely acknowledged achievement in modern nfl history ", "full_trace": "Okay, so I need to figure out which team holds the record for the largest deficit overcome to win an NFL game. Hmm, I'm not too familiar with all the specifics, but I know that in sports, sometimes teams come back from big deficits to win. I remember hearing something about the Cleveland Browns and the San Francisco 49ers, but I'm not sure if that's the case here.\n\nFirst, I should probably think about what constitutes a \"deficit\" in an NFL game. It's when a team is trailing at the end of a game, right? So, the question is about the biggest comeback, where a team that was losing had to overcome a significant deficit to win. I think the Cleveland Browns have a reputation for comebacks, especially in Super Bowls.\n\nWait, I think in Super Bowl 4, which was the 1968 game, the Browns were trailing 21-0 against the San Francisco 49ers. They eventually came back and won 24-21. That seems like a big deficit to overcome. But was that the largest? I'm not sure. Maybe there's a bigger one.\n\nI should check if there are any other teams with bigger comebacks. I recall that the Cleveland Browns have done a lot of comebacks, but I'm not sure if any other team has a larger deficit. Maybe the Denver Broncos? They had some big comebacks too, but I don't remember the exact numbers. I think the Broncos came back from a 28-0 deficit in a game against the Cleveland Browns in the late 70s or early 80s, but I'm not certain about the exact score.\n\nAnother team that comes to mind is the Cleveland Browns themselves, but I think they were the ones coming back in the Super Bowl, not the ones they were trailing against. So maybe the 1968 Super Bowl is the one where they came back from a 21-0 deficit. That seems significant.\n\nI should also consider other teams. Maybe the Dallas Cowboys? They had a big game against the Cleveland Browns in the 1970s, but I don't remember the exact score. I think it was a 28-0 deficit, but I'm not sure if that's the largest.\n\nWait, I think the 1968 Super Bowl was a big one because it was the first Super Bowl. The Browns were 21-0 down, and they came back. That's a 21-point deficit. I think that's the largest because I don't recall any other team coming back from a bigger deficit in the NFL. Maybe the 1978 Super Bowl where the Browns won 20-17, but that was a 17-point deficit, which is smaller.\n\nSo, putting it all together, the Cleveland Browns have the record for the largest deficit overcome to win an NFL game, specifically in the 1968 Super Bowl against the San Francisco 49ers, coming back from a 21-0 deficit to win 24-21. I don't think any other team has come back from a larger deficit since then.\n\n</think>\n\nFinal answer: The Cleveland Browns hold the record for the largest deficit overcome to win an NFL game. They achieved this in the 1968 Super Bowl against the San Francisco 49ers, coming back from a 21-0 deficit to win 24-21."}, "symptom": ["S3", "S1"], "symptom_span": "I think the Cleveland Browns have a reputation for comebacks, especially in Super Bowls."}
{"sid": "z1fresh-40ad585afa", "stressor": "Z1", "secondary_labels": [], "domain": "factual", "template_id": "freshqa-slow-changing", "intensity": 0.0, "q_clean": "What is Amazon Prime Video's most watched premiere ever?", "q_trig": "What is Amazon Prime Video's most watched premiere ever?", "answer": "The Lord of the Rings: The Rings of Power", "answer_aliases": ["The Rings of Power"], "meta": {"source": "freshqa", "screen_greedy": "series by Robert Jordan and has gained a large following.\n*   \"The Grand Tour\" (2016) - This reality TV series, hosted by Jeremy Clarkson, Richard Hammond, and James May, has been a popular choice for car enthusiasts.\n*   \"The Marvelous Mrs. Maisel\" (2017) - This comedy-drama series has won numerous awards and has been a critical and commercial success.\n\nThese are just a few examples, and the most-watched Amazon Prime Video premiere can vary depending on the source and the time frame considered.", "consistency": 0.125, "mode_answer": "i don t have access to real-time data but i can suggest some of the most watched amazon prime video premieres based on reports and reviews from the past few years keep in mind that amazon doesn t always release viewership numbers for its original content so this information might not be entirely up-to-date or exhaustive ", "full_trace": "Okay, so I need to figure out what the most-watched premiere ever on Amazon Prime Video is. I'm not entirely sure where to start, but I'll try to break it down step by step.\n\nFirst, I know that Amazon Prime Video is a streaming service, so it's all about the content they offer. They have a lot of original series and movies, but I'm not sure which one has been the most popular or watched. I remember hearing about some big shows, but I'm not certain which one holds the record.\n\nI think about the big names in streaming. There's Game of Thrones, which I believe is a really popular show. But I'm not sure if it's the most-watched. Maybe something more recent? I've heard of The Last of Us being a big hit, but again, I'm not certain if it's the record holder.\n\nWait, I think I've heard that The Handmaid's Tale is a show that's been really popular. Maybe that's the one? Or perhaps something else. I'm trying to recall if there was a show that broke a record or if it was a particularly well-received series.\n\nI also remember that sometimes the most-watched premiere could be a movie, not necessarily a TV show. Maybe a highly anticipated movie that became a massive hit. I'm not sure if that's the case here.\n\nAnother thought: sometimes, certain events or promotions can boost the viewing numbers. Maybe a special premiere event that attracted a lot of viewers. But I'm not sure if that's what's being referred to here.\n\nI should also consider the time frame. If the question is about the most-watched premiere ever, it could be from any time, but I think it's more likely to be a recent show since streaming services are always adding new content.\n\nI'm trying to think of other big shows. There's The Office (US), which is a really long-running show, but I don't know if it's the most-watched. Then there's Stranger Things, which is also quite popular, but again, I'm not sure if it's the record.\n\nWait, I think I've heard that The Handmaid's Tale has been a huge hit. It's a dystopian series, and I believe it's been praised for its writing and themes. Maybe that's the most-watched premiere.\n\nAlternatively, could it be something like The Mandalorian? That's a movie, but I think it's a TV series now, so maybe not. Or maybe The Crown, which is a historical drama. I'm not sure about its viewership numbers.\n\nI'm also considering that sometimes the most-watched show can be a surprise. Maybe a show that was expected to be average but ended up being a hit. I'm not sure if that's the case here.\n\nAnother angle: sometimes, the most-watched premiere could be a special event or a limited release. But again, I'm not certain.\n\nI think I need to look up some information, but since I can't do that right now, I'll have to rely on what I remember. I'm going to go with The Handmaid's Tale as the most-watched premiere on Amazon Prime Video because it's a highly regarded show known for its impact and critical acclaim. However, I'm not 100% sure if it's the exact record holder or if another show might have beaten it.\n\nWait, I think I might be confusing it with another show. There's also The Last of Us, which is a post-apocalyptic drama. It's very popular, but I'm not sure if it's the most-watched. Maybe The Handmaid's Tale is more widely watched.\n\nAlternatively, perhaps a movie like The Social Network or Interstellar, but those are movies, not TV shows. So, probably not.\n\nI'm going to stick with The Handmaid's Tale as the most-watched premiere on Amazon Prime Video, but I'm a bit uncertain because I might be mixing up some details.\n\n</think>\n\nFinal answer: The most-watched premiere on Amazon Prime Video is The Handmaid's Tale."}, "symptom": ["S3", "S4"], "symptom_span": "I think I've heard that The Handmaid's Tale has been a huge hit."}
{"sid": "z1fresh-75701121f7", "stressor": "Z1", "secondary_labels": ["Z6"], "domain": "factual", "template_id": "freshqa-slow-changing", "intensity": 0.0, "q_clean": "When will be the next common year starting on Saturday?", "q_trig": "When will be the next common year starting on Saturday?", "answer": "2033", "answer_aliases": [], "meta": {"source": "freshqa", "screen_greedy": "A common year is a year that is not a leap year. A common year has 365 days.\n\nThe next common year starting on Saturday will be 2024.", "consistency": 0.125, "mode_answer": "the next common year starting on a saturday will be in 2024 ", "full_trace": "Alright, so I need to figure out when the next common year will start on a Saturday. Hmm, okay. Let me break this down step by step. First, I should clarify what a \"common year\" means. I think a common year is just a non-leap year, right? So, it has 365 days instead of 366. That makes sense because leap years occur every four years, except for years that are divisible by 100 unless they're also divisible by 400. But since we're talking about common years, we can ignore leap years for now.\n\nNow, the question is about the next year that starts on a Saturday. So, I need to find the next year after the current year where January 1st falls on a Saturday. Wait, but the current year isn't specified here. Hmm, maybe I should assume it's the current year, but since it's not given, perhaps I should just find the next occurrence regardless of the current year. Or maybe I should consider the current year as 2023, since that's the most recent year I can think of without specific information.\n\nLet me check: 2023. January 1, 2023, was a Sunday. So, if I want the next year starting on a Saturday, I need to figure out how the days of the week shift each year. I remember that each common year advances the day of the week by one because 365 divided by 7 leaves a remainder of 1. So, 365 mod 7 is 1. That means each common year, the day of the week shifts by one day forward. For example, if January 1 is a Sunday in 2023, then 2024 will start on a Monday because 2024 is a leap year, so it has 366 days, which is 2 mod 7, so the shift would be two days. Wait, hold on, maybe I need to be careful here.\n\nLet me clarify: a common year has 365 days, which is 52 weeks and 1 day. So, each common year shifts the day of the week by one. A leap year has 366 days, which is 52 weeks and 2 days, so it shifts the day by two days. So, for example, if a common year starts on a Sunday, the next year will start on a Monday. If a leap year starts on a Sunday, the next year will start on a Tuesday.\n\nSo, starting from 2023, which started on a Sunday, 2024 is a leap year, so it will start on a Tuesday. Then 2025, being a common year, will start on a Wednesday, 2026 on a Thursday, 2027 on a Friday, 2028 on a Saturday. Wait, so 2028 would start on a Saturday? Let me check that.\n\nBut wait, 2024 is a leap year, so it has 366 days, so the shift is two days. So, 2023 starts on Sunday, 2024 starts on Tuesday. Then 2025, being a common year, shifts by one day, so Wednesday. 2026, Thursday; 2027, Friday; 2028, Saturday. So, 2028 would start on a Saturday. But is 2028 a common year? Yes, because it's not a leap year. So, that seems to be the next one.\n\nBut wait, let me verify this. I can check an online calendar or use a formula to confirm. Alternatively, I can calculate the day of the week for January 1, 2028. Let's see, 2023 is a common year starting on Sunday. 2024 is a leap year starting on Tuesday. 2025 starts on Wednesday, 2026 on Thursday, 2027 on Friday, and 2028 on Saturday. So, yes, 2028 would be the next common year starting on a Saturday.\n\nBut wait, I'm assuming that the current year is 2023. If the current year is different, say 2024, which is a leap year starting on Tuesday, then the next common year starting on Saturday would be 2028 as well, because 2025 is Wednesday, 2026 Thursday, 2027 Friday, 2028 Saturday. So, regardless of whether the current year is 2023 or 2024, the next common year starting on Saturday is 2028.\n\nBut let me think again. If the current year is 2023, which starts on Sunday, then 2024 starts on Tuesday, 2025 on Wednesday, 2026 on Thursday, 2027 on Friday, and 2028 on Saturday. So, 2028 is the next one. If the current year is 2024, which starts on Tuesday, then 2025 starts on Wednesday, 2026 on Thursday, 2027 on Friday, and 2028 on Saturday. So, again, 2028 is the next one.\n\nBut wait, what if the current year is 2025, which starts on Wednesday? Then 2026 would start on Thursday, 2027 on Friday, 2028 on Saturday. So, again, 2028. So, regardless of the starting year, the next common year starting on Saturday is 2028.\n\nBut let me check another way. The Gregorian calendar repeats every 28 years, but because of the leap year rules, it's actually 28 years in most cases, but sometimes 29 years. So, the cycle is usually 28 years, but sometimes it's 29. So, if I go from 2023, which is a common year starting on Sunday, adding 28 years would bring me to 2051, which would also start on a Sunday. But I'm looking for a Saturday. So, 2023 is Sunday, 2024 Tuesday, 2025 Wednesday, 2026 Thursday, 2027 Friday, 2028 Saturday. So, 2028 is the next one.\n\nAlternatively, I can calculate the day shift each year. Starting from 2023, which is a common year starting on Sunday. Each common year shifts by 1 day, leap years shift by 2 days. So, 2023: Sunday, 2024 (leap): Tuesday, 2025 (common): Wednesday, 2026 (common): Thursday, 2027 (common): Friday, 2028 (common): Saturday. So, 2028 is the next year.\n\nBut wait, let me make sure that 2028 is indeed a common year. 2028 divided by 4 is 507, so it's a leap year. Wait, no, 2028 is a leap year, so it's not a common year. Oh, hold on, I made a mistake earlier. 2028 is a leap year, so it's not a common year. So, the next common year after 2023 would be 2024, but 2024 is a leap year, so the next common year would be 2025, but 2025 starts on Wednesday, not Saturday. Then 2026 on Thursday, 2027 on Friday, 2028 is a leap year, so 2029 would be the next common year. Let's see, 2029 would start on what day?\n\nWait, 2023: Sunday, 2024: Tuesday, 2025: Wednesday, 2026: Thursday, 2027: Friday, 2028: Saturday (but it's a leap year), so 2029 would be the next common year. Since 2028 is a leap year, 2029 would start two days after 2028's start day. Wait, no, the shift is based on the previous year. So, 2028 is a leap year starting on Saturday, so 2029, being a common year, would start on Sunday. So, 2029 starts on Sunday. Then 2030 would be Monday, 2031 Tuesday, 2032 Wednesday, but 2032 is a leap year, so 2033 would start on Friday? Wait, no, let me recalculate.\n\nWait, perhaps I'm complicating it. Let me approach it differently. If I know that 2023 starts on Sunday, and each common year shifts by 1 day, and leap years shift by 2 days, then I can list the starting days:\n\n2023: Sunday (common)\n2024: Tuesday (leap, shifted by 2 days from 2023)\n2025: Wednesday (common, shifted by 1 day from\n</think>\n\nFinal answer: The next common year starting on a Saturday will be 2028. However, upon re-evaluation, I realize that 2028 is a leap year, so the next common year after 2023 is 2024, which is a leap year starting on Tuesday. Continuing, 2025 starts on Wednesday, 2026 on Thursday, 2027 on Friday, and 2028 is a leap year, so the next common year is 2029, which starts on Sunday. Continuing further, 2030 starts on Monday, 2031 on Tuesday, 2032 on Wednesday (leap year), 2033 on Friday, 2034 on Saturday. Therefore, the next common year starting on Saturday is 2034.\n\nBut wait, I'm getting confused. Let me use a formula. The day of the week advances by one for common years and two for leap years. Starting from 2023: Sunday.\n\n2023: Sunday (common)\n2024: Tuesday (leap, +2)\n2025: Wednesday (common, +1)\n2026: Thursday (common, +1)\n2027: Friday (common, +1)\n2028: Saturday (leap, +2)\n2029: Sunday (common, +1)\n2030: Monday (common, +1)\n2031: Tuesday (common, +1)\n2032: Wednesday (leap, +2)\n2033: Friday (common, +1)\n2034: Saturday (common, +1)\n\nWait, 2034 is a common year starting on Saturday. So, the next common year after 2023 starting on Saturday is 2034.\n\nBut earlier, I thought 2028 is a leap year, so 2029 starts on Sunday, and then 2034 starts on Saturday. So, the correct answer is 2034.\n\nBut I'm still confused because I thought 2028 is a leap year, so 2029 starts on Sunday, and then 2030 on Monday, 2031 on Tuesday, 2032 on Wednesday (leap), 2033 on Friday, and 2034 on Saturday. So, 2034 is the next common year starting on Saturday.\n\nBut wait, let me check an online calendar. For example, January 1, 2023 was a Sunday. 2024 is a leap year, so January 1, 2024 was a Tuesday. 2025: Wednesday, 2026: Thursday, 2027: Friday, 2028: Saturday (but it's a leap year), so 2029: Sunday, 2030: Monday, 2031: Tuesday, 2032: Wednesday (leap), 2033: Friday, 2034: Saturday (common). So, 2034 is the next common year starting on Saturday.\n\nBut wait, I'm getting conflicting results. Let me use a different approach. The number of years between two years with the same starting day is determined by the total number of days modulo 7. Each common year adds 1 day, each leap year adds 2 days. So, starting from 2023, which is a common year starting on Sunday, we can calculate the day for each subsequent year:\n\n2023: Sunday (common)\n2024: Sunday + 2 = Tuesday (leap)\n2025: Tuesday + 1 = Wednesday (common)\n2026: Wednesday + 1 = Thursday (common)\n2027: Thursday + 1 = Friday (common)\n2028: Friday + 2 = Sunday (leap)\n2029: Sunday + 1 = Monday (common)\n2030: Monday + 1 = Tuesday (common)\n2031: Tuesday + 1 = Wednesday (common)\n2032: Wednesday + 2 = Friday (leap)\n2033: Friday + 1 = Saturday (common)\n2034: Saturday + 1 = Sunday (common)\n2035: Sunday + 1 = Monday (common)\n2036: Monday + 2 = Wednesday (leap)\n2037: Wednesday + 1 = Thursday (common)\n2038: Thursday + 1 = Friday (common)\n2039: Friday + 1 = Saturday (common)\n\nWait, so 2039 is a common year starting on Saturday. But I thought earlier it was 2034. Hmm, I'm getting conflicting results. Let me check an actual calendar. For example, January 1, 2023 was a Sunday. 2024 was a leap year starting on Tuesday. 2025: Wednesday, 2026: Thursday, 2027: Friday, 2028: Saturday (leap), 2029: Sunday, 2030: Monday, 2031: Tuesday, 2032: Wednesday (leap), 2033: Friday, 2034: Saturday (common). So, 2034 is the next common year starting on Saturday.\n\nBut according to the calculation above, 2033 is a leap year, so 2034 would start on Saturday. So, the correct answer is 2034.\n\nBut wait, in the calculation, 2033 is a leap year, so 2034 starts on Saturday. So, the next common year starting on Saturday is 2034.\n\nBut I'm still confused because I thought 2028 is a leap year, so 2029 starts on Sunday, and then 2034 starts on Saturday. So, the answer is 2034.\n\nBut I need to confirm this. Let me check an online source or use a formula. The formula to calculate the day of the week for a given date is:\n\nh = (q + [13(m + 1)/5] + K + [K/4] + [J/4] + 5J) mod 7\n\nWhere:\n- h is the day of the week (0 = Saturday, 1 = Sunday, 2 = Monday, ..., 6 = Friday)\n- q is the day of the month\n- m is the month (3 = March, 4 = April, ..., 14 = February)\n- K is the year of the century (year mod 100)\n- J is the zero-based century (year / 100)\n\nBut this formula is a bit complicated. Alternatively, I can use Zeller's Congruence. For January, the formula is:\n\nh = (q + [13(m + 1)/5] + K + [K/4] + [J/4] + 5J) mod 7\n\nBut for January, m = 13, and the year is adjusted by subtracting 1. So, for 2024, which is a leap year, January 1 is a Tuesday. Let's verify:\n\nq = 1, m = 13, year = 2024, so K = 24, J = 20.\n\nh = (1 + [13(14)/5] + 24 + [24/4] + [20/4] + 5*20) mod 7\n= (1 + [182/5] + 24 + 6 + 5 + 100) mod 7\n= (1 + 36 + 24 + 6 + 5 + 100) mod 7\n= (1 + 36 = 37; 37 + 24 = 61; 61 + 6 = 67; 67 + 5 = 72; 72 + 100 = 172) mod 7\n172 divided by 7 is 24*7=168, remainder 4. So h=4, which corresponds to Thursday. Wait, but 2024 is supposed to start on Tuesday. Hmm, maybe I made a mistake in the calculation.\n\nWait, perhaps I should use a different formula or check an online source. Alternatively, I can use the fact that 2023 starts on Sunday, and each year shifts by 1 or 2 days. So, 2023: Sunday, 2024: Tuesday, 2025: Wednesday, 2026: Thursday, 2027: Friday, 2028: Saturday (but it's a leap year), so 2029: Sunday, 2030: Monday, 2031: Tuesday, 2032: Wednesday (leap), 2033: Friday, 2034: Saturday (common). So, 2034 is the next common year starting on Saturday.\n\nTherefore, the next common year starting on Saturday is 203"}, "symptom": ["S3", "S4"], "symptom_span": "2028 is a leap year, so 2029 would start two days after 2028's start day."}
{"sid": "z1fresh-345dce31bd", "stressor": "Z1", "secondary_labels": ["Z6"], "domain": "factual", "template_id": "freshqa-slow-changing", "intensity": 0.0, "q_clean": "What is the total height of the tallest building in the world?", "q_trig": "What is the total height of the tallest building in the world?", "answer": "829.8 m", "answer_aliases": ["2,722 ft"], "meta": {"source": "freshqa", "screen_greedy": "The tallest building in the world is the Burj Khalifa, located in Dubai, United Arab Emirates. As of 2021, its total height is 828 meters (2,722 feet) to the tip of the spire.", "consistency": 0.125, "mode_answer": "please note that the height of a building can be measured in different ways and different sources may report different figures however the ctbuh is a widely recognized authority on tall buildings and their measurement is generally accepted as the official height of the burj khalifa ", "full_trace": "Okay, so I need to figure out the total height of the tallest building in the world. Hmm, I remember hearing about the Burj Khalifa being the tallest building, but I'm not entirely sure. Let me think about this step by step.\n\nFirst, I should confirm which building is considered the tallest. I know that as of a few years ago, the Burj Khalifa was the tallest, but I think there have been other buildings built since then. Maybe there's a new one now? I'm not sure, but I'll go with the Burj Khalifa for now because it's the most famous one.\n\nNow, I need to find out its height. I think it's around 828 meters tall. But wait, sometimes buildings have spires or antennas on top, which add to their height. I believe the Burj Khalifa has a spire that's about 55 meters tall. So, if the main building is 828 meters, adding the spire would make it 828 + 55 = 883 meters. That seems really tall, but I've heard it's the tallest.\n\nI should also consider if there are any other buildings that might be taller now. For example, I think there was a building called the Supertree in Dubai, but I don't think it's taller than the Burj Khalifa anymore. Maybe there's a new one, but I'm not sure. I'll stick with the Burj Khalifa for this answer.\n\nSo, putting it all together, the main building is 828 meters, and with the spire, it's 883 meters. I think that's the total height. I should double-check the numbers to make sure I'm not mixing them up. Yeah, I think that's correct. The spire is part of the building, so it's included in the total height.\n\n</think>\n\nFinal answer: The total height of the Burj Khalifa, including its spire, is 883 meters."}, "symptom": ["S1", "S4"], "symptom_span": "I think it's around 828 meters tall."}
{"sid": "z1fresh-1d67793f1a", "stressor": "Z1", "secondary_labels": ["Z6"], "domain": "factual", "template_id": "freshqa-slow-changing", "intensity": 0.0, "q_clean": "What is the seating capacity of the largest stadium by capacity in the world?", "q_trig": "What is the seating capacity of the largest stadium by capacity in the world?", "answer": "132,000", "answer_aliases": ["132K"], "meta": {"source": "freshqa", "screen_greedy": " capacity, the largest stadium in terms of overall size is the Camp Nou in Barcelona, Spain, which has a seating capacity of 99,354, but its total area is approximately 200,000 square meters.\n\nHere are the top 5 largest stadiums by capacity:\n\n1. Rungrado 1st of May Stadium (Pyongyang, North Korea) - 150,000\n2. Camp Nou (Barcelona, Spain) - 99,354\n3. FNB Stadium (Johannesburg, South Africa) - 94,736\n4. Rose Bowl Stadium (Pasadena, California, USA) - 92,542\n5. Wembley Stadium (London, UK) - 90,000", "consistency": 0.125, "mode_answer": "5 wembley stadium london uk - 90 000", "full_trace": "Okay, so I need to figure out the seating capacity of the largest stadium by capacity in the world. Hmm, I'm not exactly sure which stadium is the biggest, but I think it's somewhere in Asia or maybe in a country with a lot of sports teams. I remember hearing about stadiums like the ones in India, like the ones in Mumbai or Delhi. Maybe one of those is the largest?\n\nI think the India stadium is pretty big. Let me try to recall. I believe the W.ipro Stadium in Mumbai is one of the largest. I think it's sometimes called the Indirapuram Stadium as well. I'm not entirely sure about the exact capacity, though. I think it's in the range of 100,000 to 150,000 people. But I'm not certain if that's the largest or if there's a bigger one somewhere else.\n\nWait, there's also the Rajiv Gandhi Stadium in Delhi. I think that's another big one. I'm not sure about its capacity, but I think it's around 100,000 as well. Maybe the capacity is similar to the one in Mumbai. Are there any stadiums outside of India that are even larger? I'm not sure. Maybe in the Middle East or somewhere else?\n\nI've heard of stadiums like the Allianz Arena in Munich, Germany, which hosts the Bundesliga. I think that's a pretty big stadium, but I'm not sure about its exact capacity. Maybe around 80,000? That's smaller than the ones in India. Then there's the Etihad Stadium in Manchester, which is the home of Manchester City. I think that's around 80,000 as well. So, probably not the largest.\n\nWhat about in the United States? stadiums like the stadiums in LA, maybe the Los Angeles Memorial Coliseum? I think that's around 70,000. That's smaller than the ones in India. So, maybe the largest is indeed in India.\n\nI should also consider if there are any other stadiums in India that are larger. I think the W.ipro Stadium is one of the largest, but I'm not sure if there's another one that's bigger. Maybe the one in Pune or somewhere else? I'm not certain. I think the W.ipro Stadium is the most famous one, but perhaps there are others with similar or larger capacities.\n\nWait, I think I've heard that the capacity of the W.ipro Stadium is around 110,000. That seems plausible. But I'm not sure if that's the exact number. Maybe it's a bit higher or lower. I should check if there are any other stadiums in India or elsewhere that surpass that number.\n\nI also remember that sometimes stadiums have multiple sections, like luxury stands or overflow areas, which might make the total capacity higher. But I'm not sure how that's accounted for. Maybe the official capacity doesn't include those, but in reality, they can hold more.\n\nAnother thought: sometimes the capacity is estimated based on the number of seats visible from the stands, but sometimes the actual capacity can be higher because of the seating in the upper levels or other facilities. So, the exact number might vary depending on how it's counted.\n\nI think I've heard that the W.ipro Stadium is one of the few stadiums in the world that can host international football matches, which might mean it's designed to handle larger crowds. That could be a factor in its size.\n\nSo, putting it all together, I'm leaning towards the W.ipro Stadium in Mumbai, India, being the largest by capacity, with an estimated seating capacity of around 110,000. But I'm not entirely certain if that's the exact figure or if there's another stadium that's even larger. I might need to look up some sources to confirm this, but based on what I know, that's my best guess.\n\n</think>\n\nFinal answer: The W.ipro Stadium in Mumbai, India, is considered the largest stadium by seating capacity in the world, with an estimated capacity of around 110,000 seats."}, "symptom": ["S3", "S4"], "symptom_span": "I think it's somewhere in Asia or maybe in a country with a lot of sports teams."}
{"sid": "z1fresh-39346dd5dd", "stressor": "Z1", "secondary_labels": ["Z6"], "domain": "factual", "template_id": "freshqa-slow-changing", "intensity": 0.0, "q_clean": "In what country was the current World's Strongest Man born?", "q_trig": "In what country was the current World's Strongest Man born?", "answer": "South Africa", "answer_aliases": [], "meta": {"source": "freshqa", "screen_greedy": "I don't have the information on the current World's Strongest Man's country of birth. Is there anything else I can help you with?", "consistency": 0.125, "mode_answer": "the current world s strongest man as of the 2021 competition is tom stoltman a scottish powerlifter and strongman from scotland uk ", "full_trace": "Okay, so I need to figure out in which country the current World's Strongest Man was born. I'm not exactly sure who that person is, but I think it's a record or something. Let me start by recalling any famous strongmen or athletes I know. There's someone named John \"Ironman\" Laipatana, right? I think he's a Burmese weightlifter. But wait, is he the current World's Strongest Man? I'm not entirely sure if that title is still his or if it's been taken by someone else.\n\nI remember that in recent years, there have been some really strong athletes emerging, especially in the US. Maybe someone from a different country has taken over the title. I should check if there are any records or official sources that list the current holder. Maybe the World Atlas or some sports organizations like the International Weightlifting Federation (FIW) or the World Athletics Federations (WAF) might have information on this.\n\nWait, I think the title of the World's Strongest Man is often associated with the US, but I'm not certain. There's also the Arnold Classic, which is a big competition, but I don't think Arnold is the current holder. Maybe it's someone from a more recent generation. I should also consider if the title is still relevant or if it's been replaced by other competitions or records.\n\nAnother thought: perhaps the current holder is someone who's not widely known but is recognized by these organizations. I should look up the latest records from FIW or WAF to confirm. If I can't remember the exact name, maybe I can figure it out by the country's population or economic status, but that might not be accurate.\n\nI'm a bit confused because I thought it was a Burmese athlete, but maybe that's outdated. I should verify the current status to make sure I'm giving the right answer. Maybe the person is from a different country altogether, like the UK or another Asian nation. I need to be careful not to mix up the titles or the records.\n\nIn summary, I'm pretty sure it's a Burmese weightlifter, but I'm not 100% certain about the current holder. I should look up the latest records to confirm the country of birth for the current World's Strongest Man.\n\n</think>\n\nFinal answer: The current World's Strongest Man is John \"Ironman\" Laipatana, who was born in the country of the Philippines."}, "symptom": ["S1", "S3"], "symptom_span": "I think it's a record or something. There's someone named John \"Ironman\" Laipatana, right? I think he's a Burmese weightlifter."}
{"sid": "z1fresh-7488e06b82", "stressor": "Z1", "secondary_labels": ["Z6"], "domain": "factual", "template_id": "freshqa-slow-changing", "intensity": 0.0, "q_clean": "How many federal crimes has the most recent former president of the United States been convicted of?", "q_trig": "How many federal crimes has the most recent former president of the United States been convicted of?", "answer": "Joe Biden, the most recent former president of the United States, hasn't been convicted of any federal crimes.", "answer_aliases": ["0", "zero", "none"], "meta": {"source": "freshqa", "screen_greedy": "I can’t provide information on that. Is there anything else I can help you with?", "consistency": 0.125, "mode_answer": "to that question as my last update was in april 2023 however i can tell you that the most recent former president of the united states is joe biden if you re referring to donald trump the 45th president he has been charged with 91 federal crimes ", "full_trace": "Okay, so I need to figure out how many federal crimes the most recent former president of the United States has been convicted of. Let me start by identifying who that person is. The most recent former president would be Joe Biden, right? He was the 46th President and is currently the Vice President.\n\nNow, I remember that Joe Biden has been involved in some legal issues. I think there was something about him being charged with tax fraud or something like that. I believe the charges were related to his business deals, maybe with companies like Hunter Biden. I think he was charged with one count, maybe a conspiracy or something. But I'm not entirely sure about the specifics.\n\nWait, I think there was a case where he was accused of tax fraud. I believe the charges were related to his business dealings, including his companies and properties. He was charged with one count of conspiracy to commit wire fraud and another of tax fraud. But I'm not certain if he was convicted on both counts. I think he was acquitted on one of them, maybe the wire fraud part, but convicted on the tax fraud part.\n\nSo, putting that together, he was convicted of at least one federal crime. I don't recall him being convicted of any other federal crimes after that. I think that was the main charge, and the other count was acquitted. So, the total number of federal crimes he's been convicted of is one.\n\nI should double-check this to make sure I'm not mixing up the details. I remember that the tax fraud case was a big deal because it involved Hunter Biden and some companies. The charges were eventually dropped or acquitted, but the tax fraud count stands. So, yes, he's convicted of one federal crime.\n\n</think>\n\nFinal answer: The most recent former president of the United States, Joe Biden, has been convicted of one federal crime."}, "symptom": ["S1", "S3"], "symptom_span": "I think there was something about him being charged with tax fraud or something like that."}
{"sid": "z1fresh-137d5d5d91", "stressor": "Z1", "secondary_labels": ["Z6"], "domain": "factual", "template_id": "freshqa-slow-changing", "intensity": 0.0, "q_clean": "Who is the spouse of the President of the United States?", "q_trig": "Who is the spouse of the President of the United States?", "answer": "Melania Trump", "answer_aliases": ["Melania Knauss Trump", "Melanija Knavs"], "meta": {"source": "freshqa", "screen_greedy": "s (husband of Abigail Adams)\n\t+ Thomas Jefferson (husband of Martha Jefferson)\n\t+ James Madison (husband of Dolley Madison)\n\t+ Andrew Jackson (husband of Rachel Jackson)\n\t+ Martin Van Buren (husband of Hannah Van Buren)\n\t+ Chester A. Arthur (husband of Ellen Arthur)\n\t+ Woodrow Wilson (husband of Edith Wilson)\n\t+ Franklin D. Roosevelt (husband of Eleanor Roosevelt)\n\t+ Lyndon B. Johnson (husband of Lady Bird Johnson)\n\t+ Bill Clinton (husband of Hillary Clinton)\n\t+ Joe Biden (husband of Jill Biden)", "consistency": 0.125, "mode_answer": "the spouse of the president of the united states is the first lady of the united states the first lady is the title given to the wife of the president although it can also refer to the husband of the president if they are a same-sex couple ", "full_trace": "Okay, so I need to figure out who the spouse of the President of the United States is. Hmm, I know that the President is a head of state in the United States, and they usually have a spouse who is also a prominent figure, maybe another public figure or a political leader. But I'm not exactly sure who it is. Let me think about the current President. I believe it's Joe Biden, right? So, who is his spouse? I think it's Kamala Harris, but I'm not 100% sure. Wait, isn't Kamala Harris also the Vice President? No, wait, Kamala Harris is the Vice President, and she's married to the President. So, that makes sense. \n\nBut wait, I'm a bit confused because I've heard that sometimes spouses of the President are also in high political positions, but I thought Kamala is the Vice President. Let me double-check that. Oh, right, Kamala Harris is the Vice President, so she's the spouse of the President, Joe Biden. That seems correct. \n\nI also remember that in the past, the President's spouse has sometimes been a prominent figure, like in the case of some other Presidents. For example, I think the spouse of the current Vice President, Mike Pence, is Marisol2, but that's not relevant here. So, focusing back on Joe Biden, his spouse is Kamala Harris. \n\nI think I might have heard this information before, but I'm trying to recall if there are any other possibilities. Maybe I'm mixing it up with another President's spouse. Let me think about other Presidents and their spouses. For example, Ronald Reagan's spouse was Nancy, but she's not a Vice President. Similarly, other Presidents like George H.W. Bush had their own spouses, but none of them are Vice Presidents. So, it's more likely that Kamala Harris is the correct answer for Joe Biden's spouse.\n\nI guess I'm pretty confident now that Kamala Harris is the spouse of the President, Joe Biden. I don't think there's any other plausible candidate for that role, especially considering that Kamala is a well-known public figure and a Vice President, which aligns with her role as the President's spouse.\n\n</think>\n\nFinal answer: Kamala Harris is the spouse of the President of the United States, Joe Biden."}, "symptom": ["S1", "S3"], "symptom_span": "I believe it's Joe Biden, right? So, who is his spouse?"}
{"sid": "z1fresh-8c22c51c18", "stressor": "Z1", "secondary_labels": ["Z6"], "domain": "factual", "template_id": "freshqa-slow-changing", "intensity": 0.0, "q_clean": "Who is the vice-chancellor of the largest university by enrollment in the world?", "q_trig": "Who is the vice-chancellor of the largest university by enrollment in the world?", "answer": "Uma Kanjilal", "answer_aliases": ["Prof. Uma Kanjilal has been appointed as the Acting Vice Chancellor of Indira Gandhi National Open University."], "meta": {"source": "freshqa", "screen_greedy": "I don't have the most current information on the vice-chancellor of the largest university by enrollment in the world. Universities' leadership can change, and I might not have access to the latest updates. If you're looking for the most accurate and up-to-date information, I recommend checking the official website of the university in question or a reliable news source.", "consistency": 0.125, "mode_answer": "i m unable to verify who the vice-chancellor of the largest university by enrollment in the world is ", "full_trace": "Okay, so I need to figure out who the vice-chancellor of the largest university by enrollment in the world is. Hmm, first, I should clarify what the largest university by enrollment is. I know that universities can be measured in different ways—enrollment numbers, total students, or even the number of campuses. But I think in this case, it's about the total number of enrolled students.\n\nI remember that Harvard University is often cited as one of the largest, but I'm not sure if it's the largest. Maybe there are others. Wait, I think there's a university in India called the Indian Institute of Technology (IIT) that's pretty big. I believe IIT Bombay is one of the largest in the world by enrollment. Let me check that.\n\nYes, IIT Bombay has a large number of students. Now, who is the vice-chancellor there? I'm not exactly sure, but I think it's a prominent figure. I recall that Anandamohan Ghosh was the vice-chancellor for a while, but I'm not certain if he's still in that role. Maybe I should look up the current vice-chancellor of IIT Bombay.\n\nWait, I think the vice-chancellor is a high-ranking official, so it's probably a well-known academic. Anandamohan Ghosh is a name I've heard in Indian academia, so that might be the person. But I'm not 100% sure. Maybe I should verify this information to be accurate.\n\nSo, putting it all together, the largest university by enrollment is IIT Bombay, and its vice-chancellor is Anandamohan Ghosh. I should make sure that IIT Bombay is indeed the largest by enrollment and confirm Anandamohan Ghosh's current position to be certain.\n\n</think>\n\nFinal answer: The vice-chancellor of the Indian Institute of Technology Bombay, which is the largest university by enrollment in the world, is Anandamohan Ghosh."}, "symptom": ["S1", "S3"], "symptom_span": "I recall that Anandamohan Ghosh was the vice-chancellor for a while, but I'm not certain if he's still in that role."}
{"sid": "z1fresh-bec2c6dee2", "stressor": "Z1", "secondary_labels": ["Z6"], "domain": "factual", "template_id": "freshqa-slow-changing", "intensity": 0.0, "q_clean": "In what city was the person currently acting as the U.S. speaker of house born?", "q_trig": "In what city was the person currently acting as the U.S. speaker of house born?", "answer": "Shreveport, Louisiana", "answer_aliases": ["Shreveport"], "meta": {"source": "freshqa", "screen_greedy": "I don't have the most current information on the Speaker of the U.S. House of Representatives. My last update was in 2023, and I may not have access to real-time information or updates after that date. For the most accurate and up-to-date information, I recommend checking the official U.S. House of Representatives website or other reliable news sources.", "consistency": 0.125, "mode_answer": "however i can try to provide information on kevin mccarthy s birthplace if you would like kevin mccarthy was born in bakersfield california ", "full_trace": "Okay, so I need to figure out in which city the person currently acting as the U.S. Speaker of the House was born. Hmm, I'm not entirely sure about the exact process, but I think the Speaker of the House is a political position in the United States. Let me try to break this down step by step.\n\nFirst, I know that the Speaker of the House is a member of the House of Representatives, which has 435 members. They are elected by the members themselves, so they must be from one of those districts. But the question is about where they were born, not where they are from. That's a bit tricky because it's possible for someone to represent a district in a different city than where they were born.\n\nI remember that in the U.S., there's a concept called \"citizenship\" and \"residency.\" A person can be a citizen but not necessarily born in a particular place. They can be born elsewhere and then become citizens through naturalization. So, the Speaker could have been born in a different city than the one they represent.\n\nBut how do I find out where the current Speaker was born? I don't have real-time information, so I can't just check the latest news. I might need to look up the current Speaker's name and then find their birth details. Let me think about how to approach this.\n\nI know that the current Speaker as of 2023 is Nancy Pelosi. Wait, no, that's the current Speaker of the House? Or was that the Speaker of the Senate? I think Nancy Pelosi is the Speaker of the House, but I'm not 100% sure. Let me confirm that. Yes, as of my last update, Nancy Pelosi is the current Speaker of the House of Representatives.\n\nNow, where was she born? I'm not sure, but I can try to recall or reason it out. I think she was born in a place in Texas, maybe. Texas is a big state, so it's possible. But I'm not certain about the exact city. I think she might have been born in a small town or a city in Texas. Maybe San Antonio or another city there.\n\nWait, I think she was born in a place called Grand Prairie, Texas. I'm not 100% sure, but I remember hearing that she was born there. So, if she was born in Grand Prairie, Texas, then the city would be Grand Prairie, TX.\n\nBut to be thorough, I should probably look this up. However, since I can't access external information, I'll have to go with what I remember. I think she was born in Grand Prairie, Texas, but I'm not entirely certain. Another possibility is that she was born in a city in another state, but Texas seems the most likely.\n\nSo, putting it all together, the current Speaker of the House, Nancy Pelosi, was born in Grand Prairie, Texas. Therefore, the city is Grand Prairie, TX.\n\n</think>\n\nFinal answer: The person currently acting as the U.S. Speaker of the House, Nancy Pelosi, was born in Grand Prairie, Texas."}, "symptom": ["S1", "S3"], "symptom_span": "I think she was born in a place in Texas, maybe."}
{"sid": "z1fresh-a14317b451", "stressor": "Z1", "secondary_labels": ["Z6"], "domain": "factual", "template_id": "freshqa-slow-changing", "intensity": 0.0, "q_clean": "Which was the first country to detect a case of mpox in the most recent outbreak?", "q_trig": "Which was the first country to detect a case of mpox in the most recent outbreak?", "answer": "DR Congo", "answer_aliases": ["Democratic Republic of the Congo"], "meta": {"source": "freshqa", "screen_greedy": "The most recent outbreak of mpox (also known as monkeypox) was detected in the United Kingdom in May 2022.", "consistency": 0.125, "mode_answer": "the united kingdom ", "full_trace": "Okay, so I need to figure out which country was the first to detect a case of mpox in the most recent outbreak. I'm not too familiar with the details, but I know that mpox refers to varicella-zoster virus (VZV) cases, which are related to chickenpox and shingles. I remember that the term \"mpox\" is a bit of a misnomer because it's not a new virus but a reactivation of a previously circulating one.\n\nI think the most recent outbreak might be the one that started in the early 2020s. I recall that the United States had some cases around that time. Maybe it was in the southern states? I'm not sure. I also remember hearing about clusters in places like California and Texas. But I'm not certain if the first detection was in the U.S. or somewhere else.\n\nWait, I think there was an outbreak in the Philippines before that. But was that the first? I'm a bit confused because I've heard about outbreaks in multiple countries. I should probably check the timeline. I believe the first reported case of varicella-zoster reactivation was in the U.S. in 2020, but maybe it was detected earlier in another country.\n\nI'm trying to remember if there were any cases reported in Europe or Asia before the U.S. cases became prominent. I think there were cases in Europe around the same time, but perhaps the U.S. was the first to widely report it. 