that's not Asia. The 2010 was in the UK, so that's Europe. The 2014 was in the US, and 2018 in Brazil. \n\nI'm trying to recall if there was an Asian event in the 1990s or early 2000s. I think the 2002 event was in Germany, so that's Europe. Maybe the 2006 was in Italy, which is Europe too. The 2010 was in the UK, also Europe. Then the 2014 was in the US, and 2018 in Brazil. So, up to 2018, no Asian events. \n\nI'm trying to think if there was any in the 2000s. Maybe the 2006 was in Italy, so that's not Asia. The 2010 was in the UK, so that's Europe. The 2014 was in the US, and 2018 in Brazil. So, no Asian events in those years. \n\nWait, maybe the 2002 event was in Germany, so that's Europe. The 2006 was in Italy, also Europe. The 2010 was in the UK, Europe. The 2014 was in the US, and 2018 in Brazil. So, no Asian events in the World Championships up to 2018. \n\nI think the next one would be 2022, but I don't know where that is yet. Maybe in the US or somewhere else. So, up to now, I don't think any World Championships have been held in Asia. \n\nWait, but I'm not 100% sure. Maybe I should check some sources or think about any official announcements. I don't recall any official announcements about an Asian World Championship yet. So, it seems like the answer is that the World Championships haven't been held in Asia yet. \n\nSo, to sum up, from 1996 up to 2018, the World Championships were held in Europe (Germany, Italy, UK), North America (US), and South America (Brazil). No Asian events. The next one, if it happens, might be in 2022, but it's not yet confirmed where. So, the number of times held in Asia is zero.\n\n</think>\n\nFinal answer: The Pokémon World Championships have not been held in Asia yet. Up to the 2018 event, they were hosted in Europe (Germany, Italy, UK), North America (US), and South America (Brazil). The next event, if any, is yet to be confirmed, but no Asian championships have occurred. Therefore, the number of times the World Championships 