ore confused. Maybe I should think about the current year, 2023. If 50 Cent was number one in 2019, he might still be there, but I'm not certain. Alternatively, maybe it's someone else like Billie Eilish, but she's not likely to be number one yet.\n\nI think I'll go with 50 Cent as the current number one on the Billboard Artist 100, based on my memory of him being there around 2018-2019. But I'm not entirely sure if he's still at the top.\n\n</think>\n\nFinal answer: The current number one on the Billboard Artist 100 is 50 Cent."}, "symptom": ["S1", "S3"], "symptom_span": "I think the current top artist is someone like 50 Cent."}
{"sid": "z1fresh-ed087f4dde", "stressor": "Z1", "secondary_labels": ["Z6"], "domain": "factual", "template_id": "freshqa-fast-changing", "intensity": 0.0, "q_clean": "What's the most popular film on Letterboxd this week?", "q_trig": "What's the most popular film on Letterboxd this week?", "answer": "The Drama", "answer_aliases": ["The Drama (2026) directed by Kristoffer Borgli"], "meta": {"source": "freshqa", "screen_greedy": "often discuss the latest releases and popular films on Letterboxd. You can check these communities to see what's currently trending.\n4. **Search online**: You can try searching for \"most popular film on Letterboxd this week\" or \"current top-rated films on Letterboxd\" to find relevant articles or blog posts that may have the information you're looking for.\n\nKeep in mind that the popularity of films on Letterboxd can change rapidly, so the most popular film this week may not be the same next week.", "consistency": 0.125, "mode_answer": "keep in mind that the most popular films on letterboxd can change rapidly so the information may not be up to the minute i hope this helps and happy film exploration ", "full_trace": "Okay, so I need to figure out what the most popular film on Letterboxd is this week. I'm not exactly sure how Letterboxd works, but I know it's a platform for watching movies. Maybe it's similar to other sites like IMDb or IMDb Top Rated. But I'm not certain. \n\nFirst, I should probably check if there's a way to look up the most popular movies on Letterboxd. I don't know if they have a feature that ranks movies by popularity. Maybe they use something like views, ratings, or community votes? I'm not sure how they measure popularity. \n\nI remember that sometimes movies that are highly rated or have a lot of reviews can be considered popular. But I'm not sure if that's the same as being the most popular. Maybe there are other factors like how many people have added the movie to their top picks or lists. \n\nI wonder if there's a way to see a list of popular movies on Letterboxd. Perhaps they have a \"Popular\" or \"Trending\" section? I'm not sure. Maybe I can look up some recent movies and see how they rank. For example, movies like \"The Matrix,\" \"Inception,\" or \"Interstellar\" are usually popular, but I don't know if they're still popular this week. \n\nI should also consider that popularity can vary based on the region or audience. Maybe a movie that's popular in one country isn't as popular in another. But since the user didn't specify, I'll assume it's a global list. \n\nAnother thought: maybe the most popular movie this week is a recent release or a critically acclaimed film. Perhaps something like \"The Dark Knight\" or \"The Social Network.\" But I'm not sure if those are still on top. \n\nI could also think about awards. If a film has won recent awards, it might be more popular. But again, I'm not certain how Letterboxd measures this. \n\nWait, maybe I can look up some recent activity on Letterboxd. If I go to the website, I can check the trending or popular sections. But since I can't browse the internet, I have to rely on my existing knowledge. \n\nI think \"The Matrix 4\" came out recently, but I'm not sure if it's still popular. It might be, considering it's a sequel and often well-received. Alternatively, maybe \"The Grand Budapest Hotel\" is still popular, but I'm not sure. \n\nI should also consider that sometimes independent films or art movies can be popular, especially if they're critically acclaimed. For example, \"Whiplash\" or \"The Grand Budapest Hotel\" might be contenders. \n\nAnother angle: maybe the most popular film is one that's been on Letterboxd for a long time but still gets a lot of views or discussions. Perhaps a classic that's been viewed by many people. \n\nI'm also thinking about the time of year. Maybe certain movies become more popular around holidays or special events. For example, around Halloween or Christmas, certain horror or comedy movies might spike in popularity. \n\nBut without specific data, it's hard to say. I might have to make an educated guess based on what I know. I think \"The Dark Knight\" is still popular, but I'm not certain. Alternatively, maybe \"The Social Network\" is still a top contender. \n\nWait, I remember that \"The Matrix\" series is very popular on platforms like IMDb, but I'm not sure about Letterboxd. Maybe it's still up there. \n\nI'm also considering that sometimes the most popular movie can be something that's been out for a while but still gets a lot of people watching it. For example, \"The Godfather\" is a classic that might still be popular. \n\nBut I'm not sure. I think I need to make a decision here. Based on what I know, I'll say that \"The Dark Knight\" is likely the most popular film on Letterboxd this week, but I'm not 100% certain. Alternatively, it could be \"The Social Network.\" \n\nWait, another thought: maybe \"The Grand Budapest Hotel\" is still popular because it's visually stunning and well-received. It's a foreign film, so it might attract a different audience. \n\nI'm still not sure. I think I'll go with \"The Dark Knight\" as the most popular, but I'm not entirely confident. Maybe I should check if there's any recent news or articles about popular movies on Letterboxd, but since I can't do that, I'll have to rely on my current knowledge.\n\n</think>\n\nFinal answer: The most popular film on Letterboxd this week is likely \"The Dark Knight.\""}, "symptom": ["S3", "S4"], "symptom_span": "I'm not exactly sure how Letterboxd works, but I know it's a platform for watching movies."}
{"sid": "z1fresh-9237488cbd", "stressor": "Z1", "secondary_labels": ["Z6"], "domain": "factual", "template_id": "freshqa-fast-changing", "intensity": 0.0, "q_clean": "What is Geoff Hinton’s h-index?", "q_trig": "What is Geoff Hinton’s h-index?", "answer": "190", "answer_aliases": [], "meta": {"source": "freshqa", "screen_greedy": "I don’t have access to a search engine to verify Geoff Hinton’s h-index.", "consistency": 0.125, "mode_answer": "i don t have the most current information on geoff hinton s h-index h-indices can change over time and may not be up to date in my current data for the most accurate and recent information i recommend checking a reliable academic database or the official academic profile of geoff hinton ", "full_trace": "Okay, so I need to figure out what Geoff Hinton's h-index is. I'm not exactly sure what an h-index is, but I think it's a measure of a researcher's productivity and influence. Maybe it's something like how many papers they've published and how many citations those papers have gotten. \n\nI remember hearing that h-index is calculated by finding the highest number h where the researcher has h papers each cited at least h times. So, for example, if someone has an h-index of 50, that means they have 50 papers each cited at least 50 times. That makes sense because it balances the number of papers with the impact of each paper.\n\nNow, who is Geoff Hinton? I think he's a computer scientist, maybe a professor, and he's known for his work in machine learning and artificial intelligence. I recall he did some work on neural networks and deep learning, which are pretty hot topics right now. He's also been involved in some influential projects or maybe even textbooks in the field.\n\nI'm not sure about his exact h-index, but I think it's a relatively high number because he's a prominent figure in his field. Maybe I can look up his publications and see how many citations they've received. Alternatively, I could check some sources that list h-indexes of notable scientists. I think some universities or research institutions publish lists of faculty members with their h-indexes. \n\nWait, I also remember that h-index can vary depending on the database or source you use. For example, Google Scholar, Scopus, or Web of Science might have different numbers. So, I should probably check a reliable source that aggregates this information.\n\nI think I've heard that some top researchers have h-indexes in the hundreds. If Hinton is a leading figure in AI, maybe his h-index is in the 100s. But I'm not certain. I should try to find a source that specifically lists his h-index. Maybe his university's website or a recent publication might have that information.\n\nAlternatively, I could look up his publications on Google Scholar and count the number of citations each paper has, then determine the h-index from there. That might be a bit time-consuming, but it would give me an accurate number. I can start by searching for his name on Google Scholar and then look through the top papers to see their citation counts.\n\nAnother thought: I remember that h-index is updated regularly, so it's possible that the number has changed if he published new high-impact papers recently. But since he's been active for many years, his h-index is likely quite high.\n\nI should also consider that h-index isn't the only metric for evaluating a researcher's impact. It's more of a measure of productivity and influence, but it's still commonly used in academic evaluations. So, even if his h-index is high, it's important to look at other factors like peer reviews, awards, and recognitions as well.\n\nIn summary, to find Geoff Hinton's h-index, I need to:\n\n1. Understand what an h-index is.\n2. Recall that it's a measure of both the number of papers and their citations.\n3. Remember that Hinton is a prominent AI researcher.\n4. Look up his publications and find the h-index, possibly through Google Scholar or a database like Scopus.\n5. Consider that his h-index is likely in the higher range due to his prominence in the field.\n\nI think the best approach is to search for his name on Google Scholar and look for his h-index there. If I can't find it directly, maybe I can estimate based on the number of highly cited papers he has. For example, if he has 50 papers each cited 50 times, that would give him an h-index of 50. But given his influence, I suspect it's higher, maybe around 100 or more.\n\nWait, I think I've heard that some of his papers, like \"Deep Neural Networks for Acoustic Modeling in Speech Recognition,\" have been cited thousands of times. So, if he has several papers with very high citations, that would significantly boost his h-index. Maybe his h-index is in the 100s, but I'm not entirely sure. I should verify this by checking a reliable source or database.\n\nAfter doing a quick search, I found that Geoff Hinton's h-index is 158 as of 2023. That seems quite high, but considering his contributions and the impact of his work, it makes sense. So, his h-index reflects his significant contributions and influence in the field of machine learning and AI.\n\n</think>\n\nFinal answer: Geoff Hinton's h-index is 158."}, "symptom": ["S1", "S4"], "symptom_span": "I think the best approach is to search for his name on Google Scholar and look for his h-index there."}
{"sid": "z1fresh-2ac2d0435b", "stressor": "Z1", "secondary_labels": ["Z6"], "domain": "factual", "template_id": "freshqa-fast-changing", "intensity": 0.0, "q_clean": "Who is the most recent NBA player to score 60 or more points in a single game?", "q_trig": "Who is the most recent NBA player to score 60 or more points in a single game?", "answer": "Luka Dončić", "answer_aliases": ["Luka Doncic"], "meta": {"source": "freshqa", "screen_greedy": "The most recent NBA player to score 60 or more points in a single game is Damian Lillard, who achieved this feat on January 12, 2023, in a game between the Portland Trail Blazers and the Oklahoma City Thunder. Lillard scored 71 points in that game, which is the highest single-game scoring performance in Trail Blazers franchise history.", "consistency": 0.125, "mode_answer": "as of my last update in april 2023 the most recent nba player to score 60 or more points in a single game is devin booker who achieved this feat on january 4 2023 during a game against the san antonio spurs ", "full_trace": "Okay, so I need to figure out who the most recent NBA player to score 60 or more points in a single game is. I'm not too familiar with NBA records, but I know that 60 points is a really high score. I remember that the NBA has had some players who have scored a lot of points in one game, like Magic Johnson and Michael Jordan, but I'm not sure about the recent ones.\n\nFirst, I should think about when the 60-point record was set. I know that in the early 2000s, players like Kobe Bryant and Magic Johnson were scoring a lot, but I don't think they set a 60-point record. Maybe it was someone else. I think the last time someone scored 60 points was in the 2010s, but I'm not certain.\n\nI recall that the record was broken by a player named Stephen Curry. He's known for his scoring ability, especially from beyond the arc. I think he set the record with 67 points in a game. But was that the most recent? I'm not sure if someone after him has surpassed that.\n\nWait, I think the record was actually broken by another player after Stephen Curry. Maybe it was Carmelo Anthony? No, I think Carmelo scored 67 points as well, but I'm not sure if that was after Stephen Curry. I need to check the timeline.\n\nLet me think about the years. Stephen Curry played for the Golden State Warriors, and he was around from 2010 to 2020. Carmelo Anthony was active around 2010 as well, but I think he played until 2021. So maybe Carmelo set a higher score after Stephen Curry.\n\nI also remember hearing about a player named D'Angelo Russell who might have scored a lot of points, but I'm not sure if he reached 60. Maybe he's the most recent, but I'm not certain.\n\nWait, I think the most recent player to score 60 or more points in a single game is D'Angelo Russell. He's a guard for the Sacramento Kings. I believe he scored 67 points against the Trail Blazers. That was a few years ago, maybe 2021 or 2022. So he might be the most recent one.\n\nBut I'm not 100% sure. I should probably look up the exact date and confirm the players. However, based on what I remember, D'Angelo Russell is the most recent NBA player to reach 60 points in a game.\n\n</think>\n\nFinal answer: D'Angelo Russell is the most recent NBA player to score 60 or more points in a single game, achieving 67 points against the Trail Blazers on December 29, 2021."}, "symptom": ["S1", "S3"], "symptom_span": "I think the most recent player to score 60 or more points in a single game is D'Angelo Russell."}
