n state. They had a unique style, perhaps a mix of country and pop. I'm not entirely sure about their name, though.\n\nI should also consider the structure of the show. Each season has a set number of contestants, and the competition is usually intense with multiple rounds. The winner is usually the one who can perform consistently and win the public vote as well as the judges.\n\nMaybe I can think about the last few years. In 2020, I think the winner was someone from California, but I'm not certain. Then in 2021, perhaps someone from the Midwest. It seems like the show rotates regions each year. So, if the latest one is from the Midwest, maybe the winner is from a place like Chicago or Minneapolis.\n\nI'm trying to piece together the details. The winner's name is usually something catchy, maybe with a nickname. I think the latest winner might have been a contestant named from a place like \"L.A.\" or \"Chicago.\" Maybe their stage name was something like \"The Voice\" or \"Soul.\"\n\nWait, I'm getting a bit confused. I think the show has had winners with stage names like \"The Voice\" or \"Soul,\" but I'm not sure if that's the case. Maybe the latest winner's name is more unique or has a different twist.\n\nI should also consider the judges' votes. The judges usually have a set of criteria, like vocal range, stage presence, and musicality. The winner is the one who can get the most votes from the public and the judges.\n\nI'm trying to remember if there was any controversy or special circumstances with the latest season. Maybe the winner had a unique performance or faced some challenges during the competition.\n\nI think I'm overcomplicating this. Maybe the latest winner is someone from a specific region, and their name is something like \"The Voice\" or \"Soul.\" I'm not entirely sure, but I think the winner's name is often something memorable and catchy.\n\nWait, I think the latest winner might have been from the Midwest, and their name was something like \"The V