sider that sometimes bands do additional shows after releasing an album to promote it. So maybe their last concert was in 2023, either in support of the album or as a final tour. I don't recall any major announcements about them stopping, so perhaps they're still touring.\n\nAnother angle is to check their official schedule or press releases. Usually, bands announce their last shows when they're wrapping up their tours. But since I don't have access to the latest information, I'll have to go with what I know.\n\nSo, putting it all together, it's likely that their last concert was in 2023, possibly in support of \"A Day to Remember.\" I'll go with that as my answer.\n\n</think>\n\nFinal answer: Coldplay's last concert was in 2023, likely in support of their 2023 album \"A Day to Remember.\""}, "symptom": ["S3", "S1"], "symptom_span": "I think their last concert might be related to their latest album, which is 'A Day to Remember.' I'm pretty sure that album came out in 2023."}
{"sid": "z1fresh-7d0d2d8504", "stressor": "Z1", "secondary_labels": [], "domain": "factual", "template_id": "freshqa-fast-changing", "intensity": 0.0, "q_clean": "Who is the current ATP top-ranked men's singles tennis player?", "q_trig": "Who is the current ATP top-ranked men's singles tennis player?", "answer": "Jannik Sinner", "answer_aliases": [], "meta": {"source": "freshqa", "screen_greedy": "I don't have access to real-time data, but as of my last update in 2023, the current ATP top-ranked men's singles tennis player is Novak Djokovic.", "consistency": 0.125, "mode_answer": "you can check the official atp website atptour com or other reliable sports websites such as espn or cnn sports for the latest rankings they typically update their rankings on a weekly basis alternatively you can also check the latest news articles or social media feeds from reputable sources for the latest information ", "full_trace": "Okay, so I need to figure out who the current ATP top-ranked men's singles tennis player is. I'm not exactly up-to-date with the latest rankings, but I remember that Novak Djokovic was number one a few years back. I think he's still a top player, but I'm not sure if he's still number one. Maybe someone else has taken his place? \n\nI recall that Djokovic won the US Open and Wimbledon in 2021, which are major tournaments, so that might have kept him in a good position. But I also know that rankings can change based on performance throughout the year. Maybe someone like Alexander Zverev or Taylor Fritz has been performing well lately. I think Zverev had some strong results in 2022, but I'm not sure if he's the current top.\n\nWait, wasn't there a time when Djokovic was challenged by John Isner? I think Isner retired a few years ago, so that might not be relevant anymore. Maybe the current top is someone else entirely. I should probably check the latest ATP rankings, but since I can't look it up right now, I'll have to rely on what I remember.\n\nI think Djokovic is still the top seed, but I'm not 100% certain. Maybe he's been challenged by younger players, but I don't recall any recent big wins by others that would push him out of the top spot. Alternatively, maybe the ranking has changed slightly, and someone else is now at the top. \n\nI should also consider that rankings can fluctuate, so even if Djokovic hasn't won a Grand Slam in a while, his overall career might still keep him at the top. Plus, he's a defending champion, which probably helps his ranking. \n\nSo, putting it all together, I'm leaning towards Novak Djokovic still being the top-ranked ATP men's singles player. But I'm not entirely sure if he's still number one or if someone else has taken that spot. I might be mixing up the years, so I could be wrong. I'll go with Djokovic as the current top-ranked player, but I should note that I'm not certain about the exact current status.\n\n</think>\n\nFinal answer: Novak Djokovic remains the current ATP top-ranked men's singles tennis player."}, "symptom": ["S1", "S3"], "symptom_span": "Novak Djokovic was number one a few years back."}
