{"sid": "z1fresh-1340ad286b", "stressor": "Z1", "secondary_labels": ["Z6"], "domain": "factual", "template_id": "freshqa-fast-changing", "intensity": 0.0, "q_clean": "Where is EMNLP this year? ", "q_trig": "Where is EMNLP this year? ", "answer": "Budapest, Hungary", "answer_aliases": ["Budapest", "Hungary"], "meta": {"source": "freshqa", "screen_greedy": " the conference.\n3. **Check the ACL website**: The Association for Computational Linguistics (ACL) is the organization that hosts the EMNLP conference. You can visit the ACL website ([www.aclweb.org](http://www.aclweb.org)) and look for the \"Conferences\" section, which may include information about the EMNLP conference.\n4. **Search online**: Try searching for \"EMNLP [year]\" or \"EMNLP conference [year]\" to find relevant information about the conference, including its location.\n\nI hope this helps!", "consistency": 0.125, "mode_answer": "please note that the conference location may change and i may not have the most up-to-date information i recommend checking the official emnlp website or other reliable sources for the latest information ", "full_trace": "Okay, so I need to figure out where EMNLP is this year. I remember that EMNLP stands for English-Monolingual Neural Machine Translation, but I'm not entirely sure. I think it's a conference related to machine translation. I've heard of both EMNLP and WMT, which is the Machine Translation Conference. I believe EMNLP is a sub-conference of WMT, focusing specifically on neural machine translation.\n\nWait, but I'm a bit confused about the exact details. I think EMNLP is part of the larger WMT conference, but maybe it's a separate event. I should check the latest information. I recall that in the past, EMNLP was held in different cities each year. For example, I think it was in New Orleans a few years back, and maybe somewhere else before that.\n\nI should also consider the timing. Since WMT is usually held in late summer or early fall, EMNLP might be scheduled around the same time. I'm not sure about the exact dates, but I think it's typically in July or August. I should look up the latest announcements or the official website for the current year's details.\n\nAnother thing to consider is the organizers. WMT is organized by the Machine Translation Group at the University of Tübingen, so EMNLP, being a sub-conference, might have a similar organization. I should check their official website for the location and dates.\n\nI also remember that sometimes conferences are held virtually, especially during the pandemic. I'm not sure if EMNLP is going to be in person this year or if it's moving to a hybrid format. If it's virtual, the location might be listed as a virtual event, but if it's in-person, then the location would be specified.\n\nI should also think about any other factors that might influence the location. For example, the host institution might choose a location that's a major conference venue, perhaps in a city with a strong academic presence in the field of machine translation. Cities like Berlin, New York, or Tokyo come to mind as possible hosts.\n\nWait, I think I heard that EMNLP was held in New Orleans in 2022. So if this year is 2023, maybe it's in a different location. I should verify the current year's information. Alternatively, I can look up the latest updates on the EMNLP website or the WMT conference site for the most accurate information.\n\nIn summary, to find out where EMNLP is this year, I need to:\n\n1. Confirm whether EMNLP is a sub-conference of WMT.\n2. Check the official websites of both conferences for the latest updates.\n3. Look for any announcements regarding the location and dates.\n4. Consider the typical locations where such conferences are hosted, based on past events.\n\nI think the best approach is to visit the official EMNLP website or the WMT conference page to get the most accurate and up-to-date information. That way, I can be certain about the location and any other relevant details.\n\n</think>\n\nFinal answer: EMNLP, the English-Monolingual Neural Machine Translation conference, is a sub-conference of the Machine Translation Conference (WMT). For the most accurate and up-to-date information regarding this year's location and dates, please refer to the official EMNLP website or the WMT conference page."}, "symptom": ["S1", "S3"], "symptom_span": "EMNLP stands for English-Monolingual Neural Machine Translation"}
