{"sid": "z1fresh-ce1d221aec", "stressor": "Z1", "secondary_labels": [], "domain": "factual", "template_id": "freshqa-fast-changing", "intensity": 0.0, "q_clean": "Which movie won the latest Academy Award for Best Picture?", "q_trig": "Which movie won the latest Academy Award for Best Picture?", "answer": "One Battle After Another", "answer_aliases": [], "meta": {"source": "freshqa", "screen_greedy": "est some options to help you find the answer:\n\n1. Check the official Academy Awards website (oscars.org) for the latest winners.\n2. Look up online news articles or entertainment websites (e.g., Variety, The Hollywood Reporter, CNN, etc.) for the latest Oscar winners.\n3. Check social media platforms (e.g., Twitter, Facebook, etc.) for updates on the latest Oscar winners.\n\nIf you're looking for the winner of a specific year, feel free to let me know, and I'll do my best to provide the information!", "consistency": 0.125, "mode_answer": "if you re looking for the winner of the best picture award from a more recent year i d be happy to try and help you find the information could you please let me know which year s oscars you re interested in ", "full_trace": "Okay, so I need to figure out which movie won the latest Academy Award for Best Picture. I'm not exactly sure about the current year, but I think it's 2021. Let me try to recall or think through what I know about recent movies and their nominations.\n\nI remember that \"Dune\" was a big contender a few years back, but I think it won in 2021. Wait, was that right? I'm a bit confused because I've heard a lot about \"Dune\" being nominated for various awards. Maybe it's the one. But I'm not 100% certain. Let me think about other movies that were nominated around that time.\n\nThere was \"First Man,\" which was about Andy Kaufman's life. I think that was a strong contender, but I'm not sure if it won. Then there was \" Parasite,\" which was really well-received and won some awards, but I believe it didn't win Best Picture. \"Joker\" was also nominated but didn't win. \"Wonder Woman 1984\" was a big hit, but I don't think it won either.\n\nWait, I think \"Dune\" was the clear favorite. It's a big-budget sci-fi film that was really talked about. The Academy tends to love films with strong acting, great visuals, and meaningful storytelling. \"Dune\" has a lot of that, so it makes sense it would win. Plus, it's based on a book by Frank Herbert, which adds to its credibility.\n\nI should also consider the timing. If it's 2021, then \"Dune\" would have been released around that time, and it's a long-running contender. I don't think any other movie from that year has come close to its nominations. \"First Man\" was more of a personal story, and while it was well-made, it might not have had the same impact on the Academy as a sci-fi epic like \"Dune.\"\n\nSo, putting it all together, I'm pretty confident that \"Dune\" won the Best Picture Oscar in 2021. It's the most likely candidate based on its popularity, the strength of its performances, and the critical acclaim it received.\n\n</think>\n\nFinal answer: The movie \"Dune\" won the 2021 Academy Award for Best Picture."}, "symptom": ["S1", "S3"], "symptom_span": "I think it's 2021. Wait, was that right?"}
{"sid": "z1fresh-6d2f17ed4b", "stressor": "Z1", "secondary_labels": ["Z6"], "domain": "factual", "template_id": "freshqa-fast-changing", "intensity": 0.0, "q_clean": "What is the title of Stephen King's most recent novel?", "q_trig": "What is the title of Stephen King's most recent novel?", "answer": "The End Times", "answer_aliases": [], "meta": {"source": "freshqa", "screen_greedy": "ke Entertainment Weekly, Publishers Weekly, or Book Riot often report on new book releases, including those by Stephen King.\n\nAs of my knowledge cutoff, some of Stephen King's recent novels include:\n\n* \"Later\" (2021)\n* \"Billy Summers\" (2021)\n* \"If It Bleeds\" (2020) (a collection of novellas)\n* \"The Institute\" (2019)\n* \"Elevation\" (2018)\n\nPlease note that this list may not be exhaustive, and I recommend checking the above sources for the most up-to-date information on Stephen King's latest novel.", "consistency": 0.125, "mode_answer": "i do not have access to a search engine to find the latest information on stephen king s published works ", "full_trace": "Okay, so I need to figure out the title of Stephen King's most recent novel. I'm not super familiar with all his works, but I know he's a big name in horror and suspense literature. I remember he's written a lot of books over the years, so I'm not sure which one is the latest. \n\nFirst, I should think about when Stephen King wrote his last book. I know he's been active in the industry for a long time, so maybe his latest release is from the last few years. I think he's been working on some new projects, but I'm not certain about the titles. \n\nI recall that sometimes his books have titles that are a bit cryptic or not directly related to the plot. Sometimes they're just \"The Next [Something]\" or something similar. That might be the case here. \n\nI also remember that he often collaborates with other authors or has co-written works, so the title might not be his alone. Maybe it's a sequel or a prequel to one of his famous series. \n\nI should consider the publication dates. If I can remember any recent releases, that might help. I think his most recent novel might be from around 2020 or 2021. I'm trying to recall if it's \"The Last of Us,\" but wait, that's a collaborating effort with others, and I think it's a TV show, not a novel. \n\nAnother thought: maybe it's part of a new series. He has a lot of series, like the Dark Tower series, but I don't think he's working on that right now. \n\nI also remember that sometimes his newer books are shorter or novellas. Maybe it's something like \"The Last House,\" but I'm not sure. \n\nWait, I think I heard something about a new novel called \"The Last House\" or maybe \"The Last House\" is a sequel. No, that might be a TV show. \n\nAlternatively, maybe it's \"The Last House\" as a standalone novel. I'm not certain. I should try to piece together any clues. \n\nI think the answer is \"The Last House,\" but I'm not 100% sure. I'll go with that, but I should note that I'm not entirely certain and that it's possible it's a different title or that I'm mixing it up with something else.\n\n</think>\n\nFinal answer: Stephen King's most recent novel is \"The Last House.\""}, "symptom": ["S1", "S3"], "symptom_span": "I think the answer is 'The Last House,' but I'm not 100% sure."}
{"sid": "z1fresh-c81821e86b", "stressor": "Z1", "secondary_labels": ["Z6"], "domain": "factual", "template_id": "freshqa-fast-changing", "intensity": 0.0, "q_clean": "When is the next U.S. federal holiday?", "q_trig": "When is the next U.S. federal holiday?", "answer": "Memorial Day", "answer_aliases": ["May 25, 2026", "May 25, 2026", "25 May 2026", "25 May 2026", "05/25/2026", "05-25-2026", "25/05/2026", "25-05-2026", "2026/05/25"], "meta": {"source": "freshqa", "screen_greedy": "here are the next few federal holidays:\n\n* Memorial Day: Monday, May 29, 2023\n* Juneteenth National Independence Day: Monday, June 19, 2023\n* Independence Day: Tuesday, July 4, 2023\n* Labor Day: Monday, September 4, 2023\n* Columbus Day: Monday, October 9, 2023\n* Veterans Day: Monday, November 11, 2023\n* Thanksgiving Day: Thursday, November 23, 2023\n* Christmas Day: Monday, December 25, 2023\n\nPlease note that federal holidays are typically observed on the nearest Monday if they fall on a weekend.", "consistency": 0.125, "mode_answer": "if you re looking for a specific date i d be happy to provide more information ", "full_trace": "Okay, so I need to figure out when the next U.S. federal holiday is. I'm not exactly sure what federal holidays are, but I think they're official days off for the country. I remember hearing about some holidays like Memorial Day and Labor Day, but I'm not clear on all of them. Let me try to recall and list what I know.\n\nFirst, I know that there's Independence Day, which is July 4th. That's a big one, celebrating the founding of the United States. Then there's Memorial Day, which I think is around May, but I'm not sure of the exact date. I think it's the last Saturday in May, but I'm not certain. \n\nThen there are federal holidays related to the U.S. military. I believe there's a day called Decoration Day, which I think is May 31st. It's in memory of military personnel who died in combat. I'm not 100% sure about the date, though.\n\nI also remember something about a federal holiday in December, maybe around the 11th or 12th. I think it's for observing the nation's flag at half-mast. I'm not sure if that's correct, but I'll go with that for now.\n\nThen there's another federal holiday in November, I believe. I think it's the 11th of November, but I'm not certain. I think it's related to the national flag, maybe for a different reason. I'll have to check that.\n\nWait, I also think there's a federal holiday in January, maybe around the 20th or 21st. I think it's for observing the national flag at half-mast as well. I'm not sure if that's accurate, but I'll include it for now.\n\nSo, putting it all together, I have Independence Day on July 4th, Decoration Day on May 31st, the flag at half-mast in December on the 11th, November 11th, and January 20th or 21st. But I'm not entirely sure about all these dates. I might be mixing up some of them or the months. I should probably verify each one to make sure I have the correct dates.\n\nLet me think about each holiday one by one. Independence Day is definitely July 4th. That's clear. Memorial Day is usually in May, but the exact date is the last Saturday in May. So, if this year is 2023, May 27th would be the last Saturday, making Memorial Day 2023 on May 29th. Wait, no, that's not right. I think it's the first Monday after the last full week of April. So, if April 30th is a Monday, then May 1st would be the next Monday, but Memorial Day is usually the first Monday in May. So, in 2023, May 29th is the last Monday in May, but Memorial Day is the first Monday after the last week of April. So, if April 30th is a Monday, then May 1st is the next Monday, but that would be Memorial Day. Wait, no, that can't be right because Memorial Day is usually in early May. I think I'm confusing it with other holidays. Maybe I should look up the exact dates, but since I can't do that right now, I'll have to go with what I remember.\n\nDecoration Day is May 31st, which is the last day of May. That seems correct. Then, the flag at half-mast is observed on the 11th of November, I believe. That's a federal holiday, so November 11th is also a federal holiday. Then, in December, the 11th is when the flag is observed at half-mast. So, December 11th is another federal holiday.\n\nWait, I'm getting confused between November and December. Let me try to organize this:\n\n- July 4th: Independence Day\n- May 31st: Decoration Day\n- November 11th: Veterans Day\n- December 11th: Flag Day\n- January 20th or 21st: Another federal holiday related to the flag\n\nI think I might have mixed up some of these. Let me try to recall correctly. I know that November 11th is Veterans Day, which is a federal holiday. December 11th is when the flag is observed at half-mast, but it's not a federal holiday. The federal holidays are probably Independence Day, Memorial Day (which is the last Monday in May), Decoration Day on May 31st, Veterans Day on November 11th, and then another one in January, maybe around the 20th or 21st.\n\nWait, I think the federal holidays are:\n\n- January 1st: New Year's Day\n- January 20th: Martin Luther King Jr. Day\n- February 19th: Valentine's Day (but I don't think that's a federal holiday)\n- May 31st: Decoration Day\n- June 19th: Juneteenth (not federal)\n- July 4th: Independence Day\n- July 4th is a federal holiday\n- September 11th: Not a federal holiday\n- November 11th: Veterans Day\n- December 11th: Flag Day\n\nWait, I'm getting more confused now. Maybe I should list the actual federal holidays. I think the federal holidays in the U.S. are:\n\n1. New Year's Day: January 1st\n2. Martin Luther King Jr. Birthday: January 20th\n3. Washington's Birthday: February 22nd\n4. Memorial Day: Last Monday in May\n5. Decoration Day: May 31st\n6. Independence Day: July 4th\n7. Labor Day: September 1st\n8. Halloween: October 31st (not federal)\n9. Thanksgiving: Last Thursday in November\n10. Christmas: December 25th\n11. New Year's Eve: December 31st\n12. January 20th: Martin Luther King Jr. Day\n13. December 11th: Flag Day\n\nWait, that doesn't make sense because December 11th is Flag Day, but I thought it was a federal holiday. Maybe I'm mixing up some of these. Let me try to get this straight.\n\nI think the correct federal holidays are:\n\n- January 1st: New Year's Day\n- January 20th: Martin Luther King Jr. Day\n- May 31st: Decoration Day\n- July 4th: Independence Day\n- September 1st: Labor Day\n- November 11th: Veterans Day\n- December 11th: Flag Day\n\nWait, but I'm not sure if December 11th is a federal holiday or just a day when the flag is observed at half-mast. I think it's the latter. So, the federal holidays are:\n\n- January 1st: New Year's Day\n- January 20th: Martin Luther King Jr. Day\n- May 31st: Decoration Day\n- July 4th: Independence Day\n- September 1st: Labor Day\n- November 11th: Veterans Day\n\nAnd then, the days when the flag is observed at half-mast are:\n\n- November 11th: Veterans Day (also a federal holiday)\n- December 11th: Flag Day (not a federal holiday)\n\nWait, that can't be right because December 11th is a federal holiday. I'm getting confused. Let me try to look up the actual federal holidays to make sure. But since I can't do that, I'll have to rely on my memory.\n\nI think the correct federal holidays are:\n\n1. New Year's Day: January 1st\n2. Martin Luther King Jr. Birthday: January 20th\n3. Washington's Birthday: February 22nd\n4. Memorial Day: Last Monday in May\n5. Decoration Day: May 31st\n6. Independence Day: July 4th\n7. Labor Day: September 1st\n8. Halloween: October 31st (not federal)\n9. Thanksgiving: Last Thursday in November\n10. Christmas: December 25th\n11. New Year's Eve: December 31st\n12. December 11th: Flag Day (not a federal holiday)\n\nWait, now I'm confused again. I think December 11th is when the flag is observed at half-mast, but it's not a federal holiday. The federal holidays are up to November 11th, which is Veterans Day. So, the next federal holiday after that would be December 11th, but it's not a federal holiday. Then, the next one would be January 20th, which is Martin Luther King Jr. Day.\n\nBut I'm not sure about the exact dates. I think I need to clarify this. Let me try to list them correctly:\n\n- January 1st: New Year's Day\n- January 20th: Martin Luther King Jr. Day\n- May 31st: Decoration Day\n- July 4th: Independence Day\n- September 1st: Labor Day\n- November 11th: Veterans Day\n\nAnd then, the flag is observed at half-mast on:\n\n- November 11th: Veterans Day (also a federal holiday)\n- December 11th: Flag Day (not a federal holiday)\n\nWait,\n</think>\n\nFinal answer: The next U.S. federal holiday is **Martin Luther King Jr. Day** on **January 20th**."}, "symptom": ["S1", "S3"], "symptom_span": "I'm not exactly sure what federal holidays are, but I think they're official days off for the country."}
{"sid": "z1fresh-db8b635f11", "stressor": "Z1", "secondary_labels": ["Z6"], "domain": "factual", "template_id": "freshqa-fast-changing", "intensity": 0.0, "q_clean": "On what date in North America did the most recent Microsoft's Patch Tuesday come out?", "q_trig": "On what date in North America did the most recent Microsoft's Patch Tuesday come out?", "answer": "Apr 14, 2026", "answer_aliases": ["April 14, 2026", "14 Apr 2026", "14 April 2026", "04/14/2026", "04-14-2026", "14/04/2026", "14-04-2026", "2026/04/14", "2026-04-14"], "meta": {"source": "freshqa", "screen_greedy": " usually post the latest security updates on the second Tuesday of the month.\n2. Check the Microsoft Security Blog: Microsoft's Security Blog ([blogs.microsoft.com/msrc](http://blogs.microsoft.com/msrc)) often posts updates on the latest security patches and vulnerabilities.\n3. Check online news sources: Websites like The Verge, ZDNet, or TechRadar often report on the latest Patch Tuesday updates.\n\nIf you provide me with the current date, I can try to help you find the most recent Patch Tuesday.", "consistency": 0.125, "mode_answer": "the patch tuesday date varies from month to month as it occurs on the second tuesday of every month however i do not have access to a search engine to find the most recent date of microsoft s patch tuesday in north america ", "full_trace": "Okay, so I need to figure out the most recent Microsoft Patch Tuesday in North America. I'm not exactly sure what Patch Tuesday is, but I think it's when Microsoft releases security updates for their products. I remember hearing about it before, maybe in the news or something. \n\nFirst, I should probably confirm what Patch Tuesday actually is. From what I recall, it's a tradition started by Microsoft where they release cumulative updates on a specific date each month. I think it's usually the first Tuesday of each month, but I'm not 100% certain. Maybe it's the last Tuesday? I'm a bit fuzzy on the details.\n\nNow, the question is about North America. So, I guess I need to consider time zones. If the event happens in North America, it would be on the same Tuesday, but depending on the time zone, it might be a Monday or Tuesday in other regions. But since the user specified North America, I can focus on dates within that region.\n\nI should check when the last Patch Tuesday was. I think it was a few months back. Maybe around October 2023? I'm not sure. I should look up the exact date. Wait, I remember that Patch Tuesday happens on the first Tuesday of each month, so the last one would be the first Tuesday of December 2023. That would make it December 5, 2023. But I'm not entirely sure if that's correct.\n\nLet me think about how Patch Tuesdays usually work. They often coincide with the first Tuesday, but sometimes there's a lag because of time zones. For example, if a Tuesday in New York is a Monday in Los Angeles, the event might be a Monday there. But the main date is the Tuesday in the New York time zone. So, if the last Patch Tuesday was in December, it would be December 5, 2023, in New York, which would be the same day in other parts of North America, just a day later or earlier depending on the time zone.\n\nI should also consider if there have been any recent updates. Maybe Microsoft released a Patch Tuesday in November 2023, but I think the last one was indeed in December. I'm trying to remember if I saw something about it in the news recently. I think it was around that time, but I'm not certain about the exact date.\n\nAnother thing to consider is that sometimes there are multiple Patch Tuesdays in a month if there are multiple vulnerabilities found. But usually, it's one per month. So, the most recent one would be the first Tuesday of December 2023, which is the 5th. That seems to make sense.\n\nI should also check if there are any other factors, like daylight saving time, which might shift the date. But since December doesn't have daylight saving time in most places, the date should remain the same. So, December 5, 2023, would be the date.\n\nWait, but I'm not 100% sure. Maybe I should look up a calendar or check a reliable source to confirm. But since I can't access external information right now, I'll go with my best guess based on what I remember and the structure of Patch Tuesdays.\n\nSo, putting it all together, the most recent Microsoft Patch Tuesday in North America was on December 5, 2023. That's the first Tuesday of December, and it's when Microsoft released their cumulative updates for that month.\n\n</think>\n\nFinal answer: The most recent Microsoft Patch Tuesday in North America was on December 5, 2023."}, "symptom": ["S1", "S3"], "symptom_span": "I think it's usually the first Tuesday of each month, but I'm not 100% certain."}
{"sid": "z1fresh-58bf430f29", "stressor": "Z1", "secondary_labels": ["Z6"], "domain": "factual", "template_id": "freshqa-fast-changing", "intensity": 0.0, "q_clean": "The upcoming Microsoft's Patch Tuesday will come out on what date in North America?", "q_trig": "The upcoming Microsoft's Patch Tuesday will come out on what date in North America?", "answer": "May 12, 2026", "answer_aliases": ["12 May 2026", "12 May 2026", "05/12/2026", "05-12-2026", "12/05/2026", "12-05-2026", "2026/05/12", "2026-05-12"], "meta": {"source": "freshqa", "screen_greedy": "Microsoft typically releases its Patch Tuesday updates on the second Tuesday of every month. To determine the exact date of the next Patch Tuesday, I'll need to know the current month. However, I can give you a general idea of when the next Patch Tuesday will be.\n\nIf you tell me the current month, I can tell you the exact date of the next Patch Tuesday.", "consistency": 0.125, "mode_answer": "1 **microsoft s official website** you can visit microsoft s official website www microsoft com http //www microsoft com and check their security bulletin page where they typically post the schedule for patch tuesday they usually announce the date and details about upcoming patches a few weeks in advance ", "full_trace": "Okay, so I need to figure out when the upcoming Microsoft Patch Tuesday is going to happen in North America. I remember that Patch Tuesdays are usually scheduled on the last Tuesday of each month, right? So, for example, the last Tuesday in January, February, and so on. But I'm not exactly sure about the exact dates, especially for the upcoming one.\n\nI think the last Tuesday of the month would be the 24th, 31st, or the 27th depending on how the month starts. Let me check the current month. Wait, the user didn't specify which month, so maybe I should consider the next one after the current date. But since I don't have the current date, perhaps I should just provide the general information that Patch Tuesday is on the last Tuesday of each month.\n\nAlternatively, maybe I should look up the current month's last Tuesday. But since I can't access the internet, I'll have to rely on my memory. Let's say today is October 2023. October 1st was a Sunday, so the last Tuesday would be the 24th. But if it's November, the last Tuesday would be the 28th. Hmm, but without knowing the current date, it's a bit tricky.\n\nWait, the user might be asking for the upcoming Patch Tuesday, so perhaps the next one after a certain date. But without knowing the current date, I can't be precise. Maybe I should explain that Patch Tuesdays are typically the last Tuesday of each month and provide an example, like in October 2023, it's the 24th.\n\nAlternatively, I could mention that the exact date depends on the month and year, and suggest checking Microsoft's official website or an IT calendar for the most accurate information. That way, the user knows where to look for the specific date.\n\nI should also consider that sometimes Patch Tuesdays might be delayed or rescheduled due to holidays or other reasons, so it's good to check for any updates. But again, without real-time data, I can't confirm any changes.\n\nSo, putting it all together, I'll explain that Patch Tuesday is usually the last Tuesday of each month and provide an example date, while also advising the user to check official sources for the latest information.\n\n</think>\n\nFinal answer: The upcoming Microsoft Patch Tuesday is typically held on the last Tuesday of each month. For example, in October 2023, it would be on October 24th. For the most accurate and updated information, please refer to Microsoft's official website or an IT calendar."}, "symptom": ["S1", "S4"], "symptom_span": "But without knowing the current date, it's a bit tricky."}
{"sid": "z1fresh-9b23dd8d74", "stressor": "Z1", "secondary_labels": [], "domain": "factual", "template_id": "freshqa-fast-changing", "intensity": 0.0, "q_clean": "Who was the winner of American Idol this year?", "q_trig": "Who was the winner of American Idol this year?", "answer": "This year's American Idol is still airing", "answer_aliases": [], "meta": {"source": "freshqa", "screen_greedy": "s to help you find the answer:\n\n1. Check the official American Idol website or social media channels for the latest updates.\n2. Look for news articles or entertainment websites that cover the latest season of American Idol.\n3. You can also check online search engines like Google to find the latest information on the winner of the current season.\n\nIf you're looking for information on a specific season, please let me know the year or season number, and I'll do my best to provide the winner's name!", "consistency": 0.125, "mode_answer": "if you re looking for information on past winners i can try to help you with that ", "full_trace": "Okay, so I need to figure out who won American Idol this year. I'm not exactly sure about the current season, but I think it's around 2023 or maybe 2022. I remember hearing about some big names in the show, but I'm not certain who it was. Let me try to recall any recent contestants or news about the show.\n\nI know that American Idol is a popular TV show where contestants perform for judges and an audience to win a million dollars. The winner is usually the one who impresses the judges the most. I think the judges are Paula Deen, Sheryl Lee Ralph, and Luke Lerdwich. They've been part of the show for a long time, so they might still be involved.\n\nI also remember that the winner often comes from a specific region, like the South or the Midwest, but I'm not sure if that's relevant. Maybe the winner is someone who's been in the news or has a big following. I think there was a contestant who was really emotional during their performance, maybe even had a heart condition, which made the judges really moved.\n\nWait, I think the winner was from the Midwest. Maybe someone from a smaller town or a place I'm not as familiar with. I'm trying to remember if it was a specific artist or singer. I think it might have been someone who was really good with their voice and had a unique style.\n\nI also recall that the winner often gets a lot of attention after the show, maybe even more than the runner-up. They might have been in the news for other reasons, like social media or personal issues. I'm not sure if the winner was also a contestant in another season or if they were a first-time contestant.\n\nAnother thing to consider is the format of the show. I think there are different versions now, like American Idol: The Next Generation or other spin-offs, but I'm not sure if that affects the current winner. Maybe the winner was part of a group or performed a duet, which is a common trend in the show.\n\nI'm also trying to remember if there were any controversies or unexpected outcomes this year. Sometimes the winner isn't the most obvious choice, and that can make the show more exciting. I think the judges might have been split on the winner, leading to some intense discussions.\n\nWait, I think the winner was from a place called Emporia, Kansas. That's a city I've heard about, but I'm not sure if that's correct. I also think the winner might have been a female contestant, maybe from a smaller town, which is a common theme in the show.\n\nI'm trying to piece together the details. The winner performed a song that was quite emotional, and maybe it was a cover version or something that stood out. I think the judges were moved by the performance, and the winner had a strong presence on stage.\n\nI'm also considering the possibility that the winner might have been someone who was already a well-known artist, but I'm not sure if that's the case. More likely, they were a contestant who surprised everyone with their talent.\n\nI'm a bit confused about the exact details, but I think the winner was a contestant from Emporia, Kansas, who performed a powerful song that left the judges speechless. They might have been a female singer with a unique style that made them stand out.\n\nWait, I think the winner was Katelyn Sherwin. She was from Emporia, Kansas, and she won the competition with her powerful performance. She had a unique voice and stage presence, which made her the favorite among the judges.\n\nI'm trying to remember if there were any other factors that contributed to her victory, like her emotional delivery or the way she handled the judges' questions. I think she was very confident and handled the pressure well, which is a big part of the competition.\n\nOverall, I'm pretty confident that Katelyn Sherwin was the winner of American Idol this year, but I'm not 100% sure about all the details. I might be mixing up some information from other seasons, but I think this is the most recent winner.\n\n</think>\n\nFinal answer: Katelyn Sherwin was the winner of American Idol in the current season. She hails from Emporia, Kansas, and was celebrated for her powerful stage presence and unique vocal style. Her emotional performance left the judges, including Paula Deen, Sheryl Lee Ralph, and Luke Lerdwich, speechless. Known for her confident demeanor and ability to handle pressure, Katelyn Sherwin emerged victorious, making her the season's winner."}, "symptom": ["S1", "S3"], "symptom_span": "This year's American Idol is still airing"}
{"sid": "z1fresh-52560f3b49", "stressor": "Z1", "secondary_labels": ["Z6"], "domain": "factual", "template_id": "freshqa-fast-changing", "intensity": 0.0, "q_clean": "What is the base price of the new Tesla Model Y Premium All-Wheel Drive?", "q_trig": "What is the base price of the new Tesla Model Y Premium All-Wheel Drive?", "answer": "$48,990", "answer_aliases": [], "meta": {"source": "freshqa", "screen_greedy": "s for the Tesla Model Y Premium All-Wheel Drive in the US:\n\n* Model Y Premium All-Wheel Drive: $52,990\n* Model Y Premium All-Wheel Drive with 19-inch Induction Wheels: $54,990\n* Model Y Premium All-Wheel Drive with 20-inch Induction Wheels: $56,990\n\nPlease note that prices may vary depending on the location, and there may be additional options or features that can increase the price. I recommend checking Tesla's website or visiting a local Tesla store for the most up-to-date pricing information.", "consistency": 0.125, "mode_answer": "the base price of the 2022 tesla model y premium all-wheel drive is around $51 990 however prices may vary depending on the location and there may be additional options and features that can affect the final price ", "full_trace": "Okay, so I need to figure out the base price of the new Tesla Model Y Premium All-Wheel Drive. I'm not too familiar with Tesla's pricing, but I know they've been updating their models over time. Let me think about how to approach this.\n\nFirst, I remember that Tesla models are usually updated with new features and sometimes changes in pricing. The Model Y is their mid-size SUV, and the Premium version comes with some nicer features compared to the base Model Y. I think the Premium version might have a higher base price than the standard Model Y.\n\nI also recall that Tesla's pricing can vary based on where you buy the car. Some dealerships might offer different pricing or packages, so the base price I get might not be the exact figure in every region. But I'm looking for the base price, not including any options or packages.\n\nI should consider checking Tesla's official website because they usually have the most accurate and up-to-date information. They might have a section where you can compare models or view the specs and pricing. Alternatively, maybe there's a press release or a press kit from when the Model Y Premium was introduced that details the pricing.\n\nAnother thought is that sometimes when a new model is released, the base price might be similar to the previous year's model but with some upgrades. So if I know the base price of the Model Y from the previous year, I might be able to estimate the new price, but I should be cautious because Tesla often makes significant price changes, especially with new features.\n\nI also wonder if there are any optional features that come with the Premium package that might affect the base price. For example, things like a sunroof, better seats, or other luxury features. But since I'm looking for the base price, I should focus on the core features without any added options.\n\nI should also consider that sometimes the base price might be slightly different in different markets. For example, in the U.S., Europe, or other regions, the pricing might vary. So, if I'm looking for the base price in a specific region, I might need to specify that in my search.\n\nMaybe I can think about the competition. Other luxury SUVs from brands like Mercedes, BMW, or Cadillac might have similar pricing ranges, but I'm not sure if that helps me directly. However, it can give me a ballpark figure to compare against.\n\nI also recall that Tesla's pricing is often competitive because they offer a range of features and sometimes have incentives like the $5,000 rebate or the $1,000 credit for college. But again, these are additional benefits, not the base price.\n\nAnother approach could be to look at press materials or news articles from when the Model Y Premium was launched. They often provide detailed breakdowns of the pricing, including the base model. I might need to search for press releases or official announcements regarding the Model Y Premium.\n\nI should also consider reaching out to Tesla's customer service or sales team directly. They might be able to provide me with the most accurate information, especially if I can provide a specific region or country where the car is sold.\n\nWait, but I'm not sure if I can access that information publicly. Maybe there are forums or communities where car enthusiasts discuss Tesla prices, but I have to be careful because prices can vary based on individual deals or test drives.\n\nI think the best approach is to go to Tesla's official website and look for the Model Y Premium specifications and pricing. They usually have a detailed breakdown, including the base price. If I can't find it on the website, maybe I can look for press kits or official press releases from when the car was introduced.\n\nAlternatively, I can check car review websites or automotive blogs where they might have covered the Model Y Premium and listed the base price. However, I should verify the information from multiple sources to ensure accuracy.\n\nI also remember that sometimes the base price can be slightly different based on the trim level. The Premium version might have a base price that's higher than the base Model Y but lower than the top trims. So, I need to make sure I'm looking at the Premium base price specifically.\n\nIn summary, my plan is to:\n\n1. Visit Tesla's official website and search for the Model Y Premium specifications and pricing.\n2. Check press releases or press kits from when the Model Y Premium was introduced.\n3. Look for any official announcements or statements from Tesla about the pricing.\n4. Verify the information with multiple sources to ensure accuracy.\n\nI should also be cautious about relying solely on online sources, as prices can fluctuate based on market conditions or promotions. However, for the purpose of this question, I think the official sources would provide the most reliable information.\n\nAfter gathering the information from these sources, I can compile the base price. I believe the base price of the Model Y Premium All-Wheel Drive is around $55,000, but I need to confirm this with the official sources to make sure.\n\n</think>\n\nFinal answer: The base price of the new Tesla Model Y Premium All-Wheel Drive is $55,000."}, "symptom": ["S1", "S4"], "symptom_span": "I believe the base price of the new Tesla Model Y Premium All-Wheel Drive is around $55,000, but I need to confirm this with the official sources to make sure."}
{"sid": "z1fresh-20d91f3544", "stressor": "Z1", "secondary_labels": ["Z6"], "domain": "factual", "template_id": "freshqa-fast-changing", "intensity": 0.0, "q_clean": "What is the latest version of Android?", "q_trig": "What is the latest version of Android?", "answer": "Android 16", "answer_aliases": [], "meta": {"source": "freshqa", "screen_greedy": "The latest version of Android is Android 13, also known as Android 13. It was officially released on October 7, 2022.", "consistency": 0.375, "mode_answer": "the latest version of android is android 13 also known as android 13 it was officially released on october 7 2022 ", "full_trace": "Okay, so I need to figure out the latest version of Android. I remember that Android is always getting updated, but I'm not exactly sure what the most recent one is. I think it's something like Android 13 or maybe 14? I'm a bit confused because I've heard people talk about different versions, and sometimes they refer to them by numbers with letters, like 12p or 13R. I'm not sure if those are official or just rumors.\n\nI think the latest version is Android 13, but I'm not 100% certain. Maybe it's 13.1 or 13.2? I've heard that sometimes companies release beta versions before the final release, so maybe there's a 13R or 13.1 version. I should check if there's an official announcement for the latest one. I remember Google usually releases updates every year, so if the last official update was Android 12, then 13 would be the next one.\n\nWait, I think I saw somewhere that Android 13 was released in 2023, but I'm not sure if that's the latest. Maybe there's a newer version after that? I should look up when Google officially released Android 13. If it was released in 2023, then maybe 13 is the latest, but I'm not certain if there's a 14 yet.\n\nAlso, I've heard about some features in the latest versions, like better privacy tools, improved security, and maybe some new UI elements. I think Google has been focusing a lot on security and privacy, so maybe the latest version has some significant updates in that area. I'm not sure if those features are only in the beta versions or the official ones.\n\nAnother thing I'm confused about is the naming convention. Sometimes it's just a number, sometimes it has letters like p or R. I think those might be different beta versions or different regions. For example, Android 13p might be a pre-release version for certain countries. But the official latest version is probably just 13.\n\nI should also consider if there are any rumors about an Android 14. Maybe Google is working on it, but it's not released yet. If that's the case, then 13 would still be the latest official version. I don't want to get confused by unofficial versions or rumors.\n\nSo, putting it all together, I think the latest official version of Android is 13, which was released in 2023. There might be beta versions like 13.1 or 13R for testing, but the main and latest one is 13. I should make sure to confirm this with an official source or release announcement to be sure.\n\n</think>\n\nFinal answer: The latest officially released version of Android is Android 13, which was released in 2023. While there may be beta versions such as 13.1 or 13R for testing, the main and latest official version is Android 13."}, "symptom": ["S1", "S3"], "symptom_span": "I think it's something like Android 13 or maybe 14?"}
{"sid": "z1fresh-e6f49448cc", "stressor": "Z1", "secondary_labels": ["Z6"], "domain": "factual", "template_id": "freshqa-fast-changing", "intensity": 0.0, "q_clean": "Who is the richest man on earth?", "q_trig": "Who is the richest man on earth?", "answer": "Elon Musk", "answer_aliases": ["Elon Reeve Musk"], "meta": {"source": "freshqa", "screen_greedy": "O of SpaceX and Tesla\n2. **Jeff Bezos** - Net worth: over $190 billion\n\t* Founder and Executive Chair of Amazon\n3. **Bernard Arnault** - Net worth: over $160 billion\n\t* CEO of LVMH (Moët Hennessy Louis Vuitton)\n4. **Bill Gates** - Net worth: over $150 billion\n\t* Co-Founder of Microsoft\n5. **Mark Zuckerberg** - Net worth: over $130 billion\n\t* Co-Founder and CEO of Facebook\n\nPlease keep in mind that these numbers are subject to change and may not reflect the current net worth of these individuals.", "consistency": 0.125, "mode_answer": "however please note that the ranking of the world s richest people can change rapidly due to various factors such as stock market fluctuations investments and other business dealings ", "full_trace": "Okay, so I need to figure out who the richest man on earth is. I remember hearing about someone named Jeff Bezos before. He's the guy who owns Amazon, right? I think he's also involved in other companies like Blue Origin and something else with a rocket. But I'm not entirely sure if he's the richest. There's also Elon Musk, who I know runs Tesla and SpaceX. I think he's also a big name in the tech industry.\n\nWait, I think there was a time when Jeff Bezos was the richest, but maybe Elon Musk has taken over now. I'm a bit confused because I've heard both of their names mentioned in the context of being the richest. Maybe it's not just one person? Or perhaps there's someone else who's even richer than both of them.\n\nI should probably look up some recent information. I remember reading that Jeff Bezos was the richest person for a while, but I think in 2022, Elon Musk became the new richest. I think his companies, especially SpaceX and Tesla, have done really well, especially with the recent success of the Starship program. That might have boosted his net worth significantly.\n\nBut then again, there are other billionaires who might be involved in industries like finance or real estate. For example, someone like Bill Gates, but I don't think he's in the running for being the richest individual. There's also Warren Buffett, but I believe he's more of a investor than a tech entrepreneur.\n\nSo, putting it all together, it seems like Elon Musk is the current richest man on earth, replacing Jeff Bezos. Both have built massive companies, but Musk's ventures into space and electric vehicles might have given him the edge. I should double-check the exact figures to confirm, but based on what I know, Elon Musk is leading the pack now.\n\n</think>\n\nFinal answer: As of the latest reports, Elon Musk is the current richest man on earth, having surpassed Jeff Bezos in terms of net worth. His ventures in Tesla, SpaceX, and other companies have significantly contributed to his wealth."}, "symptom": ["S1", "S3"], "symptom_span": "I think in 2022, Elon Musk became the new richest."}
{"sid": "z1fresh-43b53c48a6", "stressor": "Z1", "secondary_labels": ["Z6"], "domain": "factual", "template_id": "freshqa-fast-changing", "intensity": 0.0, "q_clean": "Which team is at the top of the latest Premier League season?", "q_trig": "Which team is at the top of the latest Premier League season?", "answer": "Arsenal", "answer_aliases": ["Arsenal F.C."], "meta": {"source": "freshqa", "screen_greedy": "s to help you find the latest information on the Premier League standings:\n\n1. Check the official Premier League website (premierleague.com) for the latest standings and news.\n2. Look for sports news websites or apps, such as BBC Sport, Sky Sports, or ESPN, which often provide up-to-date information on the Premier League.\n3. Follow your favorite Premier League team's social media accounts or website for the latest news and updates.\n\nI hope this helps! Let me know if you have any other questions.", "consistency": 0.125, "mode_answer": "if you provide me with the current season e g 2022-23 i can try to give you an idea of which team was at the top of the table at the time of my training data up to 2022 ", "full_trace": "Okay, so I need to figure out which team is currently at the top of the 2023-2024 Premier League season. I'm not exactly sure about all the teams, but I remember some of the big names. Let me think... I know that Manchester City and Liverpool are usually at the top, but I'm not sure which one is leading this season. \n\nI think Manchester City has been doing really well, especially with their manager, maybe Guardiola? They've won a lot of games, but I'm not certain if they're the top. On the other hand, Liverpool has had some ups and downs this season. They had a really strong start, winning a lot of games, but maybe they've faced some tough opponents later on. \n\nWait, I think there was a time when Manchester City was leading the league, but I'm not sure if they've held that title or if Liverpool has taken over. Maybe I should consider other teams too, like Chelsea or Tottenham. Chelsea has a good manager, but I don't think they're in the title race. Tottenham, well, they had some issues with injuries and maybe didn't perform as well as expected.\n\nOh, and there's also Manchester United, but they're probably not in the title race anymore. They had a good season, but not as strong as the top two. So, between City and Liverpool, I'm trying to remember who's ahead. I think Manchester City might be leading, but I'm not 100% sure. Maybe I should check some stats or news from recent games to confirm. \n\nWait, I recall that Manchester City had a few games where they lost, but they bounced back. Liverpool, on the other hand, might have had a few high-scoring games but perhaps didn't win as many. I'm a bit confused now. Maybe I should think about the points. If Manchester City has more points, they're leading. But if Liverpool has more, then they're on top. \n\nI think I've heard that Manchester City is currently leading the league, but I'm not entirely certain. They've been consistent, but sometimes Liverpool can pull ahead if they win a few more games. I'm going to go with Manchester City as the top team, but I'm not 100% sure. Maybe I should look up the latest standings to confirm.\n\n</think>\n\nFinal answer: The team currently at the top of the 2023-2024 Premier League season is Manchester City."}, "symptom": ["S3", "S4"], "symptom_span": "I think Manchester City has been doing really well, especially with their manager, maybe Guardiola?"}
{"sid": "z1fresh-5e779678a4", "stressor": "Z1", "secondary_labels": ["Z6"], "domain": "factual", "template_id": "freshqa-fast-changing", "intensity": 0.0, "q_clean": "Is Arsenal on the top of the latest Premier League standings?", "q_trig": "Is Arsenal on the top of the latest Premier League standings?", "answer": "Yes", "answer_aliases": [], "meta": {"source": "freshqa", "screen_greedy": " I'm a large language model, I don't have real-time access to current information. But I can suggest some ways for you to find out the latest Premier League standings.\n\nYou can check the official Premier League website (premierleague.com) or other reliable sports websites such as BBC Sport, Sky Sports, or ESPN for the latest standings. They usually update the standings in real-time.\n\nIf you'd like, I can also provide you with the latest standings from a specific date or season. Just let me know!", "consistency": 0.25, "mode_answer": "please let me know if there s anything else i can help you with ", "full_trace": "Okay, so I need to figure out whether Arsenal is currently on top of the Premier League standings. I'm not exactly sure about the latest standings, but I can try to recall or think through what I know.\n\nFirst, I remember that Arsenal has been a top team in recent years, especially under managers like Unai Emery and then Eddie Gabriel. They won the Premier League in 2020-2021 under Emery. But I think they might not have won it since then. Maybe they were in the race around that time.\n\nI also think about the teams that are usually at the top. Manchester City and Liverpool have been dominant recently, especially with their respective managers. They've both won the league multiple times. So, if Arsenal is on top now, that would be unusual because these two teams are usually at the top.\n\nI wonder if there's any recent news or rumors about Arsenal's form. Maybe they've had a good season so far. But I'm not sure about their current position. They might have had a tough match recently or maybe some injuries affecting their performance.\n\nAnother thing to consider is the time of the question. If it's after the 2020-2021 season, then Arsenal wouldn't be on top anymore. But if it's around that time, they were. I think the latest season ended in 2021, so if the question is about the 2021-2022 season, Arsenal isn't on top anymore.\n\nI should also think about other factors like relegation or promotion. If Arsenal is avoiding relegation, they might be near the top, but not necessarily at the very top. Similarly, if they're making a move up, they might have climbed higher, but I don't think they've done that recently.\n\nSo, putting it all together, I don't think Arsenal is currently on top of the Premier League standings. It's more likely that Manchester City or Liverpool are the ones leading now. Unless there's some recent news I'm not aware of, which I don't recall.\n\n</think>\n\nFinal answer: No, Arsenal is not currently on top of the Premier League standings. Manchester City or Liverpool are more likely to be leading the league at present."}, "symptom": ["S1", "S3"], "symptom_span": "I think they might not have won it since then."}
{"sid": "z1fresh-db99163b80", "stressor": "Z1", "secondary_labels": ["Z6"], "domain": "factual", "template_id": "freshqa-fast-changing", "intensity": 0.0, "q_clean": "Who was the most recent incumbent president worldwide who ran for re-election but was not reelected?", "q_trig": "Who was the most recent incumbent president worldwide who ran for re-election but was not reelected?", "answer": "Lazarus Chakwera", "answer_aliases": [], "meta": {"source": "freshqa", "screen_greedy": "stem was changed to a presidential system, and Erdogan was elected as the first president under the new system.\n\nHowever, if I had to choose one recent example of an incumbent president who ran for re-election and was not re-elected in a traditional sense, I would say it was:\n\n**Argentina: Mauricio Macri (2019)**\n\nMacri was the first incumbent president in Argentina's history to lose a re-election bid. He was defeated by Alberto Fernández, a Peronist candidate, in the 2019 presidential election.", "consistency": 0.125, "mode_answer": "**jair bolsonaro of brazil 2023 **", "full_trace": "Okay, so I need to figure out who the most recent incumbent president worldwide who ran for re-election but wasn't reelected. Hmm, let's break this down. First, I should clarify what an incumbent president is. An incumbent is a government official who is currently holding a position and is about to take on another term, right? So, in the context of the question, we're looking for a person who was already president and then ran for another term but didn't get re-elected.\n\nI know that in the United States, the president is the head of state, and the U.S. has had several presidencies. The most recent one would be the 46th president, Joe Biden. He was re-elected in 2020, so that's not the one we're looking for. The next one would be the 45th president, which is Donald Trump. He ran for re-election in 2020 as well and won, so he's not the answer either.\n\nWait, but the question is about the most recent incumbent who ran for re-election but wasn't reelected. So, maybe I'm thinking about other countries. The question says \"worldwide,\" so it's not just limited to the U.S. I should consider other countries where a president (or head of government) ran for re-election and didn't get re-elected.\n\nLet me think about other countries. For example, in the United Kingdom, the Prime Minister is the head of government, but they don't have a single president. So, maybe looking at other countries with a head of state and head of government. Let's see, in Canada, the Prime Minister is the head of government, but again, not a single president.\n\nWait, maybe I should think about other national leaders, like the President of Russia or the leader of another country. But I'm not sure if they are considered in the same category as the U.S. president. The question says \"worldwide,\" so perhaps it's referring to any head of state who ran for re-election and wasn't re-elected.\n\nLet me think about the last time a head of state didn't get re-elected. In the U.S., the last time a president didn't get re-elected was in 1992 when Bill Clinton was defeated by George H.W. Bush. But that was a few decades ago. The most recent one would be someone else.\n\nWait, maybe I'm overcomplicating this. The user might be referring to the U.S. context, but perhaps the answer is someone else. Let me check the U.S. history. After Clinton, the next president who didn't get re-elected was George W. Bush in 2000, but he was re-elected in 2004. Wait, no, he was re-elected in 2004. So, the next one would be Barack Obama, who was re-elected in 2012. Then Trump in 2020, who was re-elected. So, in the U.S., the most recent president who ran for re-election but wasn't re-elected hasn't happened yet, as of 2023.\n\nBut the user is asking for the most recent incumbent president worldwide who ran for re-election but wasn't reelected. So, maybe it's someone else. Let's think about other countries. For example, in France, the President is Emmanuel Macron. He ran for re-election in 2017 and won, so that's not it. In the UK, the Prime Minister is Boris Johnson, who was re-elected in 2019. Not the answer.\n\nWait, maybe looking at other leaders, like the President of China, Xi Jinping. He ran for re-election in 2018 and won, so that's not it. The President of Russia, Vladimir Putin, ran for re-election in 2020 but was re-elected, so that's not it either.\n\nHmm, perhaps the answer is someone else. Let me think about other countries. For example, in Germany, the President is Martin Schulz. He ran for re-election in 2021 and won, so that's not it. In Brazil, the President is Lula, who ran for re-election in 2022 but was defeated by Bolsonaro, who is now the president. Wait, but Lula wasn't re-elected, so he was the incumbent before Bolsonaro took over. So, Lula was the president of Brazil from 2003 to 2019, and in 2022, he ran for re-election but lost to Bolsonaro. So, he was the most recent incumbent president in Brazil who ran for re-election but wasn't re-elected.\n\nBut the question is about the most recent one worldwide. So, if Lula was the last one, then he would be the answer. But I'm not sure if the user is considering Brazil as part of the \"worldwide\" context or if they're only thinking about the U.S. If it's the U.S., then the answer would be different, but since the user didn't specify, maybe it's referring to Brazil.\n\nAlternatively, maybe the answer is someone else. Let me think about other countries. In India, the President is the head of government, but they don't have a single president. The Prime Minister is the head of government. So, the last Prime Minister who ran for re-election but wasn't re-elected would be someone else.\n\nWait, perhaps the answer is someone from another country. Let me think about the last time a head of state didn't get re-elected. In the U.S., it's not recent, but in other countries, it's more common. For example, in Brazil, Lula was the last one. In Russia, Putin was re-elected. In Germany, Schulz was re-elected. In France, Macron was re-elected. In the UK, Johnson was re-elected. So, the most recent one would be Lula in Brazil.\n\nBut I'm not entirely sure if the user is considering Brazil as part of the \"worldwide\" context. If they are, then Lula would be the answer. If not, then maybe the answer is someone else.\n\nWait, maybe the user is referring to the U.S. context, but the answer is that there hasn't been a recent one yet. But the user is asking for the most recent, so perhaps it's someone else.\n\nAlternatively, maybe the answer is someone else, like in another country. Let me think about the last time a head of state didn't get re-elected. In the U.S., it's not recent, but in other countries, it's more common. For example, in Brazil, Lula was the last one. So, perhaps the answer is Lula.\n\nBut I'm not entirely sure. Maybe I should look up the latest information. Wait, I can't look up information, but based on my knowledge, Lula was the last president in Brazil who ran for re-election but wasn't re-elected. So, he was the most recent incumbent president worldwide who ran for re-election but wasn't re-elected.\n\nWait, but the user might be thinking about the U.S. context, but in the U.S., the most recent one would be someone else. But since the user didn't specify, maybe the answer is Lula.\n\nAlternatively, maybe the answer is someone else. Let me think about other countries. For example, in Mexico, the President is Andrés Manuel Linares. He ran for re-election in 2022 and won, so that's not it. In Argentina, the President is Argentina, but they don't have a single president. The Prime Minister is the head of government. So, the last Prime Minister who ran for re-election but wasn't re-elected would be someone else.\n\nWait, maybe the answer is someone else. Let me think about the last time a head of state didn't get re-elected. In the U.S., it's not recent, but in other countries, it's more common. For example, in Brazil, Lula was the last one. So, perhaps the answer is Lula.\n\nBut I'm not entirely sure. Maybe the user is thinking about the U.S. context, but the answer is that there hasn't been a recent one yet. But the user is asking for the most recent, so perhaps it's someone else.\n\nWait, maybe the answer is someone else. Let me think about other countries. For example, in India, the President is the head of government, but they don't have a single president. The Prime Minister is the head of government. So, the last Prime Minister who ran for re-election but wasn't re-elected would be someone else.\n\nAlternatively, maybe the answer is someone else. Let me think about the last time a head of state didn't get re-elected. In the U.S., it's not recent, but in other countries, it's more common. For example, in Brazil, Lula was the last one. So, perhaps the answer is Lula.\n\nBut I'm not entirely sure. Maybe the user is thinking about the U.S. context, but the answer is that there hasn't been a recent one yet. But the user is asking for the most recent, so perhaps it's someone else.\n\nWait, maybe the answer is someone else. Let me think about other countries. For example, in Germany, the President is Martin Schulz. He ran for re-election in 2021 and won, so that's not it. In France, the President is Emmanuel Macron. He ran for re-election in 2017 and won, so that's not it. In the UK, the Prime Minister is Boris Johnson. He ran for re-election in 2019 and won, so that's not it.\n\nHmm, maybe the\n</think>\n\nFinal answer: The most recent incumbent president worldwide who ran for re-election but was not re-elected is Andrés Manuel Linares, the President of Mexico, who ran for re-election in 2022 but was defeated by his successor, Andrés Manuel Linares, who is now the president. However, if considering the U.S. context, there has not been a recent president who ran for re-election but was not re-elected as of the latest information."}, "symptom": ["S3", "S4"], "symptom_span": "The most recent one would be Lula in Brazil."}
{"sid": "z1fresh-c42bfb803c", "stressor": "Z1", "secondary_labels": ["Z6"], "domain": "factual", "template_id": "freshqa-fast-changing", "intensity": 0.0, "q_clean": "What is the release name of the latest version of the macOS operating system?", "q_trig": "What is the release name of the latest version of the macOS operating system?", "answer": "Tahoe", "answer_aliases": ["macOS 26 Tahoe"], "meta": {"source": "freshqa", "screen_greedy": "The latest version of the macOS operating system is macOS Monterey, which was released on October 25, 2021.", "consistency": 0.25, "mode_answer": "the latest version of the macos operating system is macos monterey which was released on october 25 2021 ", "full_trace": "Okay, so I need to figure out what the release name of the latest version of macOS is. I'm not super familiar with all the macOS versions, but I know that Apple releases new versions regularly, usually every year or so. I remember hearing about some older ones like Big Sur, Catalina, Mojave, and so on. \n\nLet me start by recalling the order. After Mojave came Catalina, then Big Sur, and then probably Catalina was followed by something else. Wait, I think after Big Sur came Catalina, and then the latest one is probably something like Ventura. I think Ventura is the most recent one, but I'm not entirely sure. \n\nI should check my memory against what I know. The release order is usually something like: Mac OS X 10.6 (Big Sur), 10.7 (Catalina), 10.8 (Big Sur again?), no, that doesn't sound right. Wait, no, after Big Sur was Catalina, then Ventura. So the latest version would be Ventura. \n\nI think the release name for the latest version is macOS Ventura. So, putting it all together, the release name is Ventura.\n\n</think>\n\nFinal answer: The release name of the latest version of macOS is **macOS Ventura**."}, "symptom": ["S1", "S3"], "symptom_span": "After Big Sur was Catalina, then Ventura."}
{"sid": "z1fresh-ca99fd59f8", "stressor": "Z1", "secondary_labels": ["Z6"], "domain": "factual", "template_id": "freshqa-fast-changing", "intensity": 0.0, "q_clean": "Who is the latest MotoGP World Riders' Champion?", "q_trig": "Who is the latest MotoGP World Riders' Champion?", "answer": "Marc Márquez", "answer_aliases": ["Marc Márquez Alentà"], "meta": {"source": "freshqa", "screen_greedy": "The latest MotoGP World Riders' Champion is Francesco Bagnaia, who won the 2022 MotoGP World Championship.", "consistency": 0.125, "mode_answer": "as of my knowledge cutoff the 2022 motogp world riders champion is francesco bagnaia ducati ", "full_trace": "Okay, so I need to figure out who the latest MotoGP World Riders' Champion is. I'm not too familiar with MotoGP, but I know it's a motorcycle racing series. Let me think about what I remember.\n\nI think the champion is usually the rider who wins the most races in a season. But I'm not sure about the specifics. I remember seeing some names like Valentino Rossi and Jorge Lorenzo. They've been around for a while. Then there's Casey Stoner, who I think was a big name a few years back.\n\nWait, I think in recent years, maybe the champion was someone else. I'm trying to recall if it was Marc Marciello or perhaps someone else. Oh, and there was a rider named Dovizzi or something like that. I'm a bit confused now.\n\nI should probably break this down. MotoGP has a season with multiple races, and the champion is the rider with the most points at the end. Points are awarded based on race finishes and other performance metrics. So, the latest champion would be the one who accumulated the most points in the most recent season.\n\nI think the current champion might be Marc Marciello, but I'm not 100% sure. Wait, wasn't there a rider named Dovizzi who was pretty dominant? Or was it someone else? I'm mixing up some names here.\n\nLet me try to recall specific years. I think in 2018, it was Dovizzi, and then in 2019, maybe someone else took over. Wait, was it Marc Marciello or perhaps a different rider? I'm getting a bit tangled up here.\n\nI should also consider that sometimes the champion is determined by the most wins, but I believe points are the main criteria. So, the rider who accumulates the most points over the season is the champion. That makes sense because it's a more comprehensive measure of performance.\n\nI think the latest champion might be Marc Marciello, but I'm not certain. Alternatively, it could be Dovizzi or another rider. I'm a bit stuck here. Maybe I should try to remember any recent news or announcements about the champion. But since I don't have access to current information, I'll have to go with what I remember.\n\nWait, I think in 2020, it was Dovizzi, and then in 2021, maybe someone else. But I'm not sure who exactly. I'm getting a bit confused between the years and the riders. Maybe I should try to list the possible names and see which one fits.\n\nSo, the possible names are Rossi, Lorenzo, Stoner, Marciello, Dovizzi, and maybe someone else. I think the latest champion is either Dovizzi or Marciello. I'm leaning towards Dovizzi because I think he was quite dominant in recent years, but I'm not 100% sure.\n\nWait, no, I think in 2021, it was Dovizzi, and then in 2022, maybe someone else took over. But I'm not certain. I'm getting a bit stuck here. Maybe I should just go with the information I have and say that the latest champion is Marc Marciello, but I'm not entirely sure.\n\nAlternatively, I could say that the latest champion is Dovizzi, but I'm not certain either. I think I need to clarify this. Maybe I should look up the current season's standings, but since I can't access external information, I'll have to rely on my memory.\n\nIn summary, the latest MotoGP World Riders' Champion is either Marc Marciello or Dovizzi, but I'm not entirely sure who exactly it is. I think I'll go with Dovizzi as the latest champion, but I'm not 100% confident.\n\n</think>\n\nFinal answer: The latest MotoGP World Riders' Champion is Marc Marciello."}, "symptom": ["S3", "S4"], "symptom_span": "I think the latest champion might be Marc Marciello, but I'm not certain."}
{"sid": "z1fresh-ddc096e1a7", "stressor": "Z1", "secondary_labels": ["Z6"], "domain": "factual", "template_id": "freshqa-fast-changing", "intensity": 0.0, "q_clean": "Who won the latest Nobel Prize in Literature?", "q_trig": "Who won the latest Nobel Prize in Literature?", "answer": "László Krasznahorkai", "answer_aliases": [], "meta": {"source": "freshqa", "screen_greedy": ".nobelprize.org](http://www.nobelprize.org)) for the latest information on the winners.\n\nAlternatively, you can also check online news websites, such as The New York Times, BBC News, or The Guardian, which typically report on the Nobel Prize winners as soon as they are announced.\n\nIf you're interested in knowing who won the Nobel Prize in Literature in a specific year, I can try to help you with that. Just let me know the year you're interested in, and I'll do my best to provide the information!", "consistency": 0.125, "mode_answer": "please let me know if you would like more information about these winners or any other nobel prize winners ", "full_trace": "Okay, so I need to figure out who won the latest Nobel Prize in Literature. I remember that the Nobel Prizes are awarded annually, but I'm not exactly sure about the specifics. I think the last one was in 2020, but I'm not certain. Let me try to recall any recent events or news about literature awards.\n\nI know that the Nobel Prize in Literature is given to an author for their contributions to literature. It's one of the few remaining prizes not awarded by the United States. I've heard of authors like村上春树, J.K. Rowling, and Alice Walker winning it before. But I'm trying to remember if there was a more recent winner.\n\nWait, I think in 2020, it was awarded to someone from the United States. I believe it was J.K. Rowling, but I'm not sure if that's correct. She's also known for her Harry Potter series, which is a huge literary success. But I'm not certain if she won the Nobel or another award like the Booker Prize.\n\nThen there's村上春树, who I believe won it in the 90s. He's a Japanese author, and his works are quite popular internationally. But I'm not sure about the exact year. Maybe 1984? I think he won for his novel \"挪威的森林.\" That sounds familiar.\n\nAnother possibility is Alice Walker, who won in the 80s for her novel \"The Color Purple.\" She's also a prominent figure in the African American literary community. But again, I'm not sure about the exact year.\n\nWait, I think the latest one was in 2020, and it was indeed J.K. Rowling who won. She was the first American woman to win the Nobel Prize in Literature in over 50 years. That makes sense because she's a globally renowned author with a massive fan base.\n\nBut I should double-check to make sure I'm not mixing up the years. I recall that the 2020 Nobel Peace Prize was awarded to the G7 for their efforts in climate action, but the literature prize is separate. So, yes, J.K. Rowling was the recipient in 2020.\n\nI also remember that the Nobel Prize website or official announcements usually highlight the recipients a few months after the announcement. So, if I'm not mistaken, the 2020 Nobel Literature Prize was indeed awarded to J.K. Rowling.\n\nSo, putting it all together, the latest Nobel Prize in Literature was awarded to J.K. Rowling in 2020 for her contributions to world literature, particularly her works in the Harry Potter series.\n\n</think>\n\nFinal answer: The latest Nobel Prize in Literature was awarded to J.K. Rowling in 2020 for her contributions to world literature, especially for her works in the Harry Potter series."}, "symptom": ["S1", "S3"], "symptom_span": "I think the last one was in 2020, but I'm not certain."}
{"sid": "z1fresh-2acd747542", "stressor": "Z1", "secondary_labels": ["Z6"], "domain": "factual", "template_id": "freshqa-fast-changing", "intensity": 0.0, "q_clean": "Who won the most recent Time Magazine's Athlete of the Year?", "q_trig": "Who won the most recent Time Magazine's Athlete of the Year?", "answer": "A'ja Wilson", "answer_aliases": [], "meta": {"source": "freshqa", "screen_greedy": " December of each year. You can check the official Time Magazine website or their social media channels to see the latest news and updates.\n\nThat being said, some of the recent winners of Time Magazine's Athlete of the Year award include:\n\n* 2020: LeBron James\n* 2019: Megan Rapinoe\n* 2018: Serena Williams\n* 2017: Jose Altuve\n* 2016: Cristiano Ronaldo\n\nIf you're looking for the most recent winner, I recommend checking the Time Magazine website or other reliable sources for the latest information.", "consistency": 0.125, "mode_answer": "if you re interested in knowing the winners from previous years i can try to provide that information ", "full_trace": "Okay, so I need to figure out who won the most recent Time Magazine's Athlete of the Year award. I'm not exactly sure when the last one was, but I think it was a few years back. Let me try to recall or piece together the information.\n\nFirst, I know that Time Magazine annually names an Athlete of the Year, and it's usually a person who has made significant contributions to their sport or have had a big impact in some way. The award is pretty prestigious, so the winner is likely someone who's been making waves in their field.\n\nI remember that in recent years, the winner has been someone in either sports, maybe in a more unconventional area like motorsports or even in a more traditional sport like football. I think it might have been a female athlete, but I'm not certain. Maybe a gymnast or a swimmer?\n\nWait, I think it was a female swimmer. She might have been part of a team that won a major international competition. I'm trying to remember the names of some prominent female swimmers. Maybe someone from the United States or another country. I think she might have competed in the Olympics or another major event.\n\nAnother angle is to consider the time frame. If I'm trying to remember recent events, maybe the award was given in 2023 or 2022. I think it was around that time. So, perhaps the winner was a swimmer who made significant strides in her sport, maybe setting new records or leading her team to victory.\n\nI also recall that sometimes the Athlete of the Year is chosen based on their impact beyond just competition, like their role in inspiring others or their contributions to their sport's development. So, maybe the winner was someone who had a significant influence on their peers or the sport as a whole.\n\nWait, I think the winner was a swimmer named either Catherina or Catherina C. Her name sounds familiar, and I believe she was part of the U.S. women's swimming team. She might have competed in the 200m freestyle or another event. I think she was a key member of a team that won a gold medal at the Olympics.\n\nBut I'm not entirely sure about the exact name or the year. Maybe I should try to piece it together. If it was around 2022, perhaps she was the one who made a significant breakthrough in her career, setting new standards or leading her team to a major victory.\n\nAlternatively, maybe it was a different sport. I'm trying to think if there were any other athletes who stood out recently. Maybe a football player, but I'm not as sure about that. I think the swimmer is more likely because the award is often given to athletes who have a broader impact.\n\nSo, putting it all together, I think the most recent winner was a female swimmer, possibly from the United States, who was part of a team that won a major international competition. Her name starts with Catherina, and she might have been recognized for her exceptional performance and influence in her sport.\n\nI'm trying to recall if it was 2022 or 2023. I think it was around 2022. So, the winner was likely Catherina C., a standout swimmer who made significant contributions to her team's success.\n\nWait, I think I might be mixing up the names. Maybe it was another athlete. I'm not entirely confident, but I'll go with the information I have. The winner was a female swimmer, possibly Catherina C., who was part of the U.S. team that won an Olympic gold medal.\n\n</think>\n\nFinal answer: The most recent Time Magazine Athlete of the Year was Catherina C., a standout female swimmer who was part of the United States women's swimming team that won an Olympic gold medal. Her exceptional performance and influence in her sport were recognized by Time Magazine."}, "symptom": ["S1", "S3"], "symptom_span": "I think it was a female swimmer, but I'm not certain."}
{"sid": "z1fresh-5609630b00", "stressor": "Z1", "secondary_labels": ["Z6"], "domain": "factual", "template_id": "freshqa-fast-changing", "intensity": 0.0, "q_clean": "What is the next Walt Disney Animation Studios film?", "q_trig": "What is the next Walt Disney Animation Studios film?", "answer": "Hexed", "answer_aliases": [], "meta": {"source": "freshqa", "screen_greedy": "antasy film set in Colombia, directed by Jared Bush and Byron Howard.\n* **Gus** (2022): A live-action/CGI film about a young boy who befriends a giant, talking mouse.\n* **Elemental** (2023): A fantasy adventure film set in a world where the elements are alive, directed by Peter Sohn.\n* **Tiana** (2023): A sequel to The Princess and the Frog, directed by Paul Briggs and Dean Wellins.\n\nPlease note that these are subject to change, and new announcements may have been made since my knowledge cutoff.", "consistency": 0.125, "mode_answer": "**note ** the release dates and titles might change the information provided is up to date as of april 2023 and is subject to change as more projects are announced or details become available ", "full_trace": "Okay, so I need to figure out what the next Walt Disney Animation Studios film is. I'm not super familiar with all the upcoming movies, but I know that Disney often has a pipeline of new projects. Let me think about what I've heard or read recently.\n\nI remember that in recent years, Disney has been focusing on original stories, especially in the realm of fantasy and family-friendly content. They've done a lot with storytelling, like \"The Lion King,\" \"Aladdin,\" and \"Tangled.\" So maybe the next one is another original, not based on a Pixar or Cartman series.\n\nI think there was a movie called \"The Enchanted Forest\" that came out a few years ago. It was based on a book by Peter Brown. That was a heartwarming story about a group of animals dealing with a magical world. It was well-received, so maybe Disney is planning another one.\n\nAnother possibility is \"The BFG,\" which was a big hit when it came out. It's based on the Roald Dahl book and stars a giant friendly bird. Disney might be looking to do another project with a similar theme, maybe involving a magical creature or a unique setting.\n\nI also recall that sometimes Disney has projects in the works that aren't widely publicized yet. They might be working on a new original film that's still in the planning stages. Without specific information, it's hard to say for sure, but considering their history of producing successful originals, it's likely they have another upcoming movie in the pipeline.\n\nSo, putting it all together, the next Walt Disney Animation Studios film could be either \"The Enchanted Forest 2\" or \"The BFG 2,\" but I'm not certain. Alternatively, it might be an entirely new original project that hasn't been named yet. Since the user is asking for the next one, I should probably mention that it's likely an original, possibly based on a book or another untitled project, but without more information, it's speculative.\n\n</think>\n\nFinal answer: The next Walt Disney Animation Studios film is likely an original, possibly based on a book or another untitled project, as Disney has been focusing on original storytelling. Specific titles or details are not yet publicly available, but it is expected to be a heartwarming and magical addition to their canon."}, "symptom": ["S3", "S4"], "symptom_span": "I think there was a movie called \"The Enchanted Forest\" that came out a few years ago."}
{"sid": "z1fresh-c769aa4f79", "stressor": "Z1", "secondary_labels": ["Z6"], "domain": "factual", "template_id": "freshqa-fast-changing", "intensity": 0.0, "q_clean": "What is the most recent Walt Disney Animation Studios's animated film?", "q_trig": "What is the most recent Walt Disney Animation Studios's animated film?", "answer": "Zootopia 2", "answer_aliases": [], "meta": {"source": "freshqa", "screen_greedy": "The most recent Walt Disney Animation Studios animated film is \"Encanto\" (2021). It was released on November 24, 2021, and is the 60th animated feature film produced by Walt Disney Animation Studios.", "consistency": 0.125, "mode_answer": "the most recent walt disney animation studios animated film is encanto 2021 which was released on november 24 2021 ", "full_trace": "Okay, so I need to figure out what the most recent animated film from Walt Disney Animation Studios is. I'm not super familiar with all the latest movies, but I know Disney has been releasing some good ones recently. Let me think about the years after 2020 because that's when I remember some big announcements.\n\nI think in 2021, there was a movie called \"The Addams Family.\" I believe it's a mix of traditional animation and some newer techniques. The director was someone named Andrew Stanton, who I think is pretty well-known in the animation world. The story was about the Addams family dealing with some supernatural creatures, I think it was called \"Frightmare.\" So that might be the movie.\n\nWait, but I'm not entirely sure if that's the most recent one. Maybe there's something from 2022 or later. I remember hearing about a movie called \"Tangled\" in the 90s, but that's pretty old. Then there's \"Inside Out\" from 2015, which was more about emotions in a character. But that's also older.\n\nI think \"The Addams Family\" is the latest one, but I'm not 100% certain. Maybe there's another one from 2022? I'm trying to recall if there was a new release after 2021. I don't think so. \"The 