{"sid": "z1fresh-29bf0f0d30", "stressor": "Z1", "secondary_labels": ["Z6"], "domain": "factual", "template_id": "freshqa-fast-changing", "intensity": 0.0, "q_clean": "What video game won the most recent Game Award for Game of the Year?", "q_trig": "What video game won the most recent Game Award for Game of the Year?", "answer": "Clair Obscur: Expedition 33", "answer_aliases": [], "meta": {"source": "freshqa", "screen_greedy": "ews websites: Websites like IGN, GameSpot, and Polygon often cover the Game Awards and provide updates on the winners.\n\nIf you're looking for the most recent Game of the Year winner, I can suggest some of the recent winners:\n\n* 2021: It Takes Two (developed by Hazelight Studios)\n* 2020: The Last of Us Part II (developed by Naughty Dog)\n* 2019: Sekiro: Shadows Die Twice (developed by FromSoftware)\n\nPlease let me know if you have any other questions or if there's anything else I can help you with!", "consistency": 0.125, "mode_answer": "the most recent game awards ceremony was the 8th annual the game awards which took place on december 9 2022 the game of the year award was won by elden ring developed by fromsoftware ", "full_trace": "Okay, so I need to figure out which video game won the most recent Game of the Year award. I'm not super familiar with all the latest awards, but I know that the Game Awards are a big deal in the gaming industry. Let me try to break this down step by step.\n\nFirst, I should probably check when the Game Awards are typically held. I think they're usually in December, like around Christmas time. So, the most recent one would be the one held in December 2023. I remember hearing about some big games being announced around that time.\n\nI'm trying to recall some of the big games from 2023. There's a game called \"The Last of Us Part 2,\" but I think that was actually released in 2022, so maybe it's not the most recent. Then there's \"The Witcher 4: Wild Hunt,\" which I believe came out in 2022 as well. Wait, but I think the Game Awards for 2023 might have been held before the games were released, so maybe the winners are from 2023.\n\nI'm trying to think of other big games. There's \"God of War Ragnarök,\" which came out in 2023. I think that might be a strong contender. Also, \"Outer Wilds!\" is another one I've heard about; it's a space adventure game. Then there's \"The Last of Us Part 3,\" which is the next in the series after Part 2, so that's probably from 2023.\n\nI'm not sure which of these would win. I know that the Game Awards consider multiple platforms, including PC, consoles, and handhelds. So, the winner could be a game from any of these platforms. I think \"God of War Ragnarök\" is really popular, especially for its story and gameplay. But I'm not certain if it's the Game of the Year.\n\nAnother possibility is \"Outer Wilds!\" because it's a new take on the classic space exploration games. It's got a lot of buzz and seems like it might have a strong year. \"The Last of Us Part 3\" is also a big one, but I'm not sure if it's more deserving of the award than the others.\n\nI should also consider other games. Maybe \"Stardew Valley\" is a possibility, but I think that's more of a farming sim and might not be considered a mainline game anymore. \"The Legend of Zelda: Breath of the Wild\" is a classic, but it's been around for a while, so probably not the recent Game of the Year.\n\nWait, I think I remember hearing that \"God of War Ragnarök\" won the Game of the Year award at the Game Awards in December 2023. That makes sense because it's a highly anticipated game with a great story and challenging gameplay. Plus, it's a big title that's been getting a lot of praise from critics and fans.\n\nSo, putting it all together, the most recent Game of the Year award likely went to \"God of War Ragnarök.\" It's from 2023, and considering its popularity and critical acclaim, it's a strong contender. I don't think any other game from 2023 has surpassed it in terms of recognition and awards.\n\n</think>\n\nFinal answer: The most recent Game of the Year award was won by \"God of War Ragnarök.\" This game, released in 2023, was recognized for its exceptional storytelling and challenging gameplay, solidifying its status as a standout title in the industry."}, "symptom": ["S1", "S3"], "symptom_span": "I think 'God of War Ragnarök' won the Game of the Year award at the Game Awards in December 2023."}
{"sid": "z1fresh-934a919e3e", "stressor": "Z1", "secondary_labels": [], "domain": "factual", "template_id": "freshqa-fast-changing", "intensity": 0.0, "q_clean": "When did the latest NFL season begin?", "q_trig": "When did the latest NFL season begin?", "answer": "Sep 4, 2025", "answer_aliases": ["September 4, 2025", "4 Sep 2025", "4 September 2025", "09/4/2025", "09-4-2025", "4/09/2025", "4-09-2025", "2025/09/4", "2025-09-4"], "meta": {"source": "freshqa", "screen_greedy": "ble sources for the most recent information.\n\nThat being said, the 2022 NFL season began with the following games:\n\n* Thursday Night Football: Kansas City Chiefs at Arizona Cardinals on September 8, 2022\n* Sunday Night Football: Los Angeles Rams at Buffalo Bills on September 8, 2022\n* Monday Night Football: Pittsburgh Steelers at Cincinnati Bengals on September 12, 2022\n\nPlease note that the NFL season typically runs from September to February, with the Super Bowl being played in early February.", "consistency": 0.125, "mode_answer": "please note that the nfl season may start earlier for preseason games which typically begin in late july or early august ", "full_trace": "Okay, so I need to figure out when the latest NFL season began. I'm not exactly sure, but I know that the NFL seasons usually start in the fall, around September. I remember hearing that the 2023 season started in early September, but I'm not certain about the exact date. Maybe September 10th? I think that's when the season opener was. \n\nWait, but sometimes the start date can vary. I should check if there were any changes due to the COVID-19 pandemic or other events. I recall that the 2020 season was shortened because of the pandemic, but I don't think that affected the start date much. So, probably, the 2023 season started around the same time as previous years, maybe early September.\n\nI also remember that the NFL typically has two seasons, the regular season and the playoffs. The regular season has 17 weeks, and the playoffs start right after the regular season ends. So, if the regular season starts in early September, it would end around mid-December, and then the playoffs would begin in January. \n\nBut I'm not entirely sure about the exact start date. Maybe I should think about when the previous season started. If the 2022 season started in early September, then 2023 would follow the same timeline. I think the 2022 season started on September 11, so the 2023 season would start a few days later, maybe September 10th. That makes sense because September 11 is a significant date, and they might have spaced it out a bit.\n\nI should also consider if there were any delays or changes in the scheduling due to other factors, like the NFL trying to fit more games in or any organizational changes. But I don't recall any major changes affecting the start date. So, putting it all together, the latest NFL season, which is 2023, began in early September, probably September 10th.\n\n</think>\n\nFinal answer: The 2023 NFL season began on September 10, 2023."}, "symptom": ["S1", "S3"], "symptom_span": "I think the 2022 season started on September 11, so the 2023 season would start a few days later, maybe September 10th."}
{"sid": "z1fresh-9b45dbd9ac", "stressor": "Z1", "secondary_labels": [], "domain": "factual", "template_id": "freshqa-fast-changing", "intensity": 0.0, "q_clean": "How many undergraduate students enrolled in Reed College in the most recent fall semester?", "q_trig": "How many undergraduate students enrolled in Reed College in the most recent fall semester?", "answer": "1267", "answer_aliases": [], "meta": {"source": "freshqa", "screen_greedy": "I don't have access to real-time data or the most current information on the number of undergraduate students enrolled in Reed College for the most recent fall semester. For the most accurate and up-to-date information, I recommend checking directly with Reed College's official website or contacting their admissions office. They should be able to provide you with the most current enrollment figures.", "consistency": 0.125, "mode_answer": "i don t have the most current information on the number of undergraduate students enrolled in reed college for the most recent fall semester for the most accurate and up-to-date information i recommend checking the college s official website or contacting their admissions office directly ", "full_trace": "Okay, so I need to figure out how many undergraduate students were enrolled at Reed College in the most recent fall semester. I'm not exactly sure where to start, but I'll try to break it down step by step.\n\nFirst, I know that Reed College is a private university located in Portland, Oregon. It's known for being a small liberal arts college, so I imagine it doesn't have as many students as larger universities. But I'm not certain about the exact numbers.\n\nI remember hearing that Reed College has a pretty selective admission process, so maybe it doesn't have a huge student body. I think they might have around 1,000 students, but I'm not sure if that's accurate. I should check if there's any recent information available.\n\nI could look up Reed College's official website. They usually have a section about enrollment numbers. Let me try to recall if I've seen any statistics there before. I think the number is somewhere in the 1,200 range. Maybe 1,234 students? I'm not entirely sure, but that number seems familiar.\n\nAnother way to approach this is to think about other similar colleges. For example, schools like Stanford have over 10,000 students, but Reed is much smaller. Maybe schools like Pomona College or Carleton College have around 1,000 students each. So, Reed being a smaller institution, 1,200 seems plausible.\n\nI also remember that Reed College offers a variety of programs, which might attract a diverse student body. However, despite being selective, they might not have as many students as, say, a state university. So, 1,200 seems like a reasonable estimate.\n\nWait, I think I heard somewhere that Reed College's enrollment is around 1,234. That number sounds specific enough to be accurate. I should probably go with that unless I have evidence to the contrary.\n\nTo make sure, I could cross-reference this with other sources. Maybe the U.S. News & World Report or other educational statistics websites. But since I don't have access to the internet right now, I'll have to rely on my memory. I think the number is correct, but I'm a bit uncertain. However, given the context, 1,234 seems like a solid estimate for the most recent fall semester.\n\n</think>\n\nFinal answer: Reed College enrolled approximately 1,234 undergraduate students in the most recent fall semester."}, "symptom": ["S1", "S3"], "symptom_span": "I think the number is correct, but I'm a bit uncertain. However, given the context, 1,234 seems like a solid estimate for the most recent fall semester."}
{"sid": "z1fresh-f6d310bd70", "stressor": "Z1", "secondary_labels": ["Z6"], "domain": "factual", "template_id": "freshqa-fast-changing", "intensity": 0.0, "q_clean": "Who won the latest Ballon D'or?", "q_trig": "Who won the latest Ballon D'or?", "answer": "Dembélé", "answer_aliases": ["Ousmane Dembélé", "Masour Ousmane Dembélé"], "meta": {"source": "freshqa", "screen_greedy": "on the award on October 17, 2022, at the Théâtre du Châtelet in Paris, France.\n\nBenzema received the award for his outstanding performance in the 2021-22 season, during which he scored 44 goals in 46 appearances for Real Madrid and helped the team win the La Liga title. He also scored 10 goals in 16 appearances for France in the 2022 FIFA World Cup qualifying campaign.\n\nThis was Benzema's first Ballon d'Or award, and he became the first French player to win the award since Thierry Henry in 2008.", "consistency": 0.125, "mode_answer": "the latest ballon d or winner is lionel messi he won the award in 2021 marking his seventh ballon d or title ", "full_trace": "Okay, so I need to figure out who won the latest Ballon d'Or. I'm not exactly sure what the Ballon d'Or is, but I think it's a football award. Maybe it's like the most prestigious award in soccer? I remember hearing about it in the news sometimes. Let me try to recall.\n\nI think it's given to the best player in the world football (soccer) tournament, maybe the FIFA World Cup. That makes sense because the World Cup is the biggest event in football. So, the Ballon d'Or would be the top individual award for that tournament.\n\nNow, who usually wins that? I know that the top players from each country compete, and they're judged based on their performance throughout the tournament. It's not just about one game; it's about the whole season or tournament. So, it's a very competitive award.\n\nI'm trying to remember if it's been won by a European player or an American one. I think recently, maybe in the early 2020s, an American player won it. Wait, wasn't it someone like Robert Lewandowski? I think he's from Poland, but he plays for a European team. Or was it someone else?\n\nWait, no, maybe it was someone else. I'm a bit confused. Let me think. I believe the Ballon d'Or was won by a player from either Brazil, Germany, or maybe Spain. Oh, wait, maybe it was Lautaro Martínez from Argentina? No, that doesn't sound right.\n\nHold on, I think it was an American player, Justinianiguil, but I'm not sure. Or maybe it was someone else. I'm getting a bit mixed up here. Maybe I should try to break it down.\n\nFirst, the Ballon d'Or is the best player award in the FIFA World Cup. So, the winner is the top scorer or the most valuable player of the tournament. The award is named after a French footballer, hence the 'd'Or' which is French for gold.\n\nNow, to find out who won the latest one, I need to know the most recent World Cup. I think the last one was in 2022, right? So, the 2022 FIFA World Cup. Who won that?\n\nI remember that the 2022 World Cup was held in Qatar. The host country, Qatar, won the tournament, but the Ballon d'Or was awarded to a player, not the team. So, who was that?\n\nI think it was an Argentinian player, maybe Lautaro Martínez. Wait, no, I think it was someone else. Let me think about the players who stood out. There was a lot of talk about someone named Robert Lewandowski, but I think he was with a European team, maybe Chelsea or something. But was he the Ballon d'Or winner?\n\nWait, no, I think the winner was an American player. Maybe it was someone like Weston Brown or Justinianiguil. I'm not sure. Alternatively, maybe it was a player from France or Germany.\n\nWait, I think I remember that in the 2022 World Cup, the Ballon d'Or was won by an Argentinian striker named Lautaro Martínez. But I'm not 100% sure. Alternatively, it might have been someone else.\n\nLet me try to recall the key players. The top scorers were Lautaro Martínez with 17 goals, and maybe someone else with 16. But the Ballon d'Or is not just about goals; it's about overall performance, including assists, leadership, and impact on the team.\n\nI think the winner was Lautaro Martínez because he was a very consistent player throughout the tournament. He scored a lot of goals and was a key player for Argentina. So, maybe he won the Ballon d'Or.\n\nAlternatively, I've heard that in some tournaments, the winner is determined by a combination of on-field performance and public voting, but I think in the FIFA World Cup, it's based on the official voting by the organizing committee and the players' associations.\n\nWait, no, I think the Ballon d'Or is awarded by the FIFA, so it's based on the official voting. So, the player with the highest points from the voting panels gets it.\n\nSo, if Lautaro Martínez was the top scorer, but someone else had higher overall points, maybe that's the case. Alternatively, maybe it was someone else.\n\nI'm getting a bit stuck here. Maybe I should think about other recent winners. I think in 2021, maybe someone from Brazil won it, but I'm not sure.\n\nWait, I think the 2022 World Cup was won by Qatar, but the Ballon d'Or was awarded to an Argentinian player, Lautaro Martínez. So, that might be the latest one.\n\nAlternatively, maybe it was someone else. I'm not entirely certain, but I think Lautaro Martínez is a strong candidate.\n\nWait, I just did a quick check in my mind, and I think the winner was indeed Lautaro Martínez. He was the top scorer and was a key player for Argentina, so he likely won the Ballon d'Or.\n\nSo, putting it all together, the latest Ballon d'Or was won by Lautaro Martínez of Argentina in the 2022 FIFA World Cup.\n\n</think>\n\nFinal answer: The latest Ballon d'Or was won by Lautaro Martínez of Argentina in the 2022 FIFA World Cup."}, "symptom": ["S1", "S3"], "symptom_span": "I think the 2022 World Cup was won by Qatar, but the Ballon d'Or was awarded to an Argentinian player, Lautaro Martínez."}
