{"sid": "z1fresh-9c8ab71ed4", "stressor": "Z1", "secondary_labels": ["Z6"], "domain": "factual", "template_id": "freshqa-fast-changing", "intensity": 0.0, "q_clean": "Who was the guest of honor at the most recent state dinner hosted by the President of the United States?", "q_trig": "Who was the guest of honor at the most recent state dinner hosted by the President of the United States?", "answer": "Mohammed bin Salman", "answer_aliases": [], "meta": {"source": "freshqa", "screen_greedy": "e or a news article about the most recent state dinner.\n2. Look for news articles: You can search online for news articles from reputable sources such as The New York Times, CNN, or Fox News to see if they have reported on the most recent state dinner.\n3. Check social media: You can also check the official social media accounts of the White House or the President's personal account to see if they have posted about the state dinner.\n\nI hope this helps! Let me know if you have any other questions.", "consistency": 0.25, "mode_answer": "to your question ", "full_trace": "Okay, so I need to figure out who was the guest of honor at the most recent state dinner hosted by the President of the United States. Hmm, I'm not exactly sure about the current or recent details, but I can try to recall or reason it out.\n\nFirst, I know that state dinners are usually held to honor foreign leaders, often as a gesture of friendship and good relations between the two countries. The President typically invites the head of state from the other country, along with their immediate family members, to attend the dinner.\n\nI remember that recently, Joe Biden, the President of the United States, hosted a state dinner. I think it was for a foreign leader, maybe a recent one. I'm trying to recall if it was with a British or another European leader. Wait, I think it was with the King of the Netherlands, but I'm not entirely sure. Alternatively, it could have been with a different leader.\n\nWait, I think it was actually with the King of the Netherlands, but I'm not 100% certain. I should verify that. Also, I'm trying to remember if there were any other notable guests. Maybe the President's children were there as well, as is customary.\n\nAnother thought: sometimes, the guest of honor might be a foreign leader's spouse or a prominent figure in their country. But in the case of state dinners, usually, it's the head of state and their family.\n\nI'm a bit confused because I might be mixing up the details with other events. For example, I think there was a state dinner with the Queen of England, but that might have been a different one. Or maybe it was with a different leader, like the King of Spain or another European monarch.\n\nWait, I think it was indeed the King of the Netherlands. I recall that Biden had a significant relationship with the Netherlands, and the dinner was a way to strengthen their bilateral ties. So, the guest of honor would have been the King of the Netherlands, along with his family, perhaps including his wife and children.\n\nTo make sure, I should think about the context. The state dinner is usually a formal event, and the guest of honor is the head of state. So, if Biden hosted a dinner, the guest would be the head of state from another country, likely a European one given the current administration's focus on international relations.\n\nI think I'm fairly confident that the guest of honor was the King of the Netherlands, but I'm not 100% sure. I might be mixing it up with another recent event. Alternatively, it could have been with a different leader, but I can't recall the exact name right now.\n\nIn any case, the key points are that it's the President of the United States hosting a state dinner, the guest of honor is the head of state from another country, likely a European leader, and possibly their spouse and children attending.\n\nSo, putting it all together, I believe the guest of honor was the King of the Netherlands, attended by his family, including his wife and children, at the most recent state dinner hosted by President Biden.\n\n</think>\n\nFinal answer: The guest of honor at the most recent state dinner hosted by President Joe Biden was the King of the Netherlands, attended by his wife and children."}, "symptom": ["S1", "S3"], "symptom_span": "I think it was with the King of the Netherlands, but I'm not entirely sure."}
{"sid": "z1fresh-d50991b0b2", "stressor": "Z1", "secondary_labels": ["Z6"], "domain": "factual", "template_id": "freshqa-fast-changing", "intensity": 0.0, "q_clean": "What album holds the record for the most Spotify streams reached in a single day?", "q_trig": "What album holds the record for the most Spotify streams reached in a single day?", "answer": "The Tortured Poets Department", "answer_aliases": [], "meta": {"source": "freshqa", "screen_greedy": "I don't have the most current information on the album that holds the record for the most Spotify streams reached in a single day. Records like these can change frequently due to the dynamic nature of music streaming and the constant release of new content. For the most accurate and up-to-date information, I recommend checking the latest news from reputable sources such as Spotify's official blog, music industry publications, or the artist's official social media channels.", "consistency": 0.125, "mode_answer": "but the record that still stands is held by taylor swift s album midnights was actually broken by taylor swift s own album midnights 3am edition with 106 1 million streams in a 24-hour period achieved in 2022 ", "full_trace": "Okay, so I need to figure out which album holds the record for the most Spotify streams in a single day. I'm not too familiar with music streaming records, but I know that Spotify has a lot of data, so maybe there's an album that went viral or something. \n\nFirst, I should probably think about what causes a lot of streams. Viral songs or albums often spike in streams because people are talking about them or they're trending on social media. Maybe something from a big artist or a popular collaboration.\n\nI remember hearing about some records related to streams. I think there was an album by Taylor Swift that went viral, but I'm not sure if it's the most streamed. Maybe it's something more recent. I also recall that sometimes very short-lived songs or albums can get a lot of streams because they're only available for a short time.\n\nWait, I think there was an album called \"Midnight\" by Billie Eilish. I believe that was a big deal because it was released in 2019, and it had a lot of hype. Maybe that's the one. Or was it something else?\n\nAnother thought: maybe it's a mixtape or an EP that's very short but impactful. Sometimes those can get a lot of streams quickly. I think there was an album by Dua Lipa called \"Dua\" that was released in 2020. I'm not sure if that's the record holder.\n\nI should also consider the time frame. Spotify's records might be updated regularly, so the most recent one could be from the past few years. I think the record might have been set in 2021 or 2022. Maybe an album by a big artist like Drake or Taylor Swift?\n\nWait, I think I remember something about an album by Billie Eilish called \"Midnight.\" It was released in 2019, and I believe it had over 100 million streams in a day. That seems high. Or was it even higher? Maybe it's the record.\n\nAlternatively, there's an album by Doja Cat called \"The Party\" that came out in 2020. I think that one also had a lot of streams. I'm not sure which one is higher.\n\nI should also check if there are any official sources or articles that mention this. I recall reading somewhere that \"Midnight\" by Billie Eilish was the most streamed album in a day, with over 100 million streams. That might be the case.\n\nAnother possibility is an album by a different artist, maybe a mixtape by someone like Megan Thee Stallion or Cardi B. Those could have a lot of streams because they're very popular and widely covered.\n\nBut I think the most likely candidate is \"Midnight\" by Billie Eilish because it's a well-known album with a lot of hype and it was released in a year when streaming was growing rapidly. Plus, the number of streams in a day being over 100 million seems really high, but I think that's accurate.\n\nSo, putting it all together, I think the album that holds the record for the most Spotify streams in a single day is \"Midnight\" by Billie Eilish, with over 100 million streams on a particular day in 2019.\n\n</think>\n\nFinal answer: The album that holds the record for the most Spotify streams in a single day is \"Midnight\" by Billie Eilish, which reached over 100 million streams on September 28, 2019."}, "symptom": ["S3", "S1"], "symptom_span": "I think the most likely candidate is 'Midnight' by Billie Eilish because it's a well-known album with a lot of hype and it was released in a year when streaming was growing rapidly."}
{"sid": "z1fresh-92913d1bea", "stressor": "Z1", "secondary_labels": ["Z6"], "domain": "factual", "template_id": "freshqa-fast-changing", "intensity": 0.0, "q_clean": "Who is the number 1 ranked female tennis player in the world?", "q_trig": "Who is the number 1 ranked female tennis player in the world?", "answer": "Aryna Sabalenka", "answer_aliases": ["Aryna Siarhiejeŭna Sabalenka"], "meta": {"source": "freshqa", "screen_greedy": "As of my last update in April 2023, the number 1 ranked female tennis player in the world is Iga Świątek from Poland. However, please note that rankings can change frequently due to ongoing tournaments and competitions. For the most up-to-date information, I recommend checking the official Women's Tennis Association (WTA) website or other reliable sports news sources.", "consistency": 0.125, "mode_answer": "the ranking of the number 1 female tennis player in the world can change frequently as it is based on the wta women s tennis association rankings which are updated every week however as of my last update in april 2023 the number 1 ranked female tennis player in the world is iga świątek from poland she is a young and talented player who has been on a tear in recent years winning several grand slam titles and holding the top spot in the wta rankings for many weeks ", "full_trace": "Okay, so I need to figure out who the number 1 ranked female tennis player in the world is. I'm not too familiar with tennis rankings, but I know that the top spots are usually held by a few big names. I remember that Serena Williams was number 1 for a long time, but I think she's not the only one. Maybe someone else has been at the top recently.\n\nI think the rankings are updated regularly, so it's possible that someone else is now number 1. I've heard of Maria Sharapova, but I'm not sure if she's still in the top 10. Maybe someone like Simona Halep or maybe even a younger player like Iga Swiatek? I'm not sure about their current standings.\n\nI should probab