{"sid": "z1fresh-980eaae7c7", "stressor": "Z1", "secondary_labels": [], "domain": "factual", "template_id": "freshqa-fast-changing", "intensity": 0.0, "q_clean": "How many goals did Bukayo Saka score in the most recent match between Arsenal and Liverpool?", "q_trig": "How many goals did Bukayo Saka score in the most recent match between Arsenal and Liverpool?", "answer": "0", "answer_aliases": ["zero"], "meta": {"source": "freshqa", "screen_greedy": "r:\n\n1. Check the official Arsenal or Liverpool website for the latest match reports and statistics.\n2. Look for sports news websites or apps, such as BBC Sport, Sky Sports, or ESPN, which often provide up-to-date information on recent matches.\n3. Check social media platforms, such as Twitter or Instagram, for updates from the teams, players, or sports journalists.\n\nIf you provide me with more context or information about the match you're referring to, I'll do my best to help you find the answer.", "consistency": 0.125, "mode_answer": "1 check the official premier league website or arsenal s website for the latest match results and statistics ", "full_trace": "Okay, so I need to figure out how many goals Bukayo Saka scored in the most recent match between Arsenal and Liverpool. Hmm, I'm not exactly sure about the current standings or the latest updates, but I'll try to think through this step by step.\n\nFirst, I know that Bukayo Saka is a footballer who plays for Arsenal. He's been in the news a lot recently because of his performance and maybe some controversy. I remember he had a goal in a recent match, but I'm not sure which one. I think it might have been against Liverpool because those two teams often have high-scoring matches.\n\nI should probably check the most recent fixtures. Maybe I can recall that Arsenal played Liverpool a few weeks ago. I think it was a Premier League game. In that match, I believe Arsenal ended up winning, but I'm not certain about the scoreline. Was it 2-1 or 3-1? I think it was a 2-1 win for Arsenal, but I'm not sure if that's the most recent one.\n\nWait, maybe there's a more recent match. I'm trying to remember if there was a friendly or a cup game where Saka scored. Oh, maybe the FA Cup? I think there was a game where Arsenal played against a lower division team, and Saka scored a goal. But I'm not sure if that's the most recent one either.\n\nI should also consider that sometimes players can score in training matches or friendlies, but those aren't official league games. So, I'm focusing on the official matches. I think the most recent league game was against Liverpool, but I'm not certain about the exact score or the date.\n\nAnother thought: maybe I can recall any news articles or social media posts about Saka's recent performance. I think there was some talk about him being named Man of the Match, which usually indicates a significant contribution, possibly a goal. If he was Man of the Match, that suggests he scored a goal.\n\nWait, I think in the most recent match, Arsenal beat Liverpool 2-1. Saka scored the opener, and maybe there was another goal for Arsenal but not for Liverpool. So, he might have scored one goal. But I'm not 100% sure about the exact score or the match details.\n\nI should also consider that sometimes players can score in the same match but not necessarily in the most recent one. Maybe there's a more recent match where he scored again. I'm trying to remember if there was a Champions League or another competition where he scored. But I think the most recent official match was in the Premier League against Liverpool.\n\nPutting it all together, I think Bukayo Saka scored one goal in the most recent match between Arsenal and Liverpool, which was a 2-1 win for Arsenal. But I'm not entirely certain about the exact details, so I might need to verify this information to be sure.\n\n</think>\n\nFinal answer: Bukayo Saka scored one goal in the most recent match between Arsenal and Liverpool, contributing to a 2-1 victory for Arsenal in the Premier League."}, "symptom": ["S3", "S4"], "symptom_span": "I think it might have been against Liverpool because those two teams often have high-scoring matches."}
{"sid": "z1fresh-df3f2be283", "stressor": "Z1", "secondary_labels": [], "domain": "factual", "template_id": "freshqa-fast-changing", "intensity": 0.0, "q_clean": "What's the current Tomatometer score of the most recent season of The Lord of the Rings: The Rings of Power on Rotten Tomatoes?", "q_trig": "What's the current Tomatometer score of the most recent season of The Lord of the Rings: The Rings of Power on Rotten Tomatoes?", "answer": "85%", "answer_aliases": ["84"], "meta": {"source": "freshqa", "screen_greedy": "e most recent season of The Lord of the Rings: The Rings of Power on Rotten Tomatoes.\n\nYou can check the Rotten Tomatoes website directly or use a search engine like Google to find the latest reviews and ratings for the show. You can also check other review aggregation websites like Metacritic or IMDb to get a more comprehensive view of the show's reception.\n\nPlease note that the Tomatometer score can change over time as more reviews are added, so the score may not be the same when you check it.", "consistency": 0.125, "mode_answer": "i can’t verify the current tomatometer score for the most recent season of the lord of the rings the rings of power on rotten tomatoes ", "full_trace": "Okay, so I need to figure out the current Tomatometer score for the most recent season of The Lord of the Rings: The Rings of Power on Rotten Tomatoes. Hmm, I'm not exactly sure where to start, but I'll try to break it down.\n\nFirst, I know that Tomatometer is a rating system used by Rotten Tomatoes to show how well a movie is doing based on audience reviews. It's usually a percentage, with higher numbers meaning better reviews. The show in question is The Lord of the Rings: The Rings of Power, which is a prequel to the original Lord of the Rings movies.\n\nNow, the user is asking about the \"most recent season.\" I think that means the latest episodes that have been released or are currently airing. I'm not sure how many seasons there are, but I believe there are at least three seasons, each consisting of several episodes. I'm not certain about the exact number of episodes per season, but I think each season has around 10-12 episodes.\n\nI remember that Tomatometer scores can change over time as more reviews come in. So, if the most recent season is, say, season 3, the Tomatometer score might not be final yet because more episodes could be coming out. I should check if all episodes of the current season have been released and have reviews from critics and audience members.\n\nI also need to consider that Rotten Tomatoes might not have all the reviews for a show as of a specific date. Sometimes, shows have seasons that are still ongoing, and not all episodes have been reviewed yet. So, the Tomatometer score might not be available until all episodes have been released and reviewed.\n\nAnother thing to think about is whether the Tomatometer score for the show as a whole or per episode is being referred to here. The user mentioned \"the most recent season,\" so I think they're asking for the overall score for that season, not individual episodes.\n\nI should also consider that Tomatometer scores can vary depending on the source, whether it's from Rotten Tomatoes, other websites, or official sources. But since the user specifically mentioned Rotten Tomatoes, I should focus on their system.\n\nTo get the most accurate information, I would need to go to the Rotten Tomatoes website and look up The Lord of the Rings: The Rings of Power. Then, navigate to the most recent season and check the Tomatometer score. However, since I can't browse the web, I'll have to rely on my existing knowledge.\n\nI recall that The Lord of the Rings: The Rings of Power had a mixed reception. Some episodes were well-received, while others were criticized for being too slow or lacking the depth of the original movies. This could affect the Tomatometer score, as audience reviews can swing the percentage up or down.\n\nI think the Tomatometer score for the show might be around the mid-60s or so, but I'm not entirely sure. It's possible that the score is still in flux as more episodes are released and reviewed. Also, the score might be influenced by the number of reviews each episode gets. Some episodes might have more critical acclaim, pulling the overall score up, while others might not, bringing it down.\n\nAnother factor is the timing of the release. If the most recent season is still airing, the Tomatometer score might not have been finalized yet. Rotten Tomatoes often updates scores as more reviews come in, so the score could change over time.\n\nI should also consider that the Tomatometer score is an average of all the reviews, both positive and negative. If the audience is split on the show, the score might not be extremely high or low. Maybe around 65-70%? I'm not certain, but that seems plausible.\n\nIn summary, without checking the current Rotten Tomatoes page, it's hard to give an exact number, but I can estimate that the Tomatometer score for the most recent season of The Lord of the Rings: The Rings of Power is likely in the mid-60s, possibly around 67%. However, this could change as more episodes are reviewed and released.\n\n</think>\n\nFinal answer: The current Tomatometer score for the most recent season of The Lord of the Rings: The Rings of Power on Rotten Tomatoes is estimated to be around 67%. This score is an average of audience reviews, which may fluctuate as more episodes are released and reviewed."}, "symptom": ["S1", "S3"], "symptom_span": "The Lord of the Rings: The Rings of Power had a mixed reception."}
{"sid": "z1fresh-30c7ed36c5", "stressor": "Z1", "secondary_labels": ["Z6"], "domain": "factual", "template_id": "freshqa-fast-changing", "intensity": 0.0, "q_clean": "What's the current audience score of the most recent season of The Lord of the Rings: The Rings of Power on Rotten Tomatoes?", "q_trig": "What's the current audience score of the most recent season of The Lord of the Rings: The Rings of Power on Rotten Tomatoes?", "answer": "58%", "answer_aliases": ["59"], "meta": {"source": "freshqa", "screen_greedy": "rrent audience score of the most recent season of The Lord of the Rings: The Rings of Power on Rotten Tomatoes.\n\nYou can check the Rotten Tomatoes website directly for the most up-to-date information. Alternatively, you can also check other review aggregation websites such as Metacritic or IMDB to see the current audience score.\n\nIf you'd like, I can provide you with the initial audience score of the first season of The Lord of the Rings: The Rings of Power, which was released in September 2022.", "consistency": 0.125, "mode_answer": "please note that audience scores can change over time as more people watch and rate the show so the score may not be the same when you check it ", "full_trace": "Okay, so I need to figure out the current audience score of the most recent season of The Lord of the Rings: The Rings of Power on Rotten Tomatoes. Hmm, I'm not exactly sure where to start, but I'll try to break it down.\n\nFirst, I know that The Lord of the Rings: The Rings of Power is a TV series, and Rotten Tomatoes (RT) is a website that aggregates movie and TV critic reviews. They assign scores based on audience and critic reviews. The question is about the most recent season, so I need to confirm when that was. I think the series ended in 2022, so the most recent season would be the third season, which I believe was released in 2022.\n\nNow, to find the current RT score, I should probably check the Rotten Tomatoes website. But since I can't browse the web right now, I'll have to rely on my existing knowledge or any information I can recall. I remember that Rotten Tomatoes scores are usually a combination of audience and critic scores, with the audience score being the most significant. \n\nI think the series has been well-received, especially the third season. I recall that the third season, which is the most recent, had some controversy, like the abrupt ending. That might have affected the audience's perception. However, many viewers still found it compelling. \n\nI'm not sure about the exact score, but I think the audience score for the third season is around the mid-70s. Critics might have mixed opinions, but the audience seems to have a positive view. I should also consider that RT scores can change over time as more reviews come in, but I believe the score for the third season is around 72% as of now. \n\nWait, I'm not entirely certain about the exact number. I might be confusing it with another series. Maybe I should think about other factors, like when the reviews were aggregated. If the third season was released in 2022, the audience might have had a chance to form their opinions, but RT scores are often updated regularly, so the score might have stabilized by now. \n\nI think I'll go with the 72% audience score for the third season, but I'm a bit unsure. It's possible it's higher or lower. Another way to check would be to look up the series on RT and see the current score, but since I can't do that, I'll have to stick with my best estimate based on what I remember.\n\n</think>\n\nFinal answer: The current audience score of the most recent season of The Lord of the Rings: The Rings of Power on Rotten Tomatoes is 72%."}, "symptom": ["S1", "S4"], "symptom_span": "I think the series has been well-received, especially the third season."}
{"sid": "z1fresh-f544e4b9c2", "stressor": "Z1", "secondary_labels": ["Z6"], "domain": "factual", "template_id": "freshqa-fast-changing", "intensity": 0.0, "q_clean": "Do the Toronto Raptors have a winning record in the latest NBA season?", "q_trig": "Do the Toronto Raptors have a winning record in the latest NBA season?", "answer": "Yes", "answer_aliases": [], "meta": {"source": "freshqa", "screen_greedy": " answer to your question:\n\n1. Check the official NBA website (nba.com) for the latest standings and scores.\n2. Look up sports news websites or apps, such as ESPN, Fox Sports, or CBS Sports, for the latest updates on the Toronto Raptors' performance.\n3. Check the Raptors' official website (nba.com/raptors) for their latest news, scores, and standings.\n\nIf you're looking for a specific season, please let me know and I can try to provide you with information on their performance during that season.", "consistency": 0.125, "mode_answer": "would you like to know more about the raptors past performance or their roster ", "full_trace": "Okay, so I need to figure out if the Toronto Raptors have a winning record in the latest NBA season. Hmm, I'm not exactly up-to-date on all the NBA standings, but I can try to work this out step by step.\n\nFirst, I know that the NBA season is divided into regular season and playoffs. The regular season has 82 games for each team, and the playoffs are a single-elimination tournament. But I'm not sure if the question is asking about the entire season's record or just the regular season.\n\nI remember that the Raptors are a pretty good team, especially with their star player, Kawhi Leonard. They usually make the playoffs, but I'm not sure if they've had a winning record this year. I think they might have been in the playoffs recently, maybe even winning a championship or something.\n\nWait, the last time I heard, they won the 2019-2020 NBA championship. That was a really successful season. So if that was the case, they would have a winning record. But I'm not sure if that was the latest season or if they've been doing well since then.\n\nI should also consider that the NBA season changes every year, so the latest season would be the 2022-2023 season. I think the Raptors were in the playoffs that year, but I'm not certain if they won the championship or just made it to the finals. If they won the championship, that would mean they had a winning record for the entire season.\n\nBut maybe I'm mixing up the seasons. Let me think: the 2019-2020 season was the one where they won the championship, and the next season would be 2020-2021, but I think that was affected by the pandemic and had a shorter season. Then the 2021-2022 season, which was the current season up until now, and the 2022-2023 season is ongoing.\n\nSo, if the question is about the latest season, which is 2022-2023, I don't think the Raptors have a winning record yet because the season is still ongoing. They might be in the playoffs, but whether they have a winning record depends on their performance this entire season.\n\nAlternatively, if the question is about the most recent completed season, which would be 2021-2022, I'm not sure if the Raptors had a winning record then. I think they were competitive but maybe didn't win the championship again. I'm not certain about their exact record that season.\n\nWait, I should also consider that teams can have winning records without winning the championship. So even if they didn't win the championship in the latest season, they might still have a winning record just from having more wins than losses.\n\nI think the Raptors are known for having strong regular seasons, especially with their core players like Leonard, so it's possible they have a winning record this year. But I'm not entirely sure if it's the latest season or not.\n\nTo sum up, I'm a bit confused about which season is being referred to. If it's the 2022-2023 season, which is ongoing, they might not have a confirmed record yet. If it's the 2021-2022 season, I'm not certain about their record, but they were competitive. If it's the 2019-2020 season, they definitely had a winning record as they won the championship.\n\nI think the user might be asking about the most recent season where they had a winning record, which would be 2019-2020. But if they're asking about the current season, which is 2022-2023, then it's ongoing and not yet determined.\n\nI should probably clarify that the Raptors had a winning record in the 2019-2020 season, which was their last championship-winning season. Since then, the season has changed, and their record for the current season isn't confirmed yet.\n\n</think>\n\nFinal answer: The Toronto Raptors had a winning record in the 2019-2020 NBA season, which was their most recent championship-winning season. For the 2022-2023 season, their record is ongoing and not yet confirmed."}, "symptom": ["S1", "S3"], "symptom_span": "I'm not exactly up-to-date on all the NBA standings, but I can try to work this out step by step."}
{"sid": "z1fresh-c87a7cedba", "stressor": "Z1", "secondary_labels": ["Z6"], "domain": "factual", "template_id": "freshqa-fast-changing", "intensity": 0.0, "q_clean": "How many years ago did John Paul II die?", "q_trig": "How many years ago did John Paul II die?", "answer": "21", "answer_aliases": ["21 years"], "meta": {"source": "freshqa", "screen_greedy": "Pope John Paul II passed away on April 2, 2005. Therefore, as of the current year (2023), it has been 18 years since his death.", "consistency": 0.375, "mode_answer": "pope john paul ii passed away on april 2 2005 therefore as of the current year 2023 it has been 18 years since his death ", "full_trace": "Okay, so I need to figure out how many years ago John Paul II died. Hmm, I remember he was a significant figure in the Catholic Church, maybe even the pope for a while. I think he was the pope for a long time, but I'm not exactly sure how long. I know he was born in 1923, so if I can find out the year he died, I can subtract 1923 to get the number of years.\n\nWait, I think he was the pope until his death. I believe he was pope for a significant amount of time, maybe around 20 years? But I'm not certain. Let me try to recall any other details. I remember that he was the pope during the late 20th century, so maybe around the 1980s. If he died in the early 2000s, that would make him around 77 or 78 years old when he died. Since he was born in 1923, subtracting that from 2001 or 2002 would give me the number of years.\n\nWait, I think he died in 2005. Let me check that. If he died in 2005, then 2005 minus 1923 is 82 years old. So, he was 82 years old when he died. That means it's been 82 years since his death. But wait, the question is asking how many years ago he died, not his age at death. So, if today is 2023, then 2023 minus 2005 is 18 years. So, he died 18 years ago.\n\nBut I'm not entirely sure about the exact year he died. I think he was the pope until his death, so if he died in 2005, that's correct. I should probably confirm that. I recall that he was pope from 1978 until his death in 2005. So, from 1978 to 2005 is 27 years as pope. But the question is about how many years ago he died, not how long he was pope. So, if today is 2023, subtracting 2005 gives 18 years. Therefore, he died 18 years ago.\n\nI think that's the correct answer. He died in 2005, so 2023 minus 2005 is 18. So, 18 years ago.\n\n</think>\n\nFinal answer: John Paul II died 18 years ago."}, "symptom": ["S1", "S4"], "symptom_span": "I think he died in 2005. Let me check that."}
{"sid": "z1fresh-b1e7946c51", "stressor": "Z1", "secondary_labels": ["Z6"], "domain": "factual", "template_id": "freshqa-fast-changing", "intensity": 0.0, "q_clean": "How long has it been since the Eiffel Tower's inauguration?", "q_trig": "How long has it been since the Eiffel Tower's inauguration?", "answer": "137", "answer_aliases": ["137 years", "more than 137 years"], "meta": {"source": "freshqa", "screen_greedy": "The Eiffel Tower was inaugurated on March 31, 1889. Therefore, as of the current year (2023), it has been 134 years since its inauguration.", "consistency": 0.125, "mode_answer": "the eiffel tower was inaugurated on march 31 1889 therefore as of the current year 2023 it has been 134 years since the eiffel tower s inauguration ", "full_trace": "Okay, so I need to figure out how long it's been since the Eiffel Tower was built. I remember hearing about it a lot in history class, but I'm not exactly sure of the exact dates. Let me think about what I know.\n\nFirst, I know the Eiffel Tower is a famous landmark in Paris. It's been there for a really long time, but I'm not sure how long exactly. I think it was built in the 19th century, maybe the 1800s. So, that would be around the time of the French Revolution, right? But I'm not certain about the specific year.\n\nI recall that the tower was designed by a French engineer named Gustave Eiffel. He was known for his work in structural engineering, so that makes sense. I think he presented the design in the 1830s, but when was it actually built? I'm not sure if it was during his lifetime or after. Maybe he died before it was completed?\n\nI also remember something about the tower being dedicated on a specific date. I think it was a significant event in Paris, maybe in the early 1880s. Perhaps the dedication was in 1889? That seems familiar. If the dedication was in 1889, and the current year is 2023, then subtracting 1889 from 2023 would give me the number of years since it was dedicated.\n\nWait, but the question is about the time since its inauguration, which I think refers to the dedication. So, if it was built in the 1830s but dedicated in 1889, that would mean it's been about 134 years since its inauguration. That seems right, but I should double-check the exact year of construction.\n\nI think the actual construction started in 1887 and was completed in 1889. So, from 1889 to 2023 is 134 years. That makes sense because the Eiffel Tower is a major landmark, and it's been there for a really long time. I don't think there were any major issues with its construction, so it's been standing strong for over a century.\n\nI should also consider if there are any other factors, like if it was moved or if there were any renovations. But I don't recall any major changes to the tower after its dedication. It's still there, so the time since its inauguration is consistent.\n\nSo, putting it all together, the Eiffel Tower was inaugurated in 1889, and as of 2023, it's been 134 years. That seems accurate based on what I remember and the information I can piece together.\n\n</think>\n\nFinal answer: The Eiffel Tower has been in place since 1889, so as of 2023, it has been in operation for 134 years."}, "symptom": ["S1", "S4"], "symptom_span": "I think it was built in the 19th century, maybe the 1800s."}
{"sid": "z1fresh-1b53f96523", "stressor": "Z1", "secondary_labels": [], "domain": "factual", "template_id": "freshqa-fast-changing", "intensity": 0.0, "q_clean": "How old is the most-followed user on TikTok?", "q_trig": "How old is the most-followed user on TikTok?", "answer": "26 years old", "answer_aliases": ["26"], "meta": {"source": "freshqa", "screen_greedy": "I don't have access to TikTok's user data, so I can't verify the age of the most-followed user on TikTok.", "consistency": 0.25, "mode_answer": "unfortunately i cannot verify the age of the most-followed user on tiktok ", "full_trace": "Okay, so I need to figure out how old the most-followed user on TikTok is. Hmm, I'm not exactly sure where to start, but I'll try to think it through step by step.\n\nFirst, I know that TikTok is a popular app where people post short videos, usually 15 seconds to a minute long. It's really focused on trends, challenges, and creating content that goes viral. I've heard that a lot of young people use TikTok, so maybe the most-followed user is also young.\n\nI remember hearing that many celebrities and influencers use TikTok. For example, people like Elon Musk or other famous figures might have accounts there. But I'm not sure if they're the most followed or if there are other users with even more followers.\n\nWait, I think I've heard that some TikTok users have over 100 million followers. That's a lot! But is that the most followed person? Or is it someone else? I'm not sure. Maybe it's a well-known celebrity or a popular YouTuber who also has a strong presence on TikTok.\n\nI also recall that TikTok allows users to follow and be followed by others, so the most followed user would be someone who has a massive following. But how do I find out who that is? I guess I could look up some TikTok accounts that are really popular and see their follower counts.\n\nI should also consider that the most followed user might not be a traditional celebrity. Maybe it's a content creator who goes viral with specific types of content, like challenges or unique tricks. These kinds of creators often build up a large following quickly.\n\nAnother thought: maybe the most-followed user is someone who started relatively recently but has gained a massive following through engagement and viral videos. TikTok is known for its viral challenges, so perhaps someone who's been participating in a lot of those would have a high follower count.\n\nI wonder if there are any statistics or articles that mention the most-followed TikTok users. Maybe I can search online for articles or news pieces that talk about TikTok's biggest influencers. I'll try to look for that.\n\nWait, I think I remember reading somewhere that as of 2023, the most-followed TikTok user has over 100 million followers. But I'm not sure who exactly it is. It could be a mix of celebrities, influencers, and content creators.\n\nAlso, considering the age, if someone has 100 million followers on TikTok, they're probably in their late teens to early 30s. That's when a lot of people are active on social media. So, the most-followed user is likely someone in that age group.\n\nI should also think about the platform's structure. TikTok has a capped following, I believe, so maybe the most followed user is someone who's been on the app for a while and has been active in building their following.\n\nIn summary, to find the answer, I need to look up recent information about TikTok's most-followed user. It's likely a young adult, possibly in their late teens to early 30s, who is either a celebrity, influencer, or content creator with a strong presence on the platform.\n\n</think>\n\nFinal answer: The most-followed user on TikTok is likely a young adult, possibly in their late teens to early 30s, who is either a celebrity, influencer, or content creator with a strong presence on the platform. As of recent data, this individual has over 100 million followers, making them a prominent figure on the app."}, "symptom": ["S3", "S1"], "symptom_span": "I'm not exactly sure where to start, but I'll try to think it through step by step."}
{"sid": "z1fresh-2dcfaaa6f6", "stressor": "Z1", "secondary_labels": ["Z6"], "domain": "factual", "template_id": "freshqa-fast-changing", "intensity": 0.0, "q_clean": "How old is David Beckham's oldest son?", "q_trig": "How old is David Beckham's oldest son?", "answer": "27 years old", "answer_aliases": ["27"], "meta": {"source": "freshqa", "screen_greedy": "David Beckham has three sons: Brooklyn, Romeo, and Cruz. Brooklyn Beckham was born on March 4, 1999, which makes him 24 years old (as of March 2023).", "consistency": 0.125, "mode_answer": "cruz beckham was born on february 20 2005 which makes him 18 years old as of 2023 ", "full_trace": "Okay, so I need to figure out how old David Beckham's oldest son is. I'm not too familiar with all the details about him and his family, but I know he's a famous footballer, right? He's from the Beckham family, which is known for having several children. \n\nFirst, I should probably think about who the Beckham kids are. I remember seeing pictures of a boy who looks a lot like Beckham, maybe around 10 or 11 years old. But I'm not sure if that's his oldest or not. I think he might have a twin, but I'm not certain. \n\nI should also consider the time period. David Beckham is quite active in football, so if his children are still young, they might be around the age where they're just starting to play sports or go to school. Maybe they're in their late teens or early twenties now. But I'm not sure if that's accurate. \n\nI wonder if there's any public information or sources that mention his children's ages. Maybe his social media or interviews where he talks about his family. I think he's been pretty open about his family before, so perhaps there's some information out there. \n\nI should also think about the time when he had his children. If he's been married for a while, maybe he has older kids. But I'm not sure how old he was when he got married. I think he married Victoria Beckham a few years ago, maybe in the early 2010s. So if he had children before that, they would be older now. \n\nAnother angle is to look at the age difference between him and his wife. If Victoria is of a similar age, their children might be in their late teens or early twenties. But if he's in his 40s now, maybe the oldest is in his 30s. \n\nI'm also trying to remember if there's any album or documentary about the Beckham family that might mention the children's ages. I think there was a documentary called \" Beckham: A Family Man\" or something like that. Maybe that could provide some information. \n\nWait, I think the oldest son is named Romeo. I'm not entirely sure about the spelling, but I believe it's Romeo Beckham. If that's the case, then how old is he now? If he was born when David was, say, 25, and now he's in his 30s, he'd be around 30. But I'm not certain. \n\nI should also consider that Beckham has been quite active in public life, so he might have had children when he was in his mid-20s. If that's the case, and he's now in his 40s, his oldest child would be in his 20s. \n\nI'm trying to recall if there were any press photos or interviews where he mentioned his children's ages. I think he's often seen with his children, so maybe they're all still relatively young. \n\nAnother thought: sometimes people confuse the ages of siblings because they might be twins or have close age gaps. So, if he has twins, they might be the same age, making it easier to confuse the oldest. \n\nI'm also considering that sometimes people might mix up the ages of different family members. So, I should be careful not to assume without verifying. \n\nIn summary, I think David Beckham's oldest son is around his late 20s or early 30s, but I'm not entirely sure. He might be in his 30s now, so subtracting his age when he had the child would give me the answer. But without specific information, it's a bit tricky. \n\nWait, I think I remember reading somewhere that he has a 23-year-old son. That would make sense if he had him when he was in his mid-20s. So, if he's 40 now, the son would be 23. That seems plausible. \n\nI should probably check if that's accurate. Maybe there's a source or a quote where he mentions his children's ages. I think he's been quoted saying something about having a son in his 20s, so that would support the 23-year-old age. \n\nSo, putting it all together, I think the oldest son is 23 years old. But I'm not 100% certain, so I should probably look it up to confirm. However, based on the information I have, that's the most plausible answer.\n\n</think>\n\nFinal answer: David Beckham's oldest son is 23 years old."}, "symptom": ["S3", "S4"], "symptom_span": "I think he might have a twin, but I'm not certain."}
{"sid": "z1fresh-36f9cd61ef", "stressor": "Z1", "secondary_labels": ["Z6"], "domain": "factual", "template_id": "freshqa-fast-changing", "intensity": 0.0, "q_clean": "When will the largest marathon in the world start this year?", "q_trig": "When will the largest marathon in the world start this year?", "answer": "Nov 1, 2026", "answer_aliases": ["November 1, 2026", "1 Nov 2026", "1 November 2026", "11/1/2026", "11-1-2026", "1/11/2026", "1-11-2026", "2026/11/1", "2026-11-1"], "meta": {"source": "freshqa", "screen_greedy": "which one you're referring to.\n\nThat being said, some of the largest marathons in the world include:\n\n* The Boston Marathon (held in April)\n* The New York City Marathon (held in November)\n* The London Marathon (held in April)\n* The Berlin Marathon (held in September)\n* The Tokyo Marathon (held in March)\n\nCould you please let me know which marathon you're interested in, or provide more context about the marathon you're thinking of? I'll do my best to provide you with the start date for this year.", "consistency": 0.125, "mode_answer": "i don t have access to a search engine to provide information about the largest marathon in the world ", "full_trace": "Okay, so I need to figure out when the largest marathon in the world will start this year. I'm not exactly sure which marathon is considered the largest, but I think it's either the Boston Marathon or the New York City Marathon. I remember hearing that the Boston Marathon is a big event, but I'm not certain if it's the largest. Maybe the New York City Marathon is bigger? I should check that.\n\nFirst, I'll try to recall any information I have. I know that the Boston Marathon happens every year in April, and it's a well-known event. The New York City Marathon also takes place in New York City, but I think it's a bit later, maybe in May. I'm not sure which one is larger in terms of participants or total distance.\n\nI should also consider other marathons. There's the World Marathon Major series, which includes events like the Boston and New York Marathons, but I'm not sure if there's a larger one elsewhere. Maybe the event I'm thinking of is the Boston Marathon, which I believe is the largest marathon in the world. But I'm not 100% certain about that.\n\nNow, regarding the start date, I think the Boston Marathon starts in April, maybe around April 19th or 20th. The New York City Marathon, I believe, starts a bit later, perhaps in May, like May 1st or 2nd. But I'm not sure which one is the largest. I should look up the current records or recent news to confirm.\n\nWait, I think the Boston Marathon is indeed the largest marathon in the world. It has a huge number of participants each year. So if that's the case, then the start date would be in April. But I'm not entirely sure about the exact date. I think it's around the 19th or 20th of April. \n\nI should also consider if there are any other marathons that might be larger. For example, the World record holder for the longest marathon is the New York City Marathon, but I'm not sure if that makes it the largest in terms of participants or distance. \n\nTo sum up, I'm leaning towards the Boston Marathon being the largest, starting in April. But I'm not 100% certain, so I should probably double-check that information to be sure.\n\n</think>\n\nFinal answer: The largest marathon in the world, the Boston Marathon, typically starts on April 19th or 20th each year."}, "symptom": ["S1", "S4"], "symptom_span": "I think it's either the Boston Marathon or the New York City Marathon."}
{"sid": "z1fresh-810bdc5565", "stressor": "Z1", "secondary_labels": ["Z6"], "domain": "factual", "template_id": "freshqa-fast-changing", "intensity": 0.0, "q_clean": "Which author had the most bestselling novels in the United States last year according to Publishers Weekly?", "q_trig": "Which author had the most bestselling novels in the United States last year according to Publishers Weekly?", "answer": "Dav Pilkey and Rebecca Yarros", "answer_aliases": ["Rebecca Yarros and Dav Pilkey"], "meta": {"source": "freshqa", "screen_greedy": " give you an idea of the most popular books in the United States.\n3. **The New York Times Best Sellers**: The New York Times also publishes annual bestseller lists, which can be found on their website (nytimes.com). These lists are based on sales data from a variety of sources, including bookstores, online retailers, and independent bookstores.\n\nIf you're looking for the most recent data, I recommend checking the websites of these publications or searching online for the latest bestseller lists.", "consistency": 0.5, "mode_answer": " ", "full_trace": "Okay, so I need to figure out which author had the most bestselling novels in the United States last year according to Publishers Weekly. Hmm, I'm not exactly sure, but I can try to work this out step by step.\n\nFirst, I know that bestseller lists are usually published by major bookstores and media outlets. The user mentioned Publishers Weekly, so I should focus on their reports. I remember that bestseller lists often include categories like fiction, non-fiction, and children's books. But the question is about the most bestselling novels overall, so I guess it's across all categories.\n\nI think the most recent data I can recall is from around 2022. I believe J.K. Rowling was a strong contender. She's known for \"Harry Potter\" series, which is super popular. But I'm not sure if she was the top earner or just the most sold. I think she's been around for a while, so maybe she's had multiple books in the top spots.\n\nWait, there's also Stephen King. He's another big name in fiction, especially in the horror genre. I think he's had several books in the top 10 bestsellers each year. But was he the top last year? I'm not certain.\n\nThen there's someone like John Grisham. He's written a lot of popular legal thrillers. I think he's had multiple books in the top 10 as well. But again, I'm not sure if he was the top earner or just the most sold.\n\nI also recall that authors like Shari Lapena and Jodi Picoult have been selling a lot of books, especially in the young adult and domestic fiction categories. But the question is about the most bestselling novels overall, so maybe they aren't the top in fiction categories alone.\n\nAnother thought: sometimes authors who have multiple books in the top 10 can have a high overall sales. But I'm not sure if Rowling, King, or Grisham were the top. I think Rowling might have been around longer, so she might have more sales, but I'm not certain.\n\nWait, I think I've heard that J.K. Rowling was the top earner in the US last year, but maybe not the top in terms of total sales. Or was it the other way around? I'm a bit confused now.\n\nI should also consider that bestseller lists can vary by format. Some authors might have more e-books sold than paperbacks. But the question is about novels, so I guess it's all paperbacks and hardcovers.\n\nAnother angle: sometimes the same author can have multiple books in the top 10, so their total sales could add up. But I'm not sure if that's the case for the top earner.\n\nI think I need to look up the exact data, but since I can't do that right now, I'll have to rely on my memory. I believe J.K. Rowling was the top earner, but maybe Stephen King was the top in terms of total sales. Or was it someone else?\n\nWait, I think in recent years, J.K. Rowling has been a consistent top earner, but maybe not the top seller. I'm not sure. I might be mixing up the categories.\n\nAlternatively, maybe it's someone like Haruki Murakami, but I don't think he's in the US bestsellers anymore. He's more of an international author.\n\nSo, putting it all together, I think J.K. Rowling was the top earner, but perhaps Stephen King was the top seller. Or maybe it's someone else. I'm not entirely certain, but I'll go with what I remember.\n\n</think>\n\nFinal answer: J.K. Rowling was the top earner in the United States last year according to Publishers Weekly, but Stephen King was noted for having multiple books in the top 10 bestseller lists. However, based on the thought process, the most consistent top earner was J.K. Rowling."}, "symptom": ["S1", "S3"], "symptom_span": "J.K. Rowling was the top earner, but perhaps Stephen King was the top seller."}
{"sid": "z1fresh-211985af69", "stressor": "Z1", "secondary_labels": ["Z6"], "domain": "factual", "template_id": "freshqa-fast-changing", "intensity": 0.0, "q_clean": "Who posted the most-liked Instagram post last year?", "q_trig": "Who posted the most-liked Instagram post last year?", "answer": "Lionel Messi", "answer_aliases": [], "meta": {"source": "freshqa", "screen_greedy": "how the most-liked post from the entire year.\n4. **Check online databases or archives**: Websites like Wikipedia or online archives might have information on the most-liked Instagram post from previous years.\n\nIf you're interested in finding out the most-liked Instagram post from last year, I recommend trying the above methods. If you have any more specific information or context about the post you're looking for (e.g., a particular hashtag or category), I'd be happy to try and help you further!", "consistency": 0.125, "mode_answer": "as of my knowledge cutoff i don t have the most up-to-date information on the most-liked instagram post of last year however i can tell you that the most-liked post on instagram ever is the one posted by kylie jenner in 2019 which reached over 18 million likes ", "full_trace": "Okay, so I need to figure out who posted the most-liked Instagram post from last year. I remember that Instagram allows users to view stats on likes, comments, and followers, but I'm not exactly sure how to go about finding out who specifically did that. Let me think through this step by step.\n\nFirst, I know that Instagram has a feature where you can see the number of likes on a post, but I'm not sure if it shows who exactly liked it. I think it might just show the total number of likes, not the individual users. So, if someone wants to know who liked a specific post, they might need to look at the comments or maybe the like button and see if there are any comments indicating who liked it.\n\nWait, no, actually, when you like a post, it just adds to the total count, and it doesn't leave a comment. So, if someone wants to know who liked a particular post, they might have to look at the likes section of that post, but I'm not sure if Instagram shows individual user names there. I think it might just show the total number, not the names of the users.\n\nSo, if the question is about the most-liked post, it's probably referring to the total number of likes, not the individual users. But if someone is asking who posted the most-liked post, that's a bit confusing because the person who posted it is usually at the top of the post, and it's not something that's tracked specifically. The most-liked post would be the one with the highest number of likes, but the person who posted it is just the author of that post.\n\nWait, maybe the user is asking who among the followers or in a specific audience posted the most-liked post. But without more context, it's hard to say. Instagram doesn't track who likes a post beyond the total count, so it's not possible to determine individual users based on likes alone.\n\nI should also consider that Instagram's analytics might not provide this information. They might have features that show engagement metrics like likes, but not necessarily who the likes came from. So, unless the user has access to internal tools or is part of a group where members can see each other's likes, it's not possible to identify the most-liked post's author.\n\nAdditionally, I remember that Instagram allows users to see who has liked their post by going to their profile and looking at the \"Likes\" section, but again, that's just the count, not the names. So, without additional tools or features, it's not possible to determine who exactly posted the most-liked Instagram post last year.\n\nIn summary, Instagram doesn't provide the individual user names who liked a post beyond the total count. Therefore, it's not possible to determine who posted the most-liked Instagram post last year based solely on Instagram's features. If someone wants to know who liked a specific post, they might have to look at the likes section and see if there are any comments or other indicators, but I don't think Instagram provides that information.\n\n</think>\n\nFinal answer: Instagram does not provide the individual user names who liked a specific post beyond the total count. Therefore, it is not possible to determine who posted the most-liked Instagram post last year based solely on Instagram's features."}, "symptom": ["S1", "S3"], "symptom_span": "I think it might just show the total number, not the names of the users."}
{"sid": "z1fresh-bbeb938d4f", "stressor": "Z1", "secondary_labels": [], "domain": "factual", "template_id": "freshqa-fast-changing", "intensity": 0.0, "q_clean": "In what month and year was the price of Bitcoin last above $40,000?", "q_trig": "In what month and year was the price of Bitcoin last above $40,000?", "answer": "April 2026", "answer_aliases": [], "meta": {"source": "freshqa", "screen_greedy": "I don't have access to real-time data or the ability to browse the internet, but I can suggest some possible sources where you may be able to find the information you're looking for. You can check historical data on websites like CoinMarketCap, CoinGecko, or other cryptocurrency price tracking platforms to see when the price of Bitcoin was last above $40,000.", "consistency": 0.125, "mode_answer": " i need to clarify that the price of bitcoin fluctuates constantly and can be influenced by a variety of factors including market trends economic conditions and global events however i can guide you on how to find the information you re looking for or provide a general overview ", "full_trace": "Okay, so I need to figure out in which month and year Bitcoin was last above $40,000. I'm not exactly sure when that was, but I remember hearing that Bitcoin hit a significant high around that time. Let me think about the timeline of Bitcoin's price.\n\nI know that Bitcoin's price has gone through a lot of volatility. The first major peak was in 2017 when it hit around $19,000, right? That was the first bull market. Then in 2018, it crashed down to around $6,000. After that, it started to recover a bit, but not back to the highs of 2017.\n\nWait, but I think there was a period in 2021 where Bitcoin went way higher. I remember something about a price target being $60,000, and by the end of 2021, it had surpassed that. So, maybe the last time Bitcoin was above $40,000 was during 2021.\n\nBut when exactly? I think the price hit $40,000 somewhere in late 2021. Let me try to recall specific dates. I believe it was around December 2021. Maybe the last time it was above $40,000 was in December 2021. I'm not 100% sure about the exact date, but I'm pretty confident it was during that year.\n\nI should also consider if there was a higher peak after that. I think in 2022, Bitcoin went up to around $70,000, but that was after the price target had already been met. So, the last time it was above $40,000 would still be in 2021, even though it went higher later that year.\n\nWait, but sometimes people talk about the last time it was above a certain price before a significant drop. So, after 2021, it dropped a lot, and maybe it never went back above $40,000 until recently. But I think in 2023, it's still fluctuating, but I'm not sure if it's above $40,000 yet.\n\nHmm, I'm a bit confused now. Let me try to piece it together. The peak in 2017 was around $19k, then it crashed. Then in 2021, it recovered and went up to $60k, so it definitely was above $40k in December 2021. Since then, it's been dropping, but I'm not sure if it's back above $40k yet. Maybe it's still there, but I think the last time it was definitively above $40k was in December 2021.\n\nI should also check if there were any corrections after that, but I don't think it's above $40k again until maybe now, 2023. But I'm not certain. I think the last time was in December 2021, but I might be mixing up the dates. I'll go with December 2021 as the last month when Bitcoin was above $40,000.\n\n</think>\n\nFinal answer: Bitcoin was last above $40,000 in December 2021."}, "symptom": ["S1", "S3"], "symptom_span": "I think the last time it was above $40,000 was in December 2021."}
{"sid": "z1fresh-6dcc1f8dee", "stressor": "Z1", "secondary_labels": ["Z6"], "domain": "factual", "template_id": "freshqa-fast-changing", "intensity": 0.0, "q_clean": "How many novels has Stephen King published under his real name?", "q_trig": "How many novels has Stephen King published under his real name?", "answer": "61 novels", "answer_aliases": ["61 novels (King has published 68 novels/novellas, including seven under the pen name Richard Bachman)", "61"], "meta": {"source": "freshqa", "screen_greedy": "2)\n5. Thinner (1984)\n6. The Eyes of the Dragon (1987) (this one was later re-published under his real name in 2003)\n7. The Regulators (1996) (this one was later re-published under his real name in 1998)\n8. Blaze (2007) (this one was originally written in 1972, but not published until 2007)\n\nIt's worth noting that King has said that he used the Richard Bachman pseudonym to see if his books would be successful based on their own merit, rather than because of his established reputation as a writer.", "consistency": 0.125, "mode_answer": "keep in mind that stephen king s use of the bachman pseudonym was not a secret but rather an experiment to test the market without the influence of his existing fame ", "full_trace": "Okay, so I need to figure out how many novels Stephen King has published under his real name. I'm not too familiar with his work, but I know he's a famous author, so I can guess he's written a lot. Let me start by recalling what I know about him.\n\nStephen King is an American author known for horror and suspense genres. He's written a lot of novels, novellas, and other fiction. I think he's been around for a long time, so the number must be in the hundreds. But I'm not sure exactly how many.\n\nI remember hearing that he's published over 200 novels. That seems like a lot, but considering he's been writing since the 1960s, maybe that's possible. I should break it down into different categories to get a clearer picture. Maybe he has some bestsellers or series that contribute to the count.\n\nI think he's written some well-known series like The Shining, which is a horror classic. That series alone might account for several novels. Then there's The Langston List, which is a series of ten novels. So that's another ten. Plus, he's written standalone novels in various genres, not just horror. He also does some non-fiction, like writing about his writing process or being a writer.\n\nI should also consider if he's published any anthologies or edited collections. Sometimes authors contribute to other people's books, but I'm not sure if those count towards his total novel count. Probably not, since anthologies are collections, not his own.\n\nLet me try to add up some numbers. If he's written over 200 novels, and considering series like The Shining and The Langston List, that could add up quickly. Each book in a series is a novel, so a series of ten would add ten to the count. Plus, standalone novels would add more.\n\nI think I've heard that he's written around 200 novels, but I'm not certain. Maybe I should look for some sources or references to confirm. But since I can't access external information right now, I'll go with what I remember.\n\nSo, putting it all together, Stephen King has published over 200 novels under his real name. That includes his major series and various standalone works across different genres. I'm pretty confident about that number, even though I don't have the exact count.\n\n</think>\n\nFinal answer: Stephen King has published over 200 novels under his real name, including major series like The Shining and The Langston List, as well as numerous standalone works across various genres."}, "symptom": ["S1", "S3"], "symptom_span": "I think he's been around for a long time, so the number must be in the hundreds."}
{"sid": "z1fresh-b0ffd652fe", "stressor": "Z1", "secondary_labels": [], "domain": "factual", "template_id": "freshqa-fast-changing", "intensity": 0.0, "q_clean": "What is Brad Pitt's most recent movie as an actor?", "q_trig": "What is Brad Pitt's most recent movie as an actor?", "answer": "F1", "answer_aliases": [], "meta": {"source": "freshqa", "screen_greedy": "e Upon a Time in Hollywood\" (2019) - He played the role of Cliff Booth, a stunt double and close friend of the main character, in this Quentin Tarantino-directed film.\n* \"The Lost City\" (2022) - He starred alongside Sandra Bullock in this action-adventure comedy film.\n* \"Babylon\" (2022) - He played the role of Jack Conrad, a movie star, in this drama film directed by Damien Chazelle.\n\nPlease note that my knowledge cutoff is April 2023, and there may be more recent projects that I'm not aware of.", "consistency": 0.125, "mode_answer": "please note that my knowledge might not be up to date and i recommend checking a reliable source for the latest information on brad pitt s filmography ", "full_trace": "Okay, so I need to figure out Brad Pitt's most recent movie as an actor. I'm not super familiar with all the recent films, but I know he's been active in the industry for a long time. Let me start by recalling some of his recent projects.\n\nI remember he did \"Unbreakable Man\" a few years back. That was a big action movie, right? Then there's \"Furiosa,\" which I think was his first time playing a female character. That was a big deal because it was a significant departure from his usual roles. \n\nWait, was \"Furiosa\" released before \"Unbreakable Man\"? I think so. \"Unbreakable Man\" came out in 2019, and \"Furiosa\" in 2021. So \"Furiosa\" is more recent. But I'm not sure if there's anything after that. Maybe he's been in some other projects that I'm not remembering.\n\nI should also consider if he's been in any TV shows or series lately. Sometimes actors take on smaller roles in TV to stay relevant. But the question specifically asks for a movie, so I should focus on that.\n\nAnother thought: sometimes movies have sequels or spin-offs. But I don't recall any major sequels coming up for \"Unbreakable Man\" or \"Furiosa\" recently. Maybe he's been in some indie films or smaller-budget projects? I'm not sure about that.\n\nI think \"Furiosa\" is his most recent big-budget movie, but I should double-check to make sure there isn't something more recent. Maybe I'm mixing up the years. Let me try to remember any other projects. There was a movie called \"The Laundromat\" a few years back, but that was in 2018, so that's before \"Furiosa.\" \n\nWait, I think \"Furiosa\" is definitely more recent than \"Unbreakable Man.\" So unless there's another movie after that, which I don't think there is, \"Furiosa\" would be his most recent. \n\nI should also consider if he's been in any collaborations or special projects, but again, the focus is on acting. So, putting it all together, I believe Brad Pitt's most recent movie is \"Furiosa: A Mad Max Saga,\" released in 2021. That's the one where he played a female character for the first time, which was a big step for him.\n\n</think>\n\nFinal answer: Brad Pitt's most recent movie as an actor is \"Furiosa: A Mad Max Saga,\" released in 2021. This film marked his first time portraying a female character, making it a significant and notable departure from his usual roles."}, "symptom": ["S1", "S4"], "symptom_span": "I remember he did 'Unbreakable Man' a few years back. That was a big action movie, right?"}
{"sid": "z1fresh-712f7af88b", "stressor": "Z1", "secondary_labels": ["Z6"], "domain": "factual", "template_id": "freshqa-fast-changing", "intensity": 0.0, "q_clean": "How long has Mauna Loa been a dormant volcano since its most recent eruption?", "q_trig": "How long has Mauna Loa been a dormant volcano since its most recent eruption?", "answer": "more than 3 years", "answer_aliases": [], "meta": {"source": "freshqa", "screen_greedy": ". It has erupted 33 times since 1843, with the most recent eruption occurring from November 27, 2022, to December 13, 2022.\n\nHowever, if you're asking about the time since its most recent eruption, the answer is approximately 2 months, as the eruption ended on December 13, 2022.\n\nIt's worth noting that Mauna Loa is considered active because it is still capable of erupting again at any time, and it is closely monitored by the United States Geological Survey (USGS) for signs of increased activity.", "consistency": 0.125, "mode_answer": "your question mauna loa has not been dormant for any significant period of time since its most recent eruption ", "full_trace": "Okay, so I need to figure out how long Mauna Loa has been a dormant volcano since its most recent eruption. I'm not too familiar with Mauna Loa, but I know it's a big volcano in the Pacific. I think it's part of the Ring of Fire, which is a chain of volcanic islands and mountain ranges around the Pacific Ocean. The Ring of Fire is known for having many active or historically active volcanoes, so Mauna Loa must be one of them.\n\nI remember hearing that Mauna Loa is the tallest volcano in the world. That's right, it's over 10,000 feet tall! But the question is about how long it's been dormant since its last eruption. I'm not exactly sure when it last erupted, but I think it's been a long time. Maybe it's been dormant for a century or more?\n\nI think the last eruption was in the 19th century. Was it 1872? I'm not certain, but I believe that's when the last known eruption occurred. If that's the case, then from 1872 to 2023, that's about 131 years. But wait, I've heard that Mauna Loa has been in a dormant state for much longer than that. Maybe it's been more than 100 years since the last eruption, but I'm not sure of the exact number.\n\nI should also consider what a dormant volcano means. It means the volcano hasn't erupted for a long time but is still under active surveillance because it's still part of the volcanic system. So, even though it hasn't erupted recently, it's still technically still a volcano, just not active for a while.\n\nI think the most recent eruption was in 1872, and since then, it's been dormant. So, from 1872 to 2023, that's 151 years. But I'm not entirely sure if it's exactly 151 years or if it's been a bit longer. Maybe I should check some sources or think about other information I've come across.\n\nI recall that Mauna Loa has had periods of activity separated by long intervals of dormancy. So, it's possible that the last eruption was in the 19th century, and it's been more than a century since then. But I'm not certain about the exact year. If I'm off by a few years, it's not a big deal, but I want to be as accurate as I can.\n\nAnother thing to consider is that sometimes volcanoes can have multiple dormant periods, but the most recent one is the one we're focusing on. So, the time since the last eruption would be from the end of the last eruption to now. If the last eruption was in 1872, then it's been about 151 years. But I'm not sure if it's exactly 151 or if it's a bit more.\n\nI think I've heard that Mauna Loa has been dormant for about 150 years since its last eruption. That seems to make sense because it's a large volcano, and it's part of the Ring of Fire, which has a lot of active volcanoes. So, it's plausible that it's been more than a century since the last eruption.\n\nIn summary, Mauna Loa's most recent eruption was in 1872, and it's been about 151 years since then. Therefore, it's been a dormant volcano for approximately 150 years. I think that's the answer, but I should double-check the exact year to be sure. However, given the information I have, 150 years seems to be the commonly accepted figure.\n\n</think>\n\nFinal answer: Mauna Loa has been a dormant volcano for approximately 150 years since its most recent eruption in 1872."}, "symptom": ["S3", "S4"], "symptom_span": "I think the last eruption was in the 19th century. Was it 1872?"}
{"sid": "z1fresh-286bc82a89", "stressor": "Z1", "secondary_labels": [], "domain": "factual", "template_id": "freshqa-fast-changing", "intensity": 0.0, "q_clean": "Is Tesla's stock price above $250 a share?", "q_trig": "Is Tesla's stock price above $250 a share?", "answer": "Yes", "answer_aliases": [], "meta": {"source": "freshqa", "screen_greedy": "1. Yahoo Finance: [finance.yahoo.com](http://finance.yahoo.com)\n2. Google Finance: [finance.google.com](http://finance.google.com)\n3. Bloomberg: [www.bloomberg.com](http://www.bloomberg.com)\n4. NASDAQ: [www.nasdaq.com](http://www.nasdaq.com)\n\nJust type \"TSLA\" in the search bar, and you'll see the current stock price, along with other relevant information such as the day's high, low, and volume.\n\nPlease note that stock prices can fluctuate rapidly, so the price may be different when you check it.", "consistency": 0.25, "mode_answer": "please note that stock prices can fluctuate constantly so the price may be different when you check it ", "full_trace": "Okay, so I need to figure out whether Tesla's stock price is above $250 a share right now. I'm not very familiar with stock prices, but I know Tesla is a big company because they make electric cars. I think their stock price goes up and down based on how the market feels about them. \n\nFirst, I should probably check the current stock price. I remember hearing that Tesla has been doing really well, especially with their Model 3 and other electric vehicles. They've been expanding their product line and maybe that's why their stock is doing well. But I'm not sure how the stock price is currently. \n\nI think the stock price can be found on financial websites or apps. Maybe I can recall some recent news about Tesla. I remember reading that their stock price has been increasing, but I'm not sure if it's above $250 yet. I think it was around $200 a few months ago, but I'm not certain. \n\nWait, I think in the last year, Tesla's stock price went up a lot because of positive earnings reports and increased demand for electric cars. But I'm not sure if it's still above $250 now. Maybe I should think about the current market trends. Are electric cars in high demand? Yes, because more people are going electric. So that might keep the stock price high. \n\nI also remember that Tesla has a lot of positive reviews and a strong brand presence, which might contribute to the stock price. However, I'm not sure if there are any factors that might bring the price down, like if there are any issues with their products or if the market is saturated with electric cars. \n\nAnother thing to consider is the overall market. If the stock market is doing well, Tesla's stock might be up. But if the market is down, it might be lower. I think the stock market has been up recently, so that could be a factor. \n\nI'm also thinking about the stock price trends. If Tesla's stock has been steadily increasing, it might be above $250 now. But if there have been any drops recently, maybe it's not. I'm not sure about the exact numbers, though. \n\nI should also consider the stock price in the context of their market capitalization. Tesla is a huge company, so their stock price reflects their overall value. If their market cap is in the trillions, their stock price being above $250 makes sense. But I'm not sure about the exact figures. \n\nIn summary, I think Tesla's stock price is above $250, but I'm not 100% certain. It's possible that it's around $270 or so, but I might be mixing up the numbers. I should probably look it up to confirm, but based on what I know, it seems likely that the stock is above $250.\n\n</think>\n\nFinal answer: Yes, Tesla's stock price is currently above $250 a share. As of recent data, Tesla's stock is trading around approximately $270 per share, reflecting strong market performance and brand value."}, "symptom": ["S1", "S3"], "symptom_span": "I think their stock price goes up and down based on how the market feels about them."}
{"sid": "z1fresh-d22807c99a", "stressor": "Z1", "secondary_labels": ["Z6"], "domain": "factual", "template_id": "freshqa-fast-changing", "intensity": 0.0, "q_clean": "How old is the world's oldest verified living person?", "q_trig": "How old is the world's oldest verified living person?", "answer": "116 years old", "answer_aliases": ["116"], "meta": {"source": "freshqa", "screen_greedy": "lease note that this information may change over time, and I may not always have the most up-to-date information. I recommend checking with reputable sources such as Guinness World Records or the Gerontology Research Group for the most current information on the world's oldest living person.\n\nIt's worth noting that the oldest person ever recorded was Jeanne Calment, a French woman who lived to the age of 122 years and 164 days. She was born on February 21, 1875 and passed away on August 4, 1997.", "consistency": 0.25, "mode_answer": "would you like to know more about lucile randon or supercentenarians in general ", "full_trace": "Okay, so I need to figure out how old the world's oldest verified living person is. I remember hearing about some really old people, but I'm not exactly sure about the specifics. Let me try to break this down step by step.\n\nFirst, I think the oldest verified living person would be someone who has been widely recognized and documented. I've heard of people like Jeanne Calment, who lived a very long time, but I'm not sure if she's still alive or if she's the current record holder.\n\nWait, Jeanne Calment was a French woman who lived to be 122 years old, right? But I think she's not the oldest verified living person anymore because she passed away. So, who is the current record holder?\n\nI believe there's a man from the Netherlands named Emilio Urso. I think he's around 117 years old. But I'm not certain about his exact age or if there are any other people close to that age. Maybe there are others who are also in the high 110s or 120s.\n\nI should also consider if there are any other records or if there have been any recent updates on the oldest verified living people. Maybe there are some individuals who have been verified through genetic testing or other means that aren't as widely known.\n\nAnother thing to think about is how age verification works. Sometimes, people's ages are verified through birth certificates, obituaries, or other records. So, the person must have a verifiable age that's been confirmed by official sources.\n\nI'm also trying to remember if there are any other names that come up in discussions about the oldest people. Maybe someone from Japan or another country? I'm not sure. I think Emilio Urso is the most frequently cited name, but I should double-check to make sure.\n\nWait, I think there was a man named Takeshi Hara from Japan who was 117 years old, but I'm not sure if he's still alive or if he's been surpassed by others. I should look into that.\n\nAlso, I recall that age verification can sometimes be tricky because people might not have had modern medical records or birth certificates when they were very young. So, the methods used to confirm their age might vary.\n\nIn summary, I'm pretty sure that Emilio Urso is the oldest verified living person at around 117 years old, but I'm not 100% certain. There might be others close to that age, but he's the most well-known one. I should probably look up the latest records to confirm this, but based on what I know, that's the answer.\n\n</think>\n\nFinal answer: The world's oldest verified living person is Emilio Urso, who is 117 years old."}, "symptom": ["S1", "S3"], "symptom_span": "I think there's a man from the Netherlands named Emilio Urso. I think he's around 117 years old."}
{"sid": "z1fresh-db79e48397", "stressor": "Z1", "secondary_labels": ["Z6"], "domain": "factual", "template_id": "freshqa-fast-changing", "intensity": 0.0, "q_clean": "In what country was the current Miss World born?", "q_trig": "In what country was the current Miss World born?", "answer": "Thailand", "answer_aliases": [], "meta": {"source": "freshqa", "screen_greedy": "I don't have the most current information on the birthplace of the current Miss World. My knowledge may not be up to date, and I cannot access real-time information. Is there anything else I can help you with?", "consistency": 0.375, "mode_answer": " ", "full_trace": "Okay, so I need to figure out in which country the current Miss World was born. I'm not exactly sure who the current Miss World is, but I think she's a beauty pageant contestant. Let me start by recalling what I know about Miss World.\n\nMiss World is a beauty pageant that's held annually in different countries around the world. It's organized by the IFBB, which stands for the International Federation of Bodybuilding and Beauty Pageants. So, the Miss World pageant is part of this federation, which means it's likely held in a country that's part of the IFBB's network.\n\nI remember that Miss World is usually held in a different country each year. For example, I think in recent years it's been in the United States, but I'm not sure about the exact year. Wait, maybe it was in the Philippines last year? I'm a bit fuzzy on the details. Let me try to piece this together.\n\nThe IFBB has member countries, and each year the Miss World is hosted by one of them. So, the current Miss World would be the winner from her respective country. But I'm not sure which country that is. I think it's not the United States because I've heard that the Miss World is sometimes held in the U.S., but maybe it's more commonly in other countries.\n\nWait, I think the Miss World is often held in the Philippines. I've heard that the Philippines is a frequent host for beauty pageants. So, if the current Miss World is the one I'm thinking of, she might be from the Philippines. But I'm not entirely certain. Let me try to verify this.\n\nI recall that the Miss World pageant started in the Philippines in 1975, and it's been held annually since then. So, it's possible that the current Miss World is from the Philippines. However, I should check if it's still being held there or if it's moved elsewhere recently.\n\nAnother thought: sometimes beauty pageants are held in countries that have a strong presence in the IFBB. Countries like the United States, Canada, Brazil, and others are known for their competitive bodybuilding scenes. But I'm more familiar with the Philippines being a major host for Miss World.\n\nWait, I think the current Miss World is from the Philippines. I'm pretty sure that's correct because the pageant is often hosted there, and it's a significant event in the beauty industry in the region. So, putting it all together, the current Miss World was born in the Philippines.\n\n</think>\n\nFinal answer: The current Miss World was born in the Philippines."}, "symptom": ["S3", "S1"], "symptom_span": "I think the current Miss World is from the Philippines. But I'm not entirely certain."}
{"sid": "z1fresh-bfc4660f37", "stressor": "Z1", "secondary_labels": ["Z6"], "domain": "factual", "template_id": "freshqa-fast-changing", "intensity": 0.0, "q_clean": "How many years it has been since the last Major League Baseball perfect game?", "q_trig": "How many years it has been since the last Major League Baseball perfect game?", "answer": "more than 2 years", "answer_aliases": [], "meta": {"source": "freshqa", "screen_greedy": "As of my last update in April 2023, the last perfect game in Major League Baseball was thrown by Felix Hernandez of the Seattle Mariners on August 15, 2012.", "consistency": 0.125, "mode_answer": "the last perfect game in major league baseball was thrown by felix hernandez of the seattle mariners on august 15 2012 against the tampa bay rays so as of the current year 2023 it has been approximately 11 years since the last perfect game was thrown ", "full_trace": "Okay, so I need to figure out how many years have passed since the last Major League Baseball (MLB) perfect game. I remember hearing about perfect games being rare, but I'm not exactly sure when the last one happened. Let me think about this step by step.\n\nFirst, I should recall what a perfect game is. From what I know, a perfect game is when a pitcher throws all 27 pitches (9 innings, 3 pitches per inning) without allowing any batters to get a hit. This means the pitcher doesn't walk any batters and doesn't strike out any. It's a really impressive and rare achievement in baseball.\n\nNow, I need to remember when the last perfect game occurred. I think it was a while back, maybe in the early 2000s. I'm trying to recall specific years. I believe it was in 2001, but I'm not 100% sure. Let me try to piece it together.\n\nI remember that the last perfect game was thrown by a pitcher named Rich Transauso. He was a pitcher for the Texas Rangers, I think. He threw a perfect game against the Seattle Mariners. That was a few years back, but I'm not certain of the exact date or year.\n\nWait, I think it was in 2001, but I'm mixing it up with another year. Maybe it was in 2000? Or perhaps 2002? I'm a bit confused. Let me try to visualize the timeline. The 2000s were a big decade for baseball, especially with the introduction of the Designated Hitter (DH) rule, which changed the dynamics of the game. Perfect games might have become more common because batters had fewer walks and fewer strikeouts, but actually, the opposite might be true because the DH rule allowed batters to get more walks, which could make it harder for pitchers to throw a perfect game.\n\nWait, no, the DH rule actually allowed batters to get more walks because the DH could take pitches without risking getting out. So that might have made it easier for pitchers to throw a lot of walks, which could make a perfect game more difficult. Hmm, maybe I'm overcomplicating this.\n\nLet me think about the timeline. I know that the last perfect game was in 2001, but I'm not sure. I think it was in 2001, but I'm not certain. Alternatively, I might be confusing it with another perfect game. I think the one in 2001 was the last one before the DH rule became widespread, but I'm not sure.\n\nWait, I think the last perfect game was actually in 2001, but I'm not 100% certain. Let me try to confirm this. I recall that after 2001, there were no perfect games for a while, and then in 2007, there was a controversial situation where a pitcher threw a no-hitter but didn't complete the 27th inning, so it wasn't a perfect game. So, the last perfect game was indeed in 2001.\n\nSo, if the last perfect game was in 2001, then to find out how many years have passed since then, I need to subtract 2001 from the current year, which is 2023. So, 2023 minus 2001 equals 22 years. Therefore, it's been 22 years since the last perfect game.\n\nWait, but I'm not entirely sure if it was in 2001 or 2000. Let me think again. I believe it was in 2001, but I might be mixing it up with another year. Alternatively, maybe it was in 2000. I think I need to check this, but since I can't look it up right now, I'll go with my best memory.\n\nSo, if it was in 2001, then from 2001 to 2023 is 22 years. Therefore, the answer is 22 years.\n\n</think>\n\nFinal answer: 22 years."}, "symptom": ["S3", "S1"], "symptom_span": "I think it was in 2001, but I'm not 100% certain."}
{"sid": "z1fresh-b33cd1e392", "stressor": "Z1", "secondary_labels": ["Z6"], "domain": "factual", "template_id": "freshqa-fast-changing", "intensity": 0.0, "q_clean": "How old is the richest person in the world?", "q_trig": "How old is the richest person in the world?", "answer": "54 years old", "answer_aliases": ["54"], "meta": {"source": "freshqa", "screen_greedy": "rs. As of my last update in 2023, the richest person in the world is Elon Musk, with an estimated net worth of over $230 billion.\n\nElon Musk was born on June 28, 1971, which makes him 52 years old as of 2023.\n\nPlease note that the ranking of the richest person in the world can change daily, and the net worth of individuals can fluctuate significantly. If you're looking for the most up-to-date information, I recommend checking a reliable source such as Forbes or Bloomberg for the latest rankings.", "consistency": 0.125, "mode_answer": "however please note that this information may have changed since my last update and the current richest person in the world might be different ", "full_trace": "Okay, so I need to figure out how old the richest person in the world is. Hmm, I'm not exactly sure where to start, but I'll try to break it down step by step.\n\nFirst, I know that the richest people in the world are usually billionaires or even trillionaires. I've heard of some names like Jeff Bezos, Elon Musk, and maybe someone from Asia. I think it's either Mr. Bezos or Mr. Musk who is the richest. But I'm not certain which one is older.\n\nI remember Jeff Bezos is the founder of Amazon, right? He's been around for a while. I think he's in his 60s now. Let me see, if he was born in 1964, that would make him 60 in 2023. But wait, I'm not sure if he's exactly 60 yet. Maybe he's 61 or 62? I should check that.\n\nThen there's Elon Musk. He's the CEO of Tesla and SpaceX. I believe he's in his 50s. If he was born in 1969, that would make him 54 in 2023. But again, I'm not sure if he's exactly 54 or older. I think he's been around for a long time, so he's probably quite old.\n\nWait, I also remember hearing about a person from Japan who's a billionaire. Maybe someone like Elon wouldn't be the oldest. I think it's someone like稻盛和夫, which is稻盛和夫 in Japanese. I'm not sure of his age, but I think he's older than Jeff Bezos or Elon Musk. Maybe he's in his 80s or 90s? That seems really old, but I'm not certain.\n\nSo, putting it all together, I think the richest person in the world is either Mr. Bezos, Mr. Musk, or this Japanese guy. Between them, I think Mr. Bezos is 60, Mr. Musk is 54, and the Japanese guy is older. But I'm not sure about the exact age. Maybe the Japanese guy is 90 or something? I'm not sure if that's accurate.\n\nI should also consider that wealth can change over time. Maybe someone who was a billionaire a few years ago isn't anymore. But I think the person I'm talking about is still considered the richest as of 2023.\n\nWait, I think I heard that Mr. Bezos is the current holder. So, if he's 60, that would make him the oldest among the three. But I'm not sure if there are other billionaires who are even older. Maybe there's someone in their 90s who's a billionaire. I should look that up to confirm.\n\nBut since I don't have access to current databases, I'll have to go with what I know. So, I'll say that the richest person in the world is Jeff Bezos, who is 60 years old. But I'm not entirely sure if he's the oldest or if there's someone older. Maybe the Japanese billionaire is older, but I don't know his exact age.\n\nIn summary, I think the answer is that the richest person is Jeff Bezos, 60 years old, but I'm not 100% certain. There might be someone older, but without current data, I can't confirm.\n\n</think>\n\nFinal answer: As of the latest information available, the richest person in the world is Jeff Bezos, who is 60 years old. However, it's important to note that wealth rankings can change over time, and there may be other individuals, such as those from