ield. I think it might have been a scientist because Time often covers science-related awards, like the Nobel Prize, but maybe it's a different award.\n\nWait, I think the Time Person of the Year was recently awarded to someone in the field of climate science. I believe it was someone like Greta Thunberg or maybe someone else. But I'm not sure if she was the recipient or if it was someone else. I think Greta Thunberg is more of a symbol than an individual recipient, so maybe it was someone else.\n\nAlternatively, maybe it was a scientist who made significant contributions to solving a major problem, like climate change or pandemics. I'm trying to remember if it was someone like Dr. Peter Agre or maybe someone involved in fighting climate change. I think Dr. Peter Agre is a Nobel laureate, but I'm not sure if he was the recipient.\n\nWait, I think the most recent recipient might have been Dr. Jennifer Doudna, who co-created CRISPR technology. She's a scientist, so that could be it. But I'm not sure about her birthplace. If she was born in the US, then the country would be the US. But I'm not certain if she was the most recent recipient.\n\nAlternatively, maybe it was someone like Bill Gates or Elon Musk, but I don't think they were the recipients of the Time Person of the Year. I think that award is more for individuals who have made a significant impact in their field, not necessarily for business magnitudes.\n\nI'm also trying to recall if the award was given to someone in the tech industry or in environmental science. I think it might have been someone in environmental science, given the current focus on climate change. So, maybe someone like Dr. James O'Keefe or someone else in that field.\n\nWait, I think I might be confusing it with another award. I'm not entirely sure. Maybe I should try to think about the years. If it's the most recent, perhaps 2022 or 2023. I think the award was given in 2022. So, if the recipient was born in 2000, they would be from the US,